Sixty percent of Cambodia's raw materials for garments, garments and footwear in Cambodia are imported from China. According to GMAC.
GMAC has confirmed that some garment and footwear factories in Cambodia will be shut down for one or two months from the end of February due to a shortage of raw materials from China due to the shutdown of Chinese raw materials. The lungs are caused by the coronavirus.
GMAC has confirmed that the coronavirus outbreak in China has temporarily shut down a number of raw materials factories and service providers, and may resume operations by the end of February. This will affect the supply chain to factories in Cambodia.
"For some factories, raw materials in stock for production may run out by next week or next week, and the temporary closure of factories in China may cause some factories to run out of raw materials by the end of this month," GMAC said. And in March. Faced with this problem, the factory has no choice but to temporarily suspend production operations for a full month or up to two months.
As for the procedure for temporary suspension, all factories will follow the legal procedures in force, with the negotiation, discussion and agreement between the workers and the factory management under the supervision and permission of the labor inspector.
