PRASAC Inaugurates a New Library Building in Chantrea District, Svay Rieng Province
(Svay Rieng): PRASAC, the largest financial institution in Cambodia, inaugurated a new library building at Samrong Primary School in Chek Village, Samrong Commune, Chantrea District, Svay Rieng Province this weekend to promote education and culture. Read in Cambodia, this library was built with PRASAC funds and CVC funds.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Sun Bonna, Director of Curriculum Development Department of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Thorn Thavuthea, Governor of Chantrea District, on behalf of the Governor of Svay Rieng Province, Mr. Pin Dara, Deputy Director of the Department of Education, Youth and Sports. Svay Rieng Province and Mr. Oum Sam Oeun, Executive Vice President of PRASAC MFI.
The event was also attended by monks, local authorities, teachers, students and hundreds of people in the community.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Thorn Tha Vuthea warmly welcomed the presence of the delegation and all distinguished guests who attended today's ceremony and thanked PRASAC MFI for funding the construction of the library building. To participate in the promotion of education and culture of reading in the territory of Chantrea district, Svay Rieng province.
This is PRASAC's admirable generosity in social work that has provided this invaluable achievement.
Mr. Oum Sam Oeun, Executive Vice President of PRASAC, stated that the construction of this library building is the work of PRASAC to benefit the society by participating in cultivating a culture of reading and enhancing the ability of students who are the children and grandchildren of the people. Citizens in the communities where PRASAC operates in return for supporting and using PRASAC products and services.
In Svay Rieng province, PRASAC has provided two library buildings, one of which is located in Meam Primary and Secondary School in Meam Khang Tbong Village, Meam Commune, Romeas Hek District, but has not yet been equipped. Another library is the library at Samrong Primary School, which is inaugurated on this occasion.
He said that in this Samrong school library project, PRASAC and CVC Foundation have provided funds to build a library building, equip books, equipment, training librarians and support the project for 3 years.
He requested that all stakeholders, including citizens, customers, local authorities and stakeholders continue to support PRASAC in the future so that PRASAC has more opportunities to help society.
He stated that reading books gives us the knowledge to build a prosperous life, know how to take care of health and think long-term. Therefore, parents of students must send their children to school for all and to study for a long time, do not give up studying and reading books, and all must help maintain this library to survive for many generations to come.
