(Phnom Penh): After waiting for a long time, National Road No. 2 and No. 22, with a total length of more than 72 km, have started to open the site for rehabilitation and reconstruction to facilitate people's travel more easily. .
Rehabilitation project of National Road No. 2 and National Road No. 22 with a total length of 72.17 km. The section of National Road No. 2 from Takhmao roundabout to O Chambok is 62.56 km long (passing through Phnom Penh, 5.4 km long, Kandal province, 14.21 km long and Takeo province, 52.56 km long) and National Road 22 from O Chambok to Ang Ta Som is 9.61 km long and is located in Takeo Province.
The two-lane rehabilitation project is divided into three sections, including:
* Part 1: From Takhmao roundabout to the intersection of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Blvd. To 2 lanes) Divided by road dividers, construction of sidewalks on both sides, sidewalks, drainage system, traffic signs, traffic signs, kilometer markers, safety poles and street lights in the town.
* Part 2: From the intersection of Samdech Techo Hun Sen Blvd. to the roundabout, more than 4 km long will be widened to 20.50 meters, divided into four lanes (2 lanes to 2 lanes) in These include lanes for cars and motorbikes, divided by split barriers, road signs, traffic signs, milestones, safety poles and street lights in the city.
* Section 3: From the roundabout to the junction of National Road No. 3 (Ang Ta Som), more than 63 km long, the width of the road will be widened to 13 meters, divided into two lanes (one lane to one lane). Includes traffic lanes for cars and motorbikes, divided by road dividers, construction of urban water supply system, installation of traffic signs, traffic signs, kilometer markers, safety poles and street lights in the city.
Both roads will be constructed as AC concrete roads with a total budget of 56.1 million US dollars, financed by the Government of the Republic of Korea, together with the Royal Government of Cambodia's contribution to deal with the impact of demining and munitions. Unexploded ordnance and taxes.
Residents living along National Roads 2 and 22 have been waiting for the construction for months. They also often ask when this road will start construction, because the current narrow road conditions make it more difficult to travel.
The launch of the new project requires the preparation of procedures and procedures to obtain additional funding from development partners, which delays the start of construction, he said.
