(Phnom Penh): Mr. Bun Hon, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, on February 10, 2020, rejected a statement issued by a number of civil society organizations alleging that the Royal Government of Cambodia lacked the will to amend the Law on Associations and Organizations. Not the government and requires the Royal Government to repeal the law that came into force.
The senior official of the Ministry of Interior considered that some of the statements of civil society were made for political reasons, to deviate from the rule of law and to be untrue in the discussions, and to intend to put pressure on the Royal Government for evil purposes. Any.
The statement from the Association of Civil Society Associations and Organizations was made after the Ministry of Interior and the Association of Civil Society Organizations met for the fourth consultation meeting on February 10, 2020 to discuss the proposed amendments to the law. On Associations and Non-Governmental Organizations.
According to Mr. Bun Hon, during the discussion, civil society organizations had disagreements within him, discussing only three more articles from the previous amendment because they still did not understand the content of Article that they want to amend or demand to be repealed.
According to Bun Hon, their accusation that the Royal Government "has no will to amend" is not correct, because if the government really does not have the will to amend the Association Law, the Royal Government will not come to the hearing. This is not the request of the society, and the government has explained the law to him.
(Svay Rieng): On the afternoon of February 10, 2020, at Romeas Hek District Hall, a ceremony was held to announce the new structure of Romeas Hek District Administration under the presidency of Mr. Hem Piseth, Deputy Governor of Svay Rieng Province, representing Mr. Men Vibol, Provincial Governor.
Mr. Hem Piseth stated that decentralization and deconcentration reforms were started at the commune level through the Commune / Sangkat Council elections in 2002, based on the experience and positive results achieved at the commune level, the Royal Government is committed. Expand the process of decentralization and deconcentration reforms at the capital, provincial, municipal, district and khan levels throughout the country.
He stated that through the amendment of the Constitution to prepare the legal framework for the administration of the Capital, Provinces, Municipalities, Districts, Khans and the Law on the Election of the Capital Council, Provincial Council, Municipal Council, District Council, Khan Council and held the election. Councils at the administrative level, mandated every five years from 2009 to the present.
According to the Deputy Governor, so far, the provincial administration has been cooperating in organizing and implementing the national program for nine years, which has achieved remarkable achievements, including:
* First: Sub-national administration * Second: Human resource management and development system for sub-national administration * Third: Establishment of commune, district and municipal funds, including financial decentralization * Fourth: Establish a development planning system at the sub-national level * Fifth: Restructuring of municipal, district and khan administrative systems, including the transfer of functions and resources to sub-national administrations
He stressed that in the future, the governors of the districts and districts must gather to summarize the process of integration and the beginning of the operation of the structure of the municipal, district and Khan management system to report and discuss in their council meetings to reach a consensus. To implement in accordance with the laws and regulations.
