Ministry of Tourism encourages more entertainment events in tourist destinations to promote domestic tourism movement
(Siem Reap): Mr. Tith Chantha, Acting Minister of the Ministry of Tourism, has strongly encouraged stakeholders in both the public and private sectors to jointly establish more entertainment events at various tourist destinations to promote the in-tourism tourism movement. National tourism during the outbreak of coronavirus.
Mr. Tith Chantha made this announcement during a meeting with the private sector in the tourism sector with Mr. Tea Seiha, Governor of Siem Reap Province, as well as private sector tourism operators, representatives of about 150 relevant departments, institutions and units at Siem Reap Provincial Hall on the 10th. February 2020.
He confirmed that Cambodia still has international tourists, but there is a decrease, especially Chinese tourists due to the outbreak of the coronavirus.
He said that so far there is no specific solution to the problem of declining tourists during the outbreak of coronavirus, he claimed that the Ministry of Tourism can not do this alone. Involvement of relevant ministries and institutions and the private sector in the tourism sector.
However, the relevant ministries and institutions, which are the staff of the Royal Government, will ask the Royal Government to get a specific solution in this difficult stage.
He said that there are a number of issues that require stakeholders to work together, such as taxes, electricity, interest on banks, etc. to facilitate access to companies, travel agencies, businesses, tourism services, tour operators, etc., which they are experiencing problems with high costs while revenue. Based on visits, accommodation or the use of tourist services has decreased, according to Mr. Tith Chantha.
The Acting Minister of Tourism called on stakeholders, both public and private, to jointly create more tourism events at tourist destinations, promote the internal tourism movement, both citizens and international visitors who are in Cambodia to visit. Lots.
At the same time, the private sector must also facilitate or reduce the sale of tour packages to guests, as well as discounts on hotel accommodation, food, transportation, services, etc. to encourage domestic tourism, because when there is a lot of tourism activities. It reduces the cost of tourism business and is a message to promote to foreign tourists, which attracts more foreign visitors to visit Cambodia.
The Acting Minister of Tourism stressed that Cambodia still welcomes all international tourists without any discrimination, but still maintains technical, medical and health inspections and calls for vigilance.
