Mr. Puy Kea: How to know if the information is true or false?
First, when reading the information, you should consider the source of the information, is it someone who is a writer, a Facebook activist or from a professional news organization?
Second: Do not just read the title, read the whole article to see if the title reflects the whole article? Sometimes the title is like a true story, but inside there is no argument at all.
Thirdly, you should check the writer, whether he is a professional writer or not?
Fourth: should check the source of the author's information, is there a clear source or he quotes from them?
Professional journalists always require at least two sources of information. Sometimes it is necessary to find up to 4 or 5 sources, if that is sensitive information, big information that can affect the reputation of others, high-ranking officials, can cause social unrest or national security. In the current context, coronavirus stories need multiple sources and the origins of the characters directly involved to ensure that the writing or information is accurate.
Sixth: Is it written just for fun, as a joke, for entertainment, to sell products, or just to attract more viewers?
8th: Does the article contain quotes from experts related to the story you wrote? For example, in the case of the coronavirus, which is absolutely required, ask the relevant ministry, the Ministry of Health. It is very important to confirm and confirm, because only the Ministry of Health can confirm that a person is really infected with the virus.
The Chinese man expressed his gratitude in front of the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bunheng, the leaders of the Ministry of Health, the leaders of Sihanoukville, representatives of the World Health Organization and the medical team when he He was released from the hospital on the morning of February 10, 2020, after a third test showed a negative coronavirus test.
Jachin Ho, 60, arrived in Sihanoukville, Cambodia on January 23, 2020, from Wuhan with three other family members.
Two days after his arrival, he developed an abnormal cough and fever and was examined by health officials for a throat swab, which diagnosed him with a new form of coronary heart disease on January 27, 2020. He was treated at Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital.
The Ministry of Health also confirmed that three other Chinese men were allowed to return to their families after being monitored and found to be free of coronavirus symptoms. Today.
The Chinese man was released from Sihanoukville Provincial Referral Hospital on the morning of February 10, 2020, after a third test, which showed he had no new coronary heart disease. No more in the body.
This is the first case of the new coronavirus in Cambodia as the virus has spread to many countries around the world. As of February 10, 2020, the death toll from the new coronary heart disease has risen to more than 900 and more than 39,800 cases.
