Announcing the appointment of Mr. Yin Yuth as Director of Kon Mom District Administration, Governor of Ratanakkiri Province, highly appreciated the efforts of the district administration on providing public services to the people
(Rattanakiri): Mr. Thong Savun, Governor of Rattanakiri Province, this morning, February 10, 2020, announced the launch of the new structure and the appointment of Mr. Yin Yuth as the Administrative Director of Kon Mom District.
On that occasion, the provincial governor praised and appreciated the Kon Mom district administration for its hard work in building and developing infrastructure that serves the needs of the people in accordance with the Rectangular Strategic Policy Phase. 4 of the Royal Government.
The Governor stated that in the context of Cambodia implementing the policy of decentralization and deconcentration, the Royal Government has three main objectives to make the sub-national administration run smoothly, including:
* First, to strengthen multi-party liberal democracy at the grassroots level through the election of provincial, municipal, district, khan, commune, sangkat councils, which represent the people and are key players in local administration. Through sub-national democratic governance within its jurisdiction.
* Second: Promote the effectiveness and efficiency of development through the introduction of decentralized and decentralized management policies and policies aimed at transferring functions and resources to sub-national levels that still have ownership and access. Responsible for providing services and local development to address the real challenges of local people for efficiency, transparency, accountability, environment and social equity.
* Third: Promote and own local people related to local leadership and development to contribute to poverty reduction and improve people's quality of life.
Please note that in this ceremony, there was also the announcement of the appointment of Mr. Yin Yuth as the Administrative Director of Kon Mom District, and there are 27 officials who have been announced to enter the new structure of Kon Mom District Hall now. After the implementation of the new structure of the district administration, some offices in the provincial departments will be under the control of the Kon Mom district administration, not under the same department as before.
