Many factories in China, from technology to auto parts to textiles and rubber and plastics, have been closed in China since before the Lunar New Year. Outbreaks of the new coronavirus have been advised not to resume operations, possibly next week or longer, as China continues to work to contain the spread of the virus. .
Apart from Adidas, Nike has also closed more than half of its stores in China, while South Korean carmaker Hyundai has decided to close its plant in South Korea due to a shortage of parts that need supplies from the country. China, while companies in Japan are worried about the same supply shortage if Chinese factories continue to close for longer.
In India, the pharmaceutical industry is also beginning to worry about the continued closure of Chinese pharmaceutical supplies. In Vietnam, after temporarily closing the northern border with China due to the outbreak of the virus, the Vietnamese Prime Minister ordered the reopening of the border in that area to allow goods to pass in and out again to prevent trade activities. Long crash.
In Cambodia, Heng Sour, a spokesman for the Ministry of Labor, told Fresh News on February 8, 2020 that if factories in China continue to close beyond the end of February, some factories in Cambodia may face temporary closure due to a shortage of raw materials imported from China.
