Understand the law: the definition of punishment
(Phnom Penh): We speak within the framework of the Criminal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, which was promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1109/022 dated November 30, 2009. Punishment is divided into criminal provisions in force only when the offense is committed.
To better understand what the definition of punishment means? Therefore, the legal awareness program of FRESH NEWS, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to raise the topic of "Definition of Punishment" to the following students:
According to Article 24 of the Penal Code, individuals are criminally liable only for their own actions. This suggests that criminal liability should generally be imposed only on those who have committed crimes.
Thus, the criminal convictions of juveniles are many types of sentences that the court applies, including:
* Additional punishment or parole is a punishment that is in addition to the punishment as determined by the law, which has 19 points according to Article 53 of the Penal Code. Additional sentences may be issued only if the sentence is specifically specified for a felony, misdemeanor or misdemeanor. Additional penalties may or may not be announced. Additional penalties shall be declared mandatory if the law explicitly refers to Article 54 of the Penal Code.
The court only blames the perpetrator for not committing a prison sentence or a fine if the perpetrator has already paid the damages (according to Article 76 of the Penal Code).
