National Road No. 58 with a length of nearly 200 km will be officially inaugurated on February 26 under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen
(Banteay Meanchey): National Road No. 58 connecting Poipet City, Banteay Meanchey Province to National Road No. 68 in Phong Commune, Oddar Meanchey Province, 174 kilometers long, will be officially inaugurated on February 26, 2020. Under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport.
The Senior Minister confirmed during the inspection of Stung Bot and National Road No. 58 this morning, February 9, 2020, that this road was built by Shanghai Construction Company under the credit framework from the People's Republic of China.
Senior Minister Sun Chanthol further stated that National Road No. 58 is a two-layer paved road (DBST) and in the coming days, how to improve the quality of National Road No. 58 to AC rubber road to strive. However, to make the roads in Cambodia more efficient in accordance with the principles of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, by making the roads more efficient.
"Even if the AC pavement is upgraded, if there are still trucks exceeding the limit, it will cause our roads to be damaged prematurely," he said. Trucks and those who have their own trucks must all respect the law in order to take care of the achievements of the nation, we must think of the common good, not just personal interests.
It should be noted that National Road No. 58 was built under a concessional loan from the Government of China with a total contribution of the Royal Government of Cambodia totaling more than 122 million US dollars. This road is a two-layer paved road (DBST) from National Road No. 5 at km 399 + 900, Poipet city, Banteay Meanchey province to National Road No. 68 at km 101 + 500, Oddar Meanchey province.
The road project started construction on June 10, 2015.
