The Forestry Administration confirms that Thina Development and Investment Company received the investment policy through letter No. 1650 SORN dated December 16, 2008 of the Office of the Council of Ministers on an area of 6,060 hectares located in Rei Roi commune, Rovieng district, Preah Vihear province. Signed an investment agreement with the Ministry of Agriculture on September 25, 2009.
The company has developed a master plan for investment in planting acacia, nutmeg and agro-industrial crops, divided into five sub-regions. The company has also made inventory, assessed and estimated forest resources in sub-region 4 and sub-region 5 and has already paid royalties and non-timber forest product premiums.
The company received the clearing permit through the letter No. 103 KSAK dated January 3, 2020 of the Ministry of Agriculture, in which the company has to cultivate the land that the Ministry has allowed the company to complete the clearing in 2020.
Transportation of non-timber forest products Previously, the company had a valid non-timber forest product (LP) and a non-timber forest product (PC) transportation permit.
In case the Forestry Administration finds that the company's performance is not in accordance with the principles and laws of the forestry, the Forestry Administration will take legal action.
