(Phnom Penh): In the 7th Kantha Bopha International Conference on the morning of February 08, 2020, a group of pediatricians, both domestic and foreign, shared and exchanged experiences as well as provided new knowledge related to pediatrics. To improve the effectiveness of treatment.
The conference was organized by the Kantha Bopha Foundation in collaboration with Kantha Bopha and Jayavarman VII Hospital at the Phnom Penh Hotel, chaired by Professor Thea Kruy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, and attended by Peter Studer, Executive Director of the Kantha Bopha Foundation, doctors from Switzerland and doctors. Of hospitals across Cambodia, a total of more than 200 people.
The Executive Director of Kantha Bopha Foundation stated that such conferences have already been held six times in order to provide a forum for pediatricians, both domestic and foreign, to share knowledge to discover new experiences. And good for treating more children.
The 7th Kantha Bopha International Conference also highlighted five key topics as follows:
* Demonstration of the advanced emergency development of newborns and children in general.
Demonstration of intestinal detoxification techniques for cases of acute renal failure due to drug poisoning or renal failure due to infection.
* Indicates the treatment of diseases caused by various infections, such as bacteria, viruses and so on.
At the same time, Professor Thea Kruy also instructed all members who are pediatricians from various hospitals to bring the latest knowledge to participate in the provision of effective, quality and safe pediatric treatment services. Always adhere to medical professional ethics.
