A truck hit a motorbike, causing it to overturn on National Road 4, injuring one person
(Preah Sihanouk): A traffic accident occurred when a truck collided with a motorbike, causing the car to overturn and injuring one person between km 130-131 in Veal village, Kampong Seila commune, Kampong Seila district, Preah Sihanouk province at around noon. 5 light enters on February 8, 2020.
According to local traffic officials, the accident occurred between a white Hyundai Hyundai with license plate Phnom Penh 3A-6677 and a motorcycle with the same direction (Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville) when the car overtook. There was an obstacle ahead, when the car came back, causing the motorcycle to collide, causing the car and the model to fall off the sidewalk. The driver of the car escaped, leaving only the car at the scene.
The victim was 21-year-old Ra Savun, a motorcyclist with minor injuries, residing in Thmey Village, Kampong Seila Commune, Kampong Seila District, Preah Sihanouk Province. Currently, the traffic police force of Kampong Seila district helps to avoid traffic congestion and take the car and motorbike to be stored at the police inspectorate of Kampong Seila district to deal with traffic law procedures.
