The 3,000 copies of the Law on Consumer Protection and the Law on "E-Commerce" in Khmer and English were of great interest to the legal leadership.
What is the purpose of consumer protection laws and e-commerce laws?
This Consumer Protection Law applies to all persons engaged in business, whether for-profit or non-profit, including the sale of goods or services or the right of real estate to consumers in the Kingdom of Cambodia, unless otherwise provided. Stated differently.
In the past, during the enforcement of the law by some Camcontrol officers, the abusers were only given a warning to stop. However, according to the Consumer Protection Law, Article 42 of the law stipulates imprisonment for between six months and two years and a fine of between 1 million and 4 million riels. According to Article 43, the punishment for dishonesty can be from 2 to 5 years and a fine from 4 million to 10 million riels.
The Law on E-Commerce, also known as the Law on E-Commerce, has 12 chapters and 67 articles for the purpose of governing e-commerce in the Kingdom of Cambodia and internationally. , Establish legal certainty in electronic business and civil transactions, Give the public confidence in the use of electronic communications.
According to the Law on Electronic Commerce, Article 59 of the law stipulates imprisonment between 6 months and 3 years and a fine of 1 million to 6 million riels for any person who violates the provisions of the article. 31. Pursuant to Article 64 of the law, the penalty is imprisonment between 1 and 5 years and a fine of 1 million to 10 million riels for any person who violates the provisions of the first paragraph of article 46.
