Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide 2 million Riels per month to all 23 students in Wuhan until the coronavirus situation subsides (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): 23 Cambodian students studying at the university In Wuhan, China, where a new type of respiratory infection caused by the coronavirus has spread, one person receives a monthly stipend of 2 million riel from the Royal Government of Cambodia until the virus situation subsides.
Mr. Ros Sovacha, Spokesman of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, told Fresh News this morning, February 7, 2020 that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has already agreed to the request of the Minister of Education, Youth and Sports, Mr. Hang Chuon Naron. 2 million Riels per month for all 23 Cambodian students who are staying in Wuhan until the coronary heart disease situation is relieved.
According to a letter from Minister Hang Chuon Naron, during the outbreak of a new type of pneumonia in Wuhan, Hubei Province, China, 23 Cambodian students were provided with food by the university. Students' dormitories and some students have to buy their own food from the grocery store.
As the new type of pneumonia continues to spread, which requires a high level of caution, it is affecting the daily lives of students who are stationed there. Therefore, the Ministry requested in principle from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia to provide a monthly stipend of 23,000 Riels to all 23 students to facilitate daily living expenses.
