This festival is held every year after Chinese New Year to mark the end of Chinese New Year. The duration of the procession is two days, starting from February 5-6, 2020. It is believed that this ceremony is designed to ward off bad luck and bad luck and bring good luck and good fortune in the New Year.
The Neak Ta Parade is held every year at Neak Ta Phnom Monument on Bokor Mountain in order to wish good luck to the staff working at Thansur Sokha Hotel as well as the tourists who come to visit. The event was attended by elders and many dignitaries from different parts of Cambodia.
In 2020, the He Neak Ta program will be held again on Bokor Mountain, including the relief ceremony and the ceremony to ask for good health. The liberation ceremony is held on the 5th of February with the organization of various offerings according to the year in order to ward off evil and pray for happiness, glory and good fortune in the new year.
