(Phnom Penh): Vital Drinking Water Company organized a trip abroad for more than 300 employees to celebrate the 10th anniversary of the growth in investment in the drinking water industry in Cambodia under the theme "10 steps higher "Bigger."
"10 steps higher, bigger" is a theme that the company wants to show the company's progress and commitment to greatness in a trip together as a family. This trip was organized on the occasion of the 10th anniversary of the company to thank and reward the Vital staff who have worked hard to expend both physical and mental strength to make this local company run well. In the production of drinking water.
Vital Drinking Water Company states that when it comes to travel abroad, it may be common for those who can afford it now. But for some workers or employees, we think this is one of their dreams, we as a local company that relies on his strength and ideas have a vision to join to make their dreams come true.
The tour lasts 4 nights and 5 days in Malaysia and Singapore, where Vital Drinking Water covers all the expenses of the workers and staff, including airfare, accommodation, local travel and meals. This tour will take place from 7 to 11 February 2020.
(Kampong Cham): In order to contribute to the revival of Buddhism, more than 1,000 monks, people, government officials and students participated in the celebration of "Understanding Meak Bochea" organized by Kampong Cham Provincial Administration in collaboration with the company. The shower took place on the afternoon of February 6, 2020 in the conference hall of Kampong Cham Provincial Hall.
Ieng Sotheara, Director of Phka Chhouk, stated that Meak Bochea is one of the most important festivals in Buddhism, celebrated on the 15th day of Meak every year, this year on February 8, 2020. At the same time, the Meak Bochea Awareness Program was held in order to raise awareness and encourage Buddhists to properly apply the teachings of Buddhism through Meak Bochea.
This Meak Bochea understanding program is held before Meak Bochea day in some provincial capitals, such as Svay Rieng, Battambang, Kampong Thom, Kampong Chhnang, Phnom Penh and Kampong Cham, so that Buddhists can understand before going to their favorite pagodas to celebrate. Meak Bochea ceremony according to the tradition.
The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Un Chanda, said that through the organization of the program to understand the Meak Bochea now will show two meanings for the minds of monks, people, government officials, grandchildren, students and relatives of Buddhists in Here are:
* First, emphasize the attention of the Royal Government in promoting the role of Buddhism, the state religion in society, which is the right policy of the Royal Government led by Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen * Second : Help Buddhists to understand more about Buddhism, especially to understand the meaningful ritual of Meak Bochea.
Mr. Un Chanda further stated that through this, the Buddhists will understand that Buddhism has great merits for the people, that is, the role of helping to teach to do good deeds, not persecute each other, understand the merits and demerits, understand what should be done and deeds. Which should be avoided. At the same time, this ceremony also confirms the gratitude of Buddhism for its merits.
