Cambodia, US hold forum to attract investment in agriculture in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Commerce of Cambodia and the US Embassy in Cambodia on February 6, 2020, organized a forum entitled "Business Opportunities in Agriculture in Cambodia 2020" in order to promote investment in Agriculture in Cambodia by US investors.
The forum was held at the Rosswood Hotel under the chairmanship of Commerce Minister Pan Sosak and US Ambassador to Cambodia W. Patrick Murphy, and was attended by senior officials from the Ministry of Commerce, relevant ministries and institutions. And national and international businesses. In particular, investors in the agricultural sector from many other large American companies.
In this forum, the Minister of Commerce emphasized that the agricultural sector is a priority sector defined in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government of Cambodia. The minister said that some agricultural products such as rice, corn, soybeans, cassava, mango, cashew, rubber, vegetables, fish, meat are all potential products for local and international businesses to consider doing business or investing in Cambodia.
The US Ambassador highlighted that the organization of the Business Forum on Agriculture in Cambodia is a good time to coincide with the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and the United States.
For this business forum, there are 15 large US companies, including companies that practice traditional agriculture and some companies that have modern technology that can help boost agriculture and increase yields. The ambassador hopes that these companies will cooperate with Cambodian companies to modernize the agricultural sector in Cambodia through the use of technology.
Emphasizing the use of technology, the Ambassador added that through the development of each country, the share of the agricultural sector will gradually decrease, and at that time, technology will help to increase productivity. Support food security and improve the agricultural value chain for exports.
Please be informed that as of November 2019, the bilateral trade volume between Cambodia and the United States is about 5.4 billion US dollars, an increase of 27.4% compared to 2018. The agricultural sector also plays an important role in trade relations between the two countries.
