According to Phay Siphan, the preferential treatment of everything except arms, or EBA, is just a political event, not a monster like the Corona virus, it is just a psychological subversion. He said the government had already prepared a budget package to respond to the EBA withdrawal or reduction.
He added that the reduction of the EBA would only allow Cambodia or its exporters to increase taxes, while Cambodia did not lose market share in the European Union. He said Cambodia had the right plan and that the EBA was not the foundation and key to Cambodia's economic growth.
It should be noted that the European Union sent its report to the Cambodian government on November 12, 2019 and left one month for the Cambodian side to respond. After Cambodia responds, the European Union will make a decision in February 2020 on whether to temporarily withdraw Cambodia's tariff preferences.
The decision was made by a majority vote of the 27 members of the European Commission. If the European Commission decides not to suspend the system, the procedure will be closed.
