Rice Federation of Cambodia: In the first month of this year, Cambodia exported more than 50,000 tons of rice, earning nearly $ 40 million
According to the Rice Federation of Cambodia, the revenue from rice exports in January was about $ 39 million.
The Rice Federation noted that in the overall situation, the EU continues to lead the Cambodian rice market with 37% market share, while China 30%, ASEAN 11% and other countries 22%.
Rice exports to China in January 2020 also decreased by about 20% or 3,664 tons. Overall, the reason for the decline is due to the Chinese New Year celebrations in China taking place in January 2020, which is faster than the Chinese New Year 2019 in early February. That is why the ordering and delivery process takes an average of two weeks off.
The ASEAN market, on the other hand, sees some variations depending on neighboring countries such as Thailand and Vietnam. Meanwhile, Cambodia's main markets are Malaysia and Brunei, which have not changed much, are still in good condition. Other markets grew by about 40%, with Cambodia still leading the way, while Australia has significantly increased its rice imports from Cambodia.
