(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Ieng Moly, President of the National AIDS Authority, announced that there are currently more than 10,000 people living with HIV in Cambodia who are hiding and refusing to come forward for treatment and social protection. From public health services and are not included in the AIDS care system, as they may be people with sufficient resources to find self-care services and well-known people in society.
This statement was made by Senior Minister Ieng Moly on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the Consultative Workshop on HIV Assessment and Social Protection on the morning of February 6, 2020 at the Phnom Penh Hotel.
On that occasion, all the ladies and gentlemen from the National Council for Social Protection, Ministry of Health, Ministry of Planning, Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, Health Service Expenses Agency, as well as representatives from key people and especially organizations UNAIDS and HP + provided both financial and technical support for the organization of this important workshop.
However, the main objectives of this workshop are:
* First, clarify the form of organization and implementation of social protection * Second, identify barriers to people living with HIV and the key people in accessing support services from the program * Third, find out Recommendations on how to respond to those barriers. The theme of this workshop covers two key areas: social protection and HIV / AIDS and HIV / AIDS.
