Minister of Agriculture: Natural rubber is a strategic crop to help boost the national economy, family economy, reduce poverty, in 2019, Cambodia exported nearly 300,000 tons of rubber, revenue nearly 400 million dollars
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, February 6, 2020, closed the meeting to review the work results of 2019 and the implementation direction of 2020 of the General Department of Rubber.
Minister Veng Sakhon praised and appreciated the valuable time that all private companies, development partners and operators in the rubber sector are invited to participate in this meeting, which is an opportunity to share lessons, ideas and good experiences to raise issues. Face the strengths, weaknesses and measures to address the development of the rubber sector.
At the same time, he praised the leaders and officials of the General Department of Rubber for their hard work in the past year with good results.
The Minister said that the natural rubber industry is an important sector in the agricultural sector, which in the past the rectangular strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia has also promoted the successful development of rubber in accordance with the development plan for the natural rubber industry in Cambodia 2011-2020. Also.
The Minister said that natural rubber is a strategic crop that has provided many benefits and has contributed to the national economy, family economy, poverty reduction, job creation, reduce migration, provide wood for use as fuel. Reduce deforestation, prevent soil erosion and forest cover.
In response to this huge multi-purpose, the Ministry, of which the General Department of Rubber is in charge, pays close attention to the development of a better and more competitive natural rubber industry by incorporating the natural rubber industry development plan into the plan. Agricultural Sector Development Strategy 2019-2023 National Development Strategy 2019-2023 and continue to promote the successful implementation of the Natural Rubber Development Strategy Plan to 2030 as planned.
* Update the strategic plan for the development of rubber plantations, continue to strengthen and expand cooperation with operators, development partners, banks and rubber associations and rubber plantation economic land concessions, especially with the Rubber Development Association of Cambodia (ARDC), strengthen research, training and dissemination. Apply the law.
Organize techniques in line with the trends of economic growth, climate change and the environment, strengthen the management and development of family rubber associations, continue to mobilize sources of funding or technology from development partners.
Regarding the administrative work, the Minister instructed the leaders and subordinates to pay attention to strengthen the work of leadership, management and high responsibility, respect the discipline, ethics, maintain unity, internal unity and respect for the professionalism of civil servants.
