Colonel Chim En, police inspector of Siem Pang district, told Fresh News this morning (February 6) that the Siem Pang district police and the administrative checkpoint of Sekong commune, Prek Meas commune and Sre Sambo commune have cracked down on drug trafficking cases. In Na Ong village, Ou Svay commune, Borey Ou Svay Sen Chey district, two Lao nationals were arrested and two packages of 382 tablets of methamphetamine WY were confiscated.
