Kao Kim Hourn, Minister accompanying the Prime Minister, confirmed the results of the meeting between Samdech Techo and Xi Jinping, saying that "China will provide assistance to Cambodia and provide assistance to Sihanoukville according to the needs of Cambodia."
Mr. Kao Kim Hourn also mentioned that during the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized to the Chinese President that in 2020, Cambodia's economic growth may slow down slightly due to changes in the world situation. Samdech Techo requested the Chinese government to continue to support investment in Cambodia, especially Chinese factories in Cambodia to continue to operate, Cambodia will improve the environment to ensure the operation of these factories.
Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia will strive to attract more investors to Cambodia and requested the Chinese President to expand the market for Cambodian products in China. To boost trade, Samdech Techo proposed to speed up negotiations on free trade between the two countries.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that China has always considered Cambodia as a "steel" friend, so should strengthen relations and cooperation between the two countries. Overall, the relationship between Cambodia and China, especially in terms of investment and trade, is going smoothly and at a good pace.
