Bramoy Village Chief Arrested in Pursat Province for Fraudulent Documents
(Pursat): Two suspects, including one chief of Bramoy village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province, were arrested by Veal Veng district police on February 3, 2020 in connection with a case of forgery of public documents. Encroach on 1,200 hectares of state forest land.
According to the report, the arrests were made on the orders of Pursat provincial governor Mao Thunin and chairman of the provincial state land management commission, which has ordered authorities to investigate cases of encroachment on state forest land. Illegal at the northern point of Phnom Phlit in Bramoy village, Bramoy commune, Veal Veng district, Pursat province.
The two suspects, 69-year-old Khan Khou, the chief of Pramoy village, and 33-year-old Thoeun Thi Hong, were in charge of measuring the land.
According to the report, only about 37 hectares of forest land was cleared for encroachment, according to the report. Where the suspects forged documents up to 1,200 hectares.
Currently, the suspect has been trained to build a case sent to the Pursat Provincial Court and will continue to proceed with the procedure.
