Amret: Consumer protection principles are the key to success towards loan goals
(Phnom Penh): Microfinance Institution Lending Amret emphasizes that lending is an important part of the global economy, as well as in some developing countries, including Cambodia. Small, medium and large enterprises play an important role in promoting the development of the national economy and the nation as a whole.
Borrowers who have a clear understanding of the terms of the loan and have a clear plan for the loan obtained with a responsible lender who carefully analyzes the business plan and the ability of the borrower to repay. It is a success that enables millions of people around the world to start a business and grow their business, create jobs to contribute to the development of their community and economy.
For Cambodia, as well as in some developing countries, credit services from microfinance institutions have played an important role in enabling people who do not have sufficient access to financial services to access financial services from banks. Or other financial institutions.
Mr. Rab said: “Before giving me a loan, Amret staff always explain the loan terms in detail and how to pay back the institution. I also get tips on how to prepare my business plan. Not only that, after receiving the first phase of the loan, I was also invited to participate in a financial education program organized by Amret.
Amret adhered to the key principles set out in the Consumer Protection Principles, including "Transparency" when Amret's loan officer explained in detail the terms of the loan and the repayment methods. The workshop on knowledge of finance and agricultural techniques also clearly demonstrates the practice of respecting customers and fair protection.
