Full text of meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese President in Beijing
BEIJING, Feb. 5 (Xinhua) - Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays a state visit to Beijing on February 5, 2020. This was warmly welcomed by Chinese President Xi Jinping.
The following are the results of the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the President of China, provided by Mr. Kao Kim Hourn, Minister of Foreign Affairs, accompanied by the Prime Minister:
The president said he was glad to see him again in Beijing. He added that the Chinese people, as well as the Chinese government, are facing an outbreak of coronary heart disease, and that the Cambodian people, especially students living in China, are paying close attention.
He also pointed out that from last year, the relationship between Cambodia and China began in the new era by pursuing a policy of common destiny and being able to take the relationship between the two countries to a new level from now on.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen replied that he really thanked the President for receiving him in such a short time, and he emphasized that the purpose of his visit to China was threefold:
First, show solidarity with the Chinese government as well as the Chinese people in this difficult time,
Second, to strengthen the spirit and trust for the people and students of Cambodia living and studying in China to continue to stay in China, struggle with the Chinese people
Third, send a message to the Cambodian people The disease of the Cambodian people is not a disease caused by the "corona" virus, it is a disease of fear, and so far no Cambodian has been infected with this disease. Samdech Techo also pointed out that some countries seem to be waging a psychological war to frighten the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also said that he had earlier shook Li Keqiang's hand, even though he had just returned from Wuhan. Samdech Techo emphasizes that Samdech does not wear a mask, if you wear a mask, you do not need to visit China. Samdech Techo emphasized that even though the Chinese friend had prepared a mask for Samdech, Samdech did not wear it.
The Prime Minister said that last year the two countries signed a political agreement on a common destiny. Samdech Techo added that no one can break the friendship between China and Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized to the Chinese President that in 2020, Cambodia's economic growth may slow down slightly due to changes in the world situation. Samdech Techo requested the Chinese government to continue to support investment in Cambodia, especially Chinese factories in Cambodia to continue to operate, Cambodia will improve the environment to ensure the operation of these factories.
Samdech Techo stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia will strive to attract more investors to Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the Chinese President to expand the market for Cambodian products in China. To boost trade, Samdech Techo proposed to speed up negotiations on free trade between the two countries.
Samdech Techo also pointed out that in March, Samdech will inaugurate a road with a length of more than 300 kilometers, a road built under a Chinese loan. Regarding legal cooperation, Samdech emphasized that in the past, Cambodia has completely shut down online gambling in order to strengthen security, eliminate some crimes in Cambodia and can also help China.
Once again, the Prime Minister thanked the Chinese President and the Chinese people for their continued support of Cambodia. Samdech Techo emphasized that Cambodia is a loyal friend of the Chinese people and will continue to share the same fate.
The President replied that he thanked the Prime Minister for his loyalty to the Chinese people and the Chinese government. Cambodia and Samdech Techo Prime Minister are China's "steel" friends. The president said that in the history of more than 1,000 years, the Chinese people have always faced many obstacles, and recently, the Chinese people have the courage to face the inevitable danger, but also to solve the problem.
He said that after the outbreak of the virus, the Chinese Communist Party held a meeting and set the highest and most serious ratings on the issue and agreed to put the interests of the Chinese people as a high priority.
The president stressed that if the Chinese government does not take immediate and clear action, the disease could be even more dangerous and serious.
The president assessed the disease as just a transitional one. The president also pointed out that in recent years, China has also suffered from "Sa" disease. The president also stressed that the Chinese government believes in its ability to tackle and eradicate the disease.
The President stressed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen can visit China at any time and the President can meet with Samdech Techo many times and often to strengthen cooperation between the two countries.
The President affirmed that China will provide assistance to Cambodia and Sihanoukville according to the needs of Cambodia.
The president said the Chinese government would encourage Chinese investors to invest in Cambodia and import Cambodian products into China. He called on Cambodia to improve the investment climate in Cambodia, which supports investment and business. The President asked to look at what Chinese investors face when investing in Cambodia to find measures to help those investors.
Finally, the Chinese President invited Samdech Techo to visit China at an appropriate time later. Samdech Techo Hun Sen Leaves Beijing and Returns Home
(Beijing): At 10:00 pm Beijing time (9:00 pm Cambodian time) On February 5, 2020, the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to leave Beijing to return to the country. Cambodia after a special meeting with China's top leaders.
According to the time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen may arrive in Cambodia at around 1:30 on February 6, 2020.
Before leaving Beijing, Samdech posted a message expressing joy and warmth in his heart, which China's top leaders have vowed to do their best to protect Cambodian citizens and students in Wuhan from infection. Pneumonia is not caused by the coronavirus.
Samdech Techo also instructed students living in China to take good care of their health, follow the instructions of the Chinese school and health authorities to avoid new infections, coronavirus and other diseases. . Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells Chinese PM that Cambodia still supports China in fighting Corona virus
(Beijing-China): In a meeting with Chinese Premier Li Keqiang on the evening of February 5, 2020 in Beijing, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, confirmed that his visit is to show From supporting China while China is fighting the coronavirus.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, on behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech will extend his condolences to the families of the victims of this virus. Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the Chinese government for helping Cambodians living in China while the Chinese government took some steps to help Cambodian students.
At the same time, Li Keqiang confirmed that the Chinese government and people are fighting coronavirus. Through Samdech Techo PM's visit to China now shows strong support for China in difficult times.
Li Keqiang affirmed that the Chinese government and people have a strong belief in the fight against coronary heart disease and that China will continue to support the interests of the Chinese people and the people of Cambodia.
In response, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the current visit shows solidarity with the Chinese government and people in this difficult time. In particular, it shows the faith of the Cambodian people and Cambodian students who are studying and living in China. This visit is also to eliminate fear among the people of Cambodia, especially against the fear of the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that what is important is not the coronavirus, but the fear of the people, and Samdech considers this coronary disease as a psychological war that is frightening the people and some opinions accuse That the Royal Government has traded the lives of the Cambodian people with Cambodia-China relations.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia claimed that the allegations were completely untrue because he continued to pay attention to students studying in China and could not run away from what was happening. This is possible, but the prince still shows his condolences to the people of Cambodia and the people of China. (Photo inside)
