During the suspension, the owner of the building did not show the legal letter related to the request to block the road for construction, so the authorities decided to temporarily suspend the construction process. In that, Mr. Aing Serey Piseth advised the building owner not to pour concrete to block the road during the day and forbid the workers to stay in the condominium building.
Authorities advised that at the end of the construction site, the sewer system should be restored and no construction waste materials should be left on the sidewalk to harm passengers.
The suspension took place at 9:30 am on February 5, 2020 on Street 103, Village 8, Sangkat Boeung Trabek, Khan Chamkar Morn, after receiving instructions from Mr. Theng Sothol, Governor of Chamkar Mon District at the condo construction site. Road 103 was completely closed, making it difficult for people to travel.
