(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works has set a target to continue the growth rate of civil servants from 2019-2023 in the range of 6.5%, along with the increase in the basic salary in early January by 7% of the basic salary index unit and increase the salary. Termination of duties in April in the range from 2-3 thousand Riels to all types of civil servants and forces.
These directions were presented at the closing ceremony of the Ministry of Public Function meeting held on the morning of February 5, 2020 at the Phnom Penh Hotel under the chairmanship of Mr. Prum Sokha, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Public Works.
In addition to these directions, the Ministry has also identified a number of work directions to be implemented in 2020 and beyond, including:
* Submit the draft National Program for Public Administration Reform for 2020-2030 to the Head of the Royal Government for approval in the first quarter of 2020.
* Promote the implementation of the management system based on performance, especially the development of legal documents to make it easier for ministries and institutions to implement.
* Promote the implementation of the evaluation of model public service units in the field of education, evaluation of secondary schools - primary schools and health - health centers, as well as the implementation of model leadership evaluation at the General Department level.
* Continue to increase the basic salary at the beginning of January by 7% of the unit price of the basic salary index and increase the salary in April in the range from 2-3 thousand Riels to all civil servants and the armed forces.
* Expand cooperation with relevant ministries and institutions to develop the capacity of civil servants to develop human resources in the municipal-district-Khan unity administration, especially the training of new officials and officials who are ready to become leaders in the future. In particular, strengthening and expanding the scope of training at the Royal School of Administration of 6,000 people.
* Continue good cooperation with ASEAN and international countries and participate in the implementation of the ASEAN and ASEAN Plus 3 active plans to achieve the building of the ASEAN Public Community as well as the building of the ASEAN Community 2025.
* Strengthen the efficiency and effectiveness of managing and improving the management and administration of work in an innovative way and in line with the current state of digital technology.
* Find ways and mechanisms to collaborate on the development of an automation system between information technology for public financial management and information system for civil service payroll.
* Increase the efficiency of the administration of the salary administration and the management of the civil service, especially at the sub-national level, with the Capital-Provincial Department of Civil Service as the staff.
* Promote the organization of reform work within the Ministry of Public Function, including the implementation of training mechanisms for civil servants at the local level through the establishment of regional schools, financial management, document management and human resource management, and internal audit work. Korean PM Holds Luncheon for Samdech Techo PM
