(Kampong Chhnang): Garlic cultivation is a crop that 90% of farmers live in Trapeang Krapeu village, Teuk Hot commune, Rolea Bier district, now they like to grow and sell after the core business in the rainy season.
Because the garlic plant is grown on only 40 acres of land for a period of one and a half to two months, can be sold with a decent income to support the family in addition to farming.
Garlic farmers in Trapeang Krapeu village, Teuk Hot commune, Rolea Bier district, this morning, February 5, 2020, said that today, about 90% of the farmers in the village, which has more than 300 families. Growing garlic for sale for more than 3 years to improve family life after the core business of rice cultivation.
During the harvest season, there are trucks that buy cars directly to the plantation and transport them to markets in Phnom Penh, Pursat, Battambang and Kampong Chhnang.
Apart from growing garlic, the people in Trapeang Krapeu village also grow other vegetables according to market demand, such as all kinds of cabbage, frogs and ferns. But the most favorite plant is this onion because it is easy to grow, easy to maintain and quick to harvest.
On the morning of February 5, 2020, Mr. Ngin Hun, Director of the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Kampong Chhnang Province, confirmed that in Trapeang Krapeu village, Teuk Hot commune, Rolea Bier district, it is the largest market for growing garlic to supply the market in the province because Trapeang Krapeu villagers have about 95 people. % Of farmers are engaged in growing garlic leaves, turning some of their farmland into farmland for this business.
He said that currently the market for garlic is in high demand in the country, especially in Battambang and Phnom Penh, so hundreds of families in Trapeang Krapeu have been growing garlic for sale to support the economy of any family, this business is close to home. And near the family.
Some farmers' rice paddies have been converted from rice fields to plantations for growing garlic, leafy vegetables and other mixed crops, and farmers can grow garlic four to five times a year, in no month. They did not leave the land vacant. Chamkarmon District Governor Accelerates Boeung Trabek Canal
