"Anti-personnel mines" were banned by the Ottawa Treaty and entered into force in 1999. There were 164 signatories, while the United States only stopped buying mines and banned use outside the Korean Peninsula in 2014. At the same time, the US military has not used anti-personnel mines since 1991, and has stopped producing and importing such mines for more than two decades.
(Phnom Penh): On Tuesday afternoon, February 4, 2020, Lt. Gen. Rath Sreang, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie and Commander of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie, accompanied by a working group and local authorities Mrs. Puth Vannak, Chief of Sangkat 1, Sangkat Prek Kampus, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh, who has stage 3 breast cancer, is being treated at home waiting for surgery.
At this critical stage, Ms. Puth Vannak had to undergo six chemotherapy injections every 21 days, once every 10 days before undergoing surgery.
