(Paris): Cambodia considers the social dialogue mechanism of the Global Agreement very important to jointly address challenges in the labor market and promote universal access to globalization. Let its partners achieve the Sustainable Development Goals of the 2030 Agenda of the United Nations.
This was stated by Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, in a high-level meeting on social dialogue for a better future, organized by the Global Agreement Partnership on February 4, 2020. At the OECD headquarters in Paris, France.
The Ministry of Labor organizes regular bilateral and tripartite consultative and tripartite meetings twice a year to monitor, evaluate and resolve any requests from stakeholders in the implementation of legal provisions in order to promote freedom of association, rights and working conditions; Harmony in professional relations.
It should be noted that today's conference is a forum for partners of the Global Agreement to share ideas, challenges, solutions, best practices and experiences, as well as policies related to the implementation of social dialogue to promote decent work and environmental growth. To participate in solving new challenges in the job market in the future.
On this historic occasion, the Royal Government of Cambodia would like to express its appreciation for the achievements made under the Global Agreement Initiative and its commitment to continue to work closely with stakeholders to promote social dialogue for decent work and inclusive growth. Which is the vision of the Global Agreement towards achieving the Sustainable Development Goals of the 2030 Agenda of the United Nations.
