(Phnom Penh): Lawyers representing Thi Nga Development and Investment Co., Ltd. have come forward to refute a number of online media outlets that have published untruths, accusing the company of illegally clearing and transporting timber for sale in the province. Church.
The company's lawyer claimed that the company was clearing and harvesting non-timber forest products only within the economic concession area approved by the Ministry of Agriculture. From the site where the land was cleared, the company did not transport the timber for sale, but transported it to the factory of the furniture manufacturer and board to sell it for the salary of the workers only.
