Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment, emphasized that due to the efforts to better manage and conserve protected areas, Cambodia has sold carbon credits in the Southern Cardamom Mountain National Park, Tatai Wildlife Sanctuary in Koh Kong Province and Keo Seima Wildlife Sanctuary in Mondulkiri Province within the framework of the volunteer market with a total budget of approximately 11.6 million US dollars.
