Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as other world-class dignitaries, emphasized the importance and values of peace, security and human resource development. But it also highlighted some of the challenges of peace, security and human resource development.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that peace is the foundation of development. But global peace today is still fragile due to the evolution of a polarized framework, competing interests and rebalancing of global power.
Samdech Techo said that the world is currently facing a severe and protracted trade war that creates economic risks, adversely affecting global economic growth in the medium term and the development of the socio-economy as a whole.
As Cambodia's leader who went through the war directly and worked hard to find peace for Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen offered the idea that building and maintaining peace is priceless and that peace is fundamental in Socio-economic development, strengthening security and human development.
The Prime Minister shared four views at the World Forum held in Seoul, Korea to contribute to strengthening peace, security and human development. The four concepts include:
