Cambodia Hosts Regional Coordinating Workshop on Safe Migration
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia is honored to host the two-day CLMV Regional Coordinating Workshop on Safe Migration of Transmission Countries (Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam) from 04 to 3 February 05, 2020.
The opening ceremony of the workshop on the morning of February 4, 2020 was chaired by Ms. Chou Bun Eng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Permanent Vice President of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking (NCDD), a representative of the migration organization. International (regional) IOM and US Embassy representatives.
Ms. Chou Bun Eng said that the workshop was held to share experiences on migration issues that lead to trafficking or exploitation of workers. During these two days, stakeholders will be informed of new initiatives where the four countries can share experiences and best practices in each country in response to migration.
She added that both Cambodia and the other three countries sincerely hope that the four countries will continue to have good cooperation with each other, ready to enter into talks with target countries that could start from Thailand.
According to Chou Bun Eng, the challenge that Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam have faced in the past is to resolve legal issues because some workers do not have proper legal documents and the sending countries and target countries have agreed to provide them with legal documents. He who migrates all those.
The Permanent Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking also claimed that so far, Cambodia has about 1.2 million overseas workers, most of them illegal workers going to Thailand, where the relevant ministries and institutions Trying to find all the ways to solve for them to become legal workers.
The representative of the International Organization for Migration (Regional) IOM in Cambodia claimed that both the policy of the Royal Government and other laws and regulations, the Royal Government of Cambodia has submitted to discuss the problem of irregular migration.
