(Phnom Penh): The crane of a high-rise condominium building collapsed, hitting an excavator and another vehicle of the US Embassy, as well as injuring an embassy official.
This case happened at 9 am on February 4, 2020 at the construction site of a new condominium building, Sangkat Tonle Bassac, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
Local authorities and residents near the scene told Fresh News that before the incident, they saw a group of technical experts dismantled the crane to complete its construction, but did not know that the dismantling was not technically correct. A crane fell to the ground, injuring an excavator and another vehicle, and injuring one person.
Immediately after this information, Mr. Aing Serey Piseth, Deputy Governor of Chamkar Mon District, arrived at the scene and inspected the site until the construction site was temporarily suspended.
