The announcement comes as more than 1.4 billion Chinese people are suffering from pneumonia caused by the coronavirus, and more than 70 countries have said they do not welcome Chinese people into their country. On the other hand, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, not only did not suspend flights from China to Cambodia, he also announced that he would visit more Cambodian students in Wuhan, which moved hundreds of thousands of Chinese people.
A Chinese man expressed his opinion, "Please give advice to Samdech, understand well, do not go, think about safety first, the spirit of Samdech Prime Minister Hun Sen, I think the Cambodian people must understand clearly. "As a Chinese person, I really thank Prime Minister Hun Sen for his solidarity with China."
