(Banteay Meanchey): While the technical team of the Department of Protection and Preservation of Ancient Buildings of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts was excavating at the port of Baray Mebon in the area of Banteay Chhmar temple, the team also found the statue of "Lion or Reachsey" buried In the mud of that port for hundreds of years.
Mr. Kuwit said that the lion or lion statues were built in the Bayon style from the late 12th to early 13th centuries during the reign of Jayavarman VII during the construction of Banteay Chhmar. But over the course of hundreds of years, it collapsed into the bottom of a water bar and was buried under mud until it was discovered.
The reason for this finding was stated by the director of the above department, "While the team of the Department of Protection and Preservation of Ancient Buildings is carrying out the repair of the port of Baray Mebon, but usually before the repair is to dig first. If you want to know the structure of any building, such as the repair of the Baray Mebon port of Banteay Chhmar, you also need to dig in advance.
He said that during the excavation, the team found many pieces of rock that are the structure of the Baray Mebon port, especially the lion statue, which may be placed for decoration or receipt of the port.
However, Mr. Kovit noted that at the Baray Mebon port, there are still rocks and fragments of other structures, which may also have more heritage.
He added that in order to protect the safety of the newly discovered lion statue, the department has been working closely with the heritage police stationed at the Banteay Chhmar temple to deploy regular guards. When the upper baray is repaired, the lion statue will be returned to the port to improve the beauty of the Baray Mebon, Banteay Chhmar.
Cambodia is known as one of the countries most devastated and devastated by the three decades of war crisis. Cambodia was given the opportunity to re-develop the country after the flames of war were completely extinguished in late 1998.
In the presence of well-known dignitaries attending the Global Peace Forum of the Global Peace Federation, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that as a country that has experienced war and destruction, peace is invaluable to Cambodia. Samdech Techo added that everything that Cambodia has achieved so far, both development and prosperity, is the fruit of peace.
In order to maintain peace and social security, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that since 1998, after achieving complete peace, the Royal Government of Cambodia has always focused on human resource development, considering the development of resources. People are one of the top four priorities.
The Prime Minister emphasized that the Royal Government of Cambodia has carried out in-depth reforms in the field of education to strengthen both the quality and expansion of education services to obtain quality human resources to support the achievement of Cambodia's long-term vision. With this goal in mind, the Royal Government has also significantly increased the budget for the sector.
Samdech Techo emphasized that this budget focuses on the construction of schools, school processes, strengthening the quality of exams at all levels, strengthening the quality of the new generation of schools, strengthening the technical skills in general education and Technology, research on real science, technology, engineering and mathematics (STEM) and scholarships for poor students, etc.
