Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that the past story between Cambodia and Korea went through a flood situation, which was caused by the problems on the Korean Peninsula and the Cold War. He claimed that the conflict between North and South Korea had changed Cambodia's diplomatic policy, but that he had tried to strike a balance between South and North Korea.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo, recalled the development of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and South Korea until South Korea agreed to establish an embassy in Cambodia. After the explanation, the South Korean prince agreed to upgrade from a mission to an embassy, from a mission representative to an ambassador.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the relationship between Cambodia and South Korea has been very successful so far, and that if Samdech had not signed a diplomatic agreement with South Korea in 1996, he would not have been present. Cambodians in South Korea now as well.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "So far, I can say that as the founder of relations with the Republic of Korea, with the support of the King, we have achieved great success in establishing Diplomatic relations with this country Now that we and Korea have gone through good and bad things, over the past 20 years of diplomatic relations, there has been no crack for We.
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia reminded that when Cambodia decided to establish diplomatic ties with South Korea, there were concerns affecting the relationship between Cambodia and North Korea, but the establishment of relations between Cambodia and South Korea is a historical fact that can not be taken. Can not hide that.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia is very proud of its efforts to facilitate the 2019 Anniversary Summit between Cambodia and South Korea in Busan. Samdech also expressed pride that Cambodia has facilitated the upgrading of Mekong-South Korea relations.
Among them, the prince noted that about 7,000 Cambodian workers living illegally in South Korea, some of which are living illegally in South Korea, are trying to insult the government.
Due to good relations between Cambodia and the Republic of Korea, the Prime Minister of Cambodia said that from 1996 to 2018, South Korea provided more than 300 million US dollars in grants. In 2019, the grant was $ 17 million and in 2020 it is planned to provide $ 24 million.
