(Kandal): After holding a meeting with relevant institutions on February 3, 2020, the Kandal Provincial Administration has decided to hold a public parade on February 6 to celebrate the ASEAN Clean Tourism City Award. Second, 2020 in Takhmao city.
The march was determined by the committee to locate the pig's nose at the Bassac River Park as a venue for the event, with nearly 3,000 participants in attendance, including: provincial councils, provincial governors, leaders of all government institutions around the province, forces Armed with monks, people, teachers, students and prepared 83 trucks, 53 cars and 50 motorcycles for use in this event.
As planned, they will gather at the Pig Nose Park on the banks of the Bassac River in Takhmao City and start marching on Street 21A towards Street 206, around Kandal Provincial Hall, on National Road 2 to the traffic light at Prek Ho Bridge and turn left. On Street 21B to the Red Cross traffic light, turn left at the Takhmao roundabout and turn right onto Street 107 toward the venue.
Takhmao won the ASEAN Clean Cities Award in Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam on January 16, 2020, while the Daun Penh districts of Phnom Penh and Kampot also won like Takhmao in Kandal province. Also.
It should be noted that the selection of clean cities in ASEAN is based on seven major indicators, focusing on good cooperation between the people and local authorities, maintaining cleanliness, clean environment, no air pollution. Manage garbage and waste properly, people cooperate to protect security, safety, maintain good order and have a beautiful park.
