On January 30, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen presented a clear position of the Royal Government of Cambodia in response to the "Corona" respiratory disease, which has been attacking China and spreading around the world. Mr. To help solve the difficulties of China, Cambodia's steel friend, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced to maintain flights between China and Cambodia and not to evacuate Cambodian diplomats and students from China.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also announced his efforts to help treat a Chinese citizen who had a respiratory illness in Cambodia. In particular, help prevent the spread of this respiratory disease to the Chinese people as well as Cambodians in Cambodia. Samdech Techo Hun Sen stressed that non-discrimination against the Chinese people is an important contribution to the fight against the new respiratory virus.
In response to Samdech Techo Hun Sen's strong stance, Mr. Wang Vinthean said that the Chinese side highly appreciated and thanked Samdech Techo for his kindness to the Chinese government and people.
The Chinese ambassador stated, "Only by strong winds can we know the endurance of weeds, and only in difficult circumstances can true friends be known." "Samdech Techo and the Royal Government of Cambodia have stood with the Chinese people hand in hand against this virus while China is facing the coronavirus, we are very excited to always remember in the heart."
Mr. Wang Winthean also stated that so far, the Chinese government continues to ensure the safety and health of all Cambodians living in China and provide assistance to all Cambodians in need.
Respiratory diseases caused by the coronavirus, which originated in Wuhan, Hubei Province, China, affected 17,388 people and killed 362 patients. However, 480 patients were rehabilitated.
The victims were all Chinese living in China. One of the dead was a Chinese man traveling to the Philippines.
Apart from China, respiratory diseases caused by the "coronavirus" have also occurred in 23 other countries. Ministry of Tourism continues to promote tourism potential in Cambodia at International Tourism Fair in India
