(Kampong Cham): Police in Kampong Cham province arrested a total of 15 men and women in connection with drug use and distribution cases in Chamkar Leu, Prey Chhor and Kang Meas districts on February 2, 2020.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal said that after receiving information from the people, he immediately ordered the Provincial Anti-Drug Bureau with Chamkar Leu District, Prey Chhor District, Kang Meas District, led by Lieutenant Colonel Chiv Seng Ros. The director of the Anti-Drug Bureau launched three operations to crack down on drug trafficking.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture said at a conference on "Updates and Progress of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries" organized by the Royal Government Spokesperson's Office at the Council of Ministers this morning, February 3, 2020. In 2019, the number of livestock in Cambodia increased by almost 3.47 percent compared to 2018, when there were a total of nearly 45.8 million animals.
Ms. Vuthy said that raising cattle decreased because raising in Cambodia has just become a family and the problem of raising a family has also decreased. He said pig farming was declining because people feared African swine fever would make them reluctant to raise pigs.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Agriculture said that raising chickens and ducks increased by 6% as people changed their habits from family farming to modern industrial farming.
Regarding the decrease in cattle raising, Mr. Phay Siphan, Head of the Spokesperson Unit of the Royal Government of Cambodia, explained the social aspects. He said people stopped raising cows because they had migrated to work in the city, especially in factories. Another point that Mr. Phay Siphan sees is that due to the rapid development of technology, people have stopped raising cows for agriculture.
"The Industrial Revolution 4.0 has begun and the power of the tractor has been completely replaced," said Phay Siphan. "Farmers' brides go to the factories, so cows are no longer needed, but raised for meat."
In addition, the scientists made the remarks after finding that the first symptoms of some coronavirus-infected patients were diarrhea rather than fever.
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, officially inaugurated the resort of "Phka Trakoun Village", a modern and natural Borey in Saang District, Kandal Province.
"Phka Trakoun Village" is a creative place of Khmer founder and entrepreneur Din Somethearith, the owner of Phka Trakoun Village Resort, created with the idea of preserving the Khmer house style with a modern era for people to feel naturally fresh.
Speaking at the inauguration ceremony on the night of February 2, 2020, the Minister of Information praised the idea of creating a modern, natural Borey of Phka Trakoun village, which is part of serving the needs of some people. Who wants to live naturally, in line with the natural air.
Mr. Din Somethearith, owner of Phka Trakoun Village Resort, said that Phka Trakoun Village is not just a place to visit from time to time, you can stay there with Khmer style house with modern and eye-catching beauty of Phka Trakoun. Prosperous in the fields, on the other hand, this location is not far from Phnom Penh, Takhmao and other towns, which allows tourists to travel faster than other places.
He stated that his vision is to plant all kinds of trees and flowers in his resort of Phka Trakoun village to contribute to the protection of the environment, educate the next generation to know about those species, especially to inspire the spirit of nature protection. Forests will also be replanted.
Phka Trakoun village has a total area of about 100 hectares, of which 40 hectares have been sold and another 60 hectares are underway to implement projects to meet the needs of people who dream of living in a natural way with a large yard. Grow various crops as needed.
