A number of senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia accompanied Samdech Techo to South Korea today. Officials accompanying Samdech Techo include Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as well as a number of senior government officials and business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
As an NGO with a special role in consulting with the UN Economic and Social Council, the UPF supports the work of the United Nations, especially in the areas of interfaith peacebuilding, peace education, and peace. Both strengthening marriage and family.
During his visit to South Korea, the Prime Minister will also meet with the Cambodian community, students and Cambodian workers living and working in South Korea.
Through Samdech Techo Hun Sen's recent visit to South Korea is seen as a new contribution to the promotion of relations and cooperation between Cambodia and South Korea.
Cambodia and South Korea established ties on October 30, 1997, under the direct initiative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Kim Jong-un, then President of South Korea. Relations between the two countries have steadily improved in all areas, including politics, economy, culture and society.
Trade volume between Cambodia and South Korea is seen to be growing steadily. The trade volume in 2019 was nearly 1 billion US dollars. Of that, Cambodia's exports to South Korea account for about 30 percent and South Korea imports about 70 percent.
Cambodian goods exported to South Korea are mostly garments, electronics, footwear, beverages, rubber bags, medicines, cardboard and some agricultural products. Cambodian goods imported from South Korea include textiles, cars, beverages, electronics, machinery, home decor, medicines, soaps and plastic products.
In terms of investment, Cambodia received more than $ 4 billion from South Korea in the textile, agriculture, real estate and construction sectors. Of the 214 investment projects, 123 invested in factories with a capital of $ 486 million, creating about 80,000 jobs.
Currently, there are about 10,000 Cambodian women who have obtained Korean citizenship through marriage, and there are about 300 students studying in Korea.
Another 57 people have died, bringing the total to 360 and 2,829 to be infected, bringing the total number of cases worldwide to 172,000, according to health authorities.
This morning, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit held a press conference to present the update and progress of the Ministry of Agriculture.
(Phnom Penh): On February 3, 2020, the Royal Government Spokesperson Unit organized a press conference on "Update and Progress of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries."
The purpose of this conference is to show the public a clear understanding of the activities and achievements of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries in response to the Royal Government's Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 in the core direction of promoting better governance policies.
The Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries is an important agency of the Royal Government of Cambodia working on agriculture, including agriculture, animal husbandry, promoting and promoting investment, export of agricultural products and food. The Ministry also plays an important role in inspecting the food safety of all agricultural products from the beginning of production to the final stage of primary processing.
Agriculture has contributed significantly to the livelihood of the people and the national economy. According to the report, agriculture currently contributes about 25 percent to the national economy.
A report by the Ministry of Agriculture shows that in 2019, the rice harvest reached more than 2.5 million hectares, with a total yield of nearly 8 million tons, up from nearly 500,000 tons last year. Combined crops cover more than 25,000 hectares, up from nearly 5,000 hectares last year. Implemented nearly 50,000 hectares of industrial crops, less than 9,000 hectares last year.
