Phillip Bank and KREDIT Microfinance Institution Merge to Become the Third Largest Commercial Bank in the Country
The new entity will operate under the name of Phillip Bank Plc. And will have more than 2,000 employees, and the management of Phillip Bank is committed to keeping both Phillip Bank and KREDIT staff intact after the merger. .
The combined Phillip Bank has a total of 89 branches throughout Cambodia, including 83 KREDIT branches and 6 Phillip Bank branches.
This combination means that KREDIT customers will be able to access all of Philip Bank's advanced services such as savings, loans, mobile banking and online banking, which will be launched soon. Separately, Phillip Bank customers will be able to use KREDIT ATMs / Deposits Nationwide at no extra charge.
In the first phase, after this formal merger, KREDIT's 12 branches in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Battambang, Kampot, Takeo, Banteay Meanchey, Kampong Chhnang, Kampong Speu, Kratie and Svay Antor districts will be transformed.
These redesigned branches will have an attractive appearance and modern style, similar to the model branches of Phillip Bank, located along Kampuchea Krom Boulevard in Phnom Penh, which was officially inaugurated in November 2019.
As of December 2019, the financial statements of Phillip Bank show that the consolidated entity has a total assets of US $ 623 million, US $ 400 million in deposits and US $ 490 million in loans, along with depositors. 91,000 people and nearly 69,000 loan customers.
KREDIT started as a small NGO project under the auspices of the United States World Relief in 1993 and has gradually transformed itself for 27 years into one of the leading microfinance institutions in the world. Cambodia, with a core mission to support the country's development through its financial services and a strong social program to help vulnerable people.
This social program will continue to operate under the management of Phillip Bank and will be renamed "Support Our Village", an NGO that focuses primarily on child welfare, education and financial literacy. The body of Samdech Thommalikhet Las Lay was cremated 100 days after his death
(Phnom Penh): The body of Samdech Sangha Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay was cremated this morning, February 3, 2020, in the garden in front of Wat Botum Vatey. His body was cremated by Senate President Samdech Say Chhum.
Prior to the cremation, the monk was paraded from Wat Sansom Kosal with the participation of many monks, officials and other Buddhists.
Mr. Seng Somony, spokesman for the Ministry of Cults and Religions, said that the relics of Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay will be kept at the stupa in Wat Sansom Kosal. Mr. Somony said that officials, priests and pagoda committee will hold the ceremony until February 5, 2020.
Please be informed that Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Sansom Kosal, passed away on October 29, 2019 at the age of 106.
Samdech Preah Thommalikhet Las Lay was born on Wednesday, the 7th day of the lunar month of Chhnang Thao in the Buddhist era 2457, corresponding to the Christian era 1914 in Thoung village, Thoung commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province. His father is Acharya Lak and his mother is Su Ouch. He has 10 siblings, 7 brothers and 3 sisters, and is the fifth son in the family.
At the age of 12, his parents asked Las Lay to take him to be a monk in the presence of Rev. El Kom, and his parents sent him to study the Dharma in the presence of Rev. Moha M. at Wat Preah Puth Mean Bon in Phnom Penh. Later, he went to live at Wat Ounalom to continue his studies until he was 19 years old, before leaving the seminary to serve his parents.
According to the book "The Great Man of Buddhism in Cambodia", at the age of 21, his parents took him to be a monk under the name of Ouk at Wat Samrong, Veal Pun Commune, Thpong District, Kampong Speu Province (west of Udong Market). Which is the hometown of Nhom Srey. In that year, Bhikkhu Las Lay went to stay at Wat Mohamandrey to continue his studies.
