The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) presents the results of a two-day party convention chaired by Samdech Techo Hun Sen (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On February 2, 2020, under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Party, and Samdech Heng Samrin, Honorary President of the Party, closed, and laid down many work plans for 2020.
According to the announcement of the Cambodian People's Party, in the meeting attended by about 3,420 members discussed and approved 11 points, including:
1. The meeting unanimously discussed and approved the report on the general situation and work of the party in 2019 and the direction of tasks for 2020, including the roles, responsibilities and procedures of the grassroots working group and sub-national administrative reform.
2. The Conference noted and was proud of the general situation of the nation moving forward on the path of peace, democracy, rule of law and development.
3. A conference to thank the Cambodian people everywhere who clearly understand the value of peace and are committed to maintaining peace. In particular, actively involved with the government in the prevention and repression of extremists.
4: The meeting also respected and thanked the Commune / Sangkat Council for giving confidence to the leadership of the party by going to the polls and voting for the Capital, Provincial, District and Khan Councils of the third mandate on May 26, 2019.
The meeting examined and evaluated the movement of public administration reform, public financial management reform, decentralization reform, decentralization and anti-corruption. Promote institutional governance, human resource development, quality public service, transparency, and justice. Srah Dai together to reform all fields, all sectors according to the 5th approach: mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, healing and surgery.
6. The conference promotes the implementation of national social protection policies by strengthening and developing aid and social security systems, and strengthening food and nutrition security. Strive to maintain the job security of workers, strengthen policies to help farmers maintain stable agricultural prices and expand agricultural markets.
7. The Assembly declares that it strongly opposes the color revolution movement and promotes strict implementation of the law against organizations and individuals who violate the law. Affirm the unwavering position in preserving the multi-party liberal democracy in Cambodia.
8: The Conference of the National League for the Preservation of Peace, held a public gathering on December 29 every year to commemorate the anniversary of the end of the civil war in Cambodia, a memorial of win-win politics and education on the meaning of win-win politics.
9. The Conference shall pay attention to the global situation, which is evolving in a complex, fast, and unpredictable way, which poses increasing challenges and risks in the military, security, economy and society. Some strong countries are using the issues of democracy and human rights to pressure and violate the sovereignty of small countries as a threat to the peace, stability and development of Cambodia and small countries.
The Conference praised the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, for successfully defending the independence, national sovereignty, territorial integrity, neutrality, peace, security, political stability and national unity, conducive to socio-economic development and maintaining the internal reform motto. Develop external friends in an independent spirit.
10. The meeting highly appreciated the Party committees at all levels, the Party working group, the grassroots officials who have accomplished all the tasks and are confident that they will continue to actively in the spirit of unity, high internal unity, sharp will to be the core of the people's movement. People.
11. The Conference calls on all people to unite as a whole around the government under the shadow of the King together to build national social achievements, safeguard peace and promote socio-economic development towards a bright and prosperous future. .
