National Commission: In 2019, 59 forest crime perpetrators were arrested
(Phnom Penh): In 2019, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resources Crimes arrested and sent 59 forest crime perpetrators to court. In addition to arresting the perpetrators of the forest crime, 491 vehicles and timber transport vehicles were confiscated, and a total of 212 Bakong vehicles and processing vehicles were blown up, burned and destroyed.
The press release on the progress of the work of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes on February 2, 2020 said that in 2019, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes seized 9 mixed trees. , 215,876 cubic meters.
At present, large-scale illegal logging and timber transportation is quiet, but there is still fraud, illegal transportation of non-timber forest products in the form of Samsung trucks, recycling trucks. Small bulldozers, motorcycles, ox carts, buffalo carts, tuk-tuks and so on.
However, the National Commission and the competent authorities continue to educate the public so that everyone is aware of the laws related to the forest in order to avoid illegal activities and participate in the preservation of the forest for the benefit. Nation and the whole world.
The National Commission also called on the public and the media to continue to provide accurate information to the authorities at all levels in order to prevent and crack down on forest crime.
For 2020, in order to participate in the conservation of natural resources more effectively, the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes has set out the following measures:
First, the Governor of the Capital-Province, Municipality-District-Khan, through the Capital-Province-Municipality-District-Khan-Khan Administrative Unity Command, leads and coordinates the competent forces and competent officers within their jurisdiction to inspect all transportation. All permitted non-timber forest products from the beginning, middle and end.
Inspect warehouses, warehouses, handicrafts, non-timber forest products and take necessary measures in accordance with the Royal Government's Circular No. 05 S.R.N. on necessary measures to strengthen natural resource management dated 22 September 2012 2016.
Second, the person or company involved in committing this forest crime will have to take legal action. Suspects and exhibits must build a case to be sent to the prosecutor's office according to the procedure.
Third, the means of equipment and materials that destroy the forest, such as cars, motorcycles, ox carts, buffalo carts, chainsaws, etc., have been requested to the competent authorities to be destroyed in accordance with Article 119 of the Code of Criminal Procedure. Or for property such as weapons or explosives, as well as illegally possessed items, cannot be returned. "Those items must be confiscated as state property or destroyed."
It should be noted that the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes was established by the Royal Government on December 7, 2016, with the composition of the Royal Gendarmerie, the Ministry of Environment and the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and other authorities. Sub-national as well.
In that decision, Mr. Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, was appointed Chairman of the National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resources Crimes.
The National Commission for the Prevention and Suppression of Natural Resource Crimes has the role and duties of preventing and cracking down on natural resource crimes such as deforestation, illegal timber transportation and export, wildlife capture and illegal wildlife export, logging. Invasion of state land as well as illegal mining throughout the country.
The commission also has the role and responsibilities of investigating and investigating the perpetrators and stakeholders and activities of natural resource crimes. Arrest the perpetrators and evidence of the crime and prepare a case to be sent to court. Cooperate with Vietnam, Thailand and Laos to prevent and suppress natural resource crimes effectively if necessary.
