He added that such a design is unique to the Cambodian market, which is more attractive and appeals to users of all ages. Legal Awareness: Cambodian Judicial Jurisdiction for Offenses Committed Abroad
(Phnom Penh): In general, in Cambodian society, criminal offenses are always prevalent, and those crimes are not only in the Kingdom of Cambodia, but also abroad, the same crimes are committed. .
At the same time, there are some cases of crimes committed abroad, in which there are perpetrators or victims who are Cambodian and as well as some other crimes that are committed against and affect the interests. Of the Kingdom of Cambodia, for example. Therefore, how does the Cambodian court have jurisdiction to deal with crimes committed abroad?
This week, the Cambodian International Cooperation Lawyers Association, in collaboration with FRESH NEWS, would like to raise the topic of "Cambodian judicial jurisdiction for crimes committed abroad" to share with the people and students as follows:
According to the Criminal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, in criminal cases, the courts of Cambodia have jurisdiction over all cases committed on the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia, meanwhile, for certain offenses committed outside the territory. Overseas) Cambodian courts also have jurisdiction.
Defining jurisdiction over crimes committed abroad is one of the principles of the application of Cambodian criminal law in the territory or outside the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
According to the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the jurisdiction over the crimes committed abroad, in which the Cambodian court has jurisdiction over all crimes and misdemeanors committed by Cambodian citizens and all crimes committed. Has committed crimes against Cambodians, including a number of separate crimes.
1 * Offenses committed by Cambodian citizens: Cases where Cambodian citizens have committed any crime in foreign (foreign) territory, the Cambodian court has jurisdiction over all crimes. This means that if Cambodian law determines that an act committed by a Cambodian citizen abroad is a type of crime, then Cambodian law must be applied and the Cambodian court has jurisdiction to try it, even though in that foreign state there is no law that That act is a crime.
For misdemeanors, Cambodian law has jurisdiction unless the laws of the country in which the Cambodian citizen committed the offense determine that the act is a criminal offense. This means that if the foreign state does not have a law that stipulates that the act committed by a Cambodian citizen is a crime, Cambodian law has no jurisdiction to apply, even if that act is an actual crime.
2 * Cases of crimes committed against Cambodians: The Cambodian criminal law also has jurisdiction over all crimes committed abroad, whether by Cambodian citizens or by foreigners on the victims. Khmer nationality when the crime was committed. This means that for Cambodian victims, the Cambodian court has jurisdiction only for crimes, whether the perpetrators are Cambodian or foreign.
In fact, according to the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, those offenses include: * Offenses against the security of the Kingdom of Cambodia. * Offenses against forgery of official seals of the Kingdom of Cambodia. Law in the Kingdom of Cambodia. * Offenses against the location or agency of the embassy or consulate of the Kingdom of Cambodia. And * Offenses against the embassy or consulate of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
In summary, for offenses committed abroad, the courts of Cambodia are competent in accordance with the application of the criminal law of the Kingdom of Cambodia for offenses committed outside the territory, including offenses committed by naturalized citizens. Khmer for crimes is a felony and misdemeanor, and in all crimes where the victim is a Cambodian citizen, as well as a number of other specific crimes committed against Cambodia.
Defining jurisdiction over crimes abroad is a principle to ensure the protection of the rights and interests of the Cambodian people, as well as to protect the interests of Cambodia, as the law abroad may have more severe penalties. The law in Cambodia, or there is a gap that leads the perpetrators to escape punishment, for example.
However, the Kingdom of Cambodia respects the principle of sovereignty and does not interfere in the internal affairs of foreign states, therefore, in order to implement the powers of this Cambodian law, it is necessary to obtain the consent of that foreign state through the signing of a bilateral agreement. For example, the extradition treaty.
