Police crack down on forest crime in O'Yadao district, confiscate 32 pieces of wood
(Ratanakkiri): Coalition forces cracked down on two forest crimes in O'Yang Dao district, Ratanakkiri province, confiscating 32 pieces of wood but could not find the perpetrators.
The operation to crack down on forest crime, which took place on February 2, 2020, was under the direct command of Brigadier General Thao Yen, Commander of the Ratanakkiri Provincial Gendarmerie, and was joined by six local O'Yadao District Gendarmerie forces in collaboration with One National Gendarmerie and four 102nd Regiment troops led by Brigadier General Sok Min, Commander of O'Yadao District Local Gendarmerie.
Colonel Sok Min said that during this operation, the joint police went to two different targets, the first target was located in Lum village, Pak Nhay commune, and found 18 pieces of sokrom wood, and the second target was In Lum village, Pak Nhay commune, 14 pieces of Sokrom wood were found.
The local military commander of O'Yadao district confirmed that the two wooden objects were taken by an unidentified person and left at the above location. The above-mentioned timber was confiscated and transported by the police to be stored at the O'Yadao District Military Police Base temporarily to be handed over to the specialized force to measure and take further action.
