Health officials: Breastfeeding provides many benefits to maternal and infant health, including reducing the risk of certain diseases.
(Phnom Penh): Pharmacist Hun Huang, Deputy Director General of Health Technology of the Ministry of Health, said that breastfeeding provides many benefits to the health of mothers and babies, especially to reduce the high risk of postpartum hemorrhage. Babies help prevent iron deficiency and frequent pregnancies.
"Breast milk is considered to be the perfect food to provide the most energy and nutrients that babies need during the first six months of their lives," he said. Therefore, breastfeed for up to 6 months and continue to breastfeed for up to two years or more.
In addition, breastfeeding is important to: * Reduce breast and cervical cancer in mothers * Reduce the risk of hip fractures in mothers * Burn 5,000 calories per day * Cut Reduces the risk of diarrhea, vomiting, respiratory tract, constipation, eczema and obesity in infants.
This statement was made by Mr. HUN HUANG during the opening ceremony of the training course on the implementation of Sub-Decree No. 133 on the promotion of infant and child feeding products to health inspectors from the Phnom Penh Municipal Health Department, Kandal Province. Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang and Pursat provinces.
For the safety of people who use milk instead of breast milk, Pharmacist Ang Hok Srun, Director of the Food Safety Office of the Department of Food, Drug, Medical Equipment and Cosmetics, Ministry of Health, in addition to training, also inspected the markets and pharmacies. Selling products for feeding babies and children, such as milk, formula, bottle, milk, powder, nipple, etc.
