Samdech Heng Samrin: Political power alone has forced the CPP to increase its responsibility to the nation and the people of Cambodia (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary President The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) has stated that political power alone has forced the CPP to increase its responsibility to the nation and its people.
This statement was made by Samdech Heng Samrin on the occasion of the opening of the 42nd Meeting of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center this morning, February 1, 2020.
The Cambodian People's Party (CPP) won a landslide victory in the 6th National Assembly election in July 2018, controlling all 125 seats in the National Assembly and leading the current government. The election involved 20 parties, but 19 other parties won some votes but did not win seats.
However, this is not the first time for Cambodia to have a one-party National Assembly. Cambodia has existed in the history of Lon Nol during the Sangkum Reastr Niyum and Khmer Republic eras, and this one-party rule has also occurred in some democracies around the world.
