(Bangkok): At the 2nd Asia Tourism Film Festival and the 2nd Mekong Mega Film Festival in Bangkok, Thailand, the forum was very encouraging for the production and filming of many tourist destinations. To contribute to the promotion of those tourist sites, according to Mr. Kuch Panhasa, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, who confirmed to Fresh News after participating in this forum.
The forum was held on January 30, 2020 to promote the tourism potential of the Mekong region, which was organized by the Mekong Tourism Coordinating Office (MTCO) in collaboration with the Asia-Pacific Tourism Association (PATA) and Major tour operators in Bangkok, with the participation of guest speakers from public and private tourism businesses from a total of 150 countries in Asia.
Kuch Panhasa said that Asia and the Mekong are one of the fastest growing regions in the world in tourism, investment and trade, as well as film production. The program provides an opportunity for travelers to exchange their experiences and realities through film.
Sometimes problems that occur in an area (incident or accidental factor) create an opportunity for marketing that reflects the tourist destination in that area, as in the case of Thailand with 12 people. Trapped in a cave, a film was made about the purpose of the mountain.
The forum sees that the film has not only grossed hundreds of millions of dollars, but also shows the destinations and tourism products, as well as the lifestyle of the local people, which can attract tourists. More national-international.
