The meeting agreed on the promotion of ecotourism development through a joint study to identify ecotourism sites throughout the country, using mechanisms under the inter-ministerial work to manage and develop community-based tourism and ecotourism to request the Royal Government to designate ecotourism priority areas. To be developed based on a clear guideline (Guideline) and 4P cooperation mechanism.
UNESCO has supported the speedy launch of the Siem Reap Master Development Plan, which the Ministry of Tourism and the Inter-Ministerial Working Group are working on, focusing on six priority areas: Angkor, Siem Reap, Tonle Sap-Prek Toal, Phnom Kulen, Banteay Srei and Siem Reap Thmey. UNESCO will provide experts to review and comment on the draft plan.
