Singapore deploys 1,500 troops to pack 5.2 million masks for distribution
A total of 1,500 Singaporean troops are rushing to pack 5.2 million protective masks to distribute to the masses as Singapore seeks to curb the new strain of coronavirus. From China. This is according to a quote from CNA on Friday night, January 31, 2020.
The operation was carried out at the Singapore Military Institute (SAFTI), which began on Thursday night after Singapore authorities announced they would distribute four masks to each Singaporean family. The 1,500 Singapore troops have to take turns, each lasting eight hours, and should be able to pack 200,000 masks each.
