Samdech Kittipritthbandit Provides 45 Water Wells at a Cost of Over $ 100,000 to People in 3 Provinces
(Phnom Penh): In order to continue to solve water needs in remote rural areas, on January 31, 2020, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, provided 45 water wells worth 108,484 Dollars to provide water to 850 families (equivalent to 3,054 people) living in 3 provinces.
Among the 45 wells, 13 are water wells for Mondulkiri, 13 for Stung Treng and 19 for Preah Vihear.
From 2010 to 2019, the Cambodian Red Cross provided clean water to tens of thousands of families across the country by providing 1,695 water wells, as well as community ponds and water tanks.
