(Phnom Penh): The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will lead a high-level delegation to attend the 2020 World Summit of the Global Peace Federation on Peace, Security and Human Development in the Republic of Korea (South Korea). Three days from February 3 to 5, 2020. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia, which was received by Fresh News.
Senior officials accompanying Samdech Techo include Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, as well as a number of senior government officials and business leaders of the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce.
The Prime Minister will deliver a keynote address on the theme of the Summit on "Peace, Security and Human Development" along with a number of foreign dignitaries attending the 2020 World Summit of the Global Peace Federation. The Prime Minister will also meet with the Cambodian community, students and Cambodian workers living and working in the Republic of Korea. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs.
Please note that Cambodia and the Republic of Korea have excellent friendly relations and cooperation in many fields such as trade, investment, employment and education. Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipadei Non Nget is the Honorary President of the Meak Bochea Ceremony in Phnom Penh
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Preah Moha Sometheathipady Non Nget, Samdech Preah Sang, Director of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Preah Chao Athikar Wat Botum Vatey Reach Varam, on the afternoon of January 31, 2020, paid a courtesy call on the program to understand the Meak Bochea ceremony. Understanding and encouraging Buddhists to properly apply the teachings of Buddhism.
In addition, the Lotus Company and the Lotus Foundation have published a book on Meak Bochea, the Buddhist Birth Day, as an organization, written by Dr. Heng Mony Chenda, for distribution and reading. More understanding.
Meak Bochea is a major Buddhist festival that Cambodia celebrates every year. For this year, Meak Bochea will be celebrated on the 15th day of Meak, which is Wednesday, February 08, 2020. Not only Cambodia, but also other countries such as: Sri Lanka, Myanmar, Thailand and some other countries that practice Buddhism also celebrate this festival.
The celebration of Meak Bochea is to commemorate three important events, namely: the making of a rectangular assembly, the second: the Buddha performing the Patimok advice to the monks, and the third: the Buddha placing the age of Sangkha.
The age of Sangkha is the day when the Buddha determined that in the next three months he would enter Nirvana, which is the passing away of this world without returning. Three months later, he entered Nirvana at the age of 80.
