Minister Pan Sosak Chairs a Meeting to Discuss, Discuss and Approve Draft E-Commerce Strategy
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, chaired a meeting to review, discuss and approve the draft e-commerce strategy at the Ministry of Commerce on the evening of January 30, 2020.
In his opening remarks, Minister Pan Sosak said that the rapid evolution of technology and digital innovation has created many opportunities as well as challenges that require careful consideration of technology-based operations. Means.
These works are clearly highlighted with a long-term vision in the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 of the Royal Government of the sixth mandate at the third angle, as well as in the National Strategic Development Plan 2019-2023, which requires the government to review and prepare Body for the digital economy and in response to the Fourth Industrial Revolution.
In response to and contributing to the achievement of the priority goals set out in those policies and strategies, the Ministry of Commerce has developed an e-commerce strategy as a clear roadmap for the development of the trade sector. Electronic systems in Cambodia.
In addition, e-commerce strategies respond to the needs of the private sector, which needs a document outlining the government's vision and policy to develop the sector.
The development of e-commerce strategy at this time is in line with the passage of the e-commerce law, which the King, in the highest regard, has signed under Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1119/017, dated November 2, 2019.
The minister added that e-commerce is also an important topic in the negotiation of trade agreements in the regional and global framework. In fact, Cambodia has signed and ratified the ASEAN Agreement on E-Commerce, which is an important part of the legal framework and regulatory framework and facilitation of e-commerce growth in the ASEAN region.
E-commerce is also part of the Regional Comprehensive Partnership Agreement (RCEP) and is also under intense negotiation at the WTO to compile a WTO framework agreement.
Mr. Pan Sosak also informed the meeting that this e-commerce strategy is not just for the Ministry of Commerce alone, but a joint strategy that requires all ministries and institutions related to trade to work together to implement in Aims to promote e-commerce development policy in the current and future context for the common benefit of Cambodia as a whole.
After the discussion at the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak instructed the Secretariat to consider the opinion of the inter-ministerial at that time to review as necessary before preparing for implementation. Director of Phnom Penh Department of Social Affairs Holds Vocational Training on Life Skills for Drug Victims at My Opportunity Center
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of January 31, 2020, My Opportunity Center opened the first vocational skills training course for life victims in 2020 for 64 drug victims with the participation of representatives from 14 districts and Guardians, too.
Ms. Mom Chandani, Director of the Department of Social Affairs of Phnom Penh and President of the Opportunity Center, said that this event was held to help young people who are receiving treatment for drug addicts with the attention of the Royal Government. The leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, as well as Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh.
Ms. Mom Chandani continued that the victims of drug abuse are all have the opportunity to develop themselves, society, family and society, important on their own commitment. Therefore, let all young people who are addicted to drugs make an effort to learn and acquire knowledge and skills in order to work for the benefit of our society and our families.
She said that you have to be a good citizen to ease the burden of family, society and contribute to the development of our society. For parents, guardians must strive to heal their children while integrating back into the community to become good children, citizens.
Ms. Mom Chandani said that currently there are 1,865 young people who have used drugs and are being treated at Opportunity Health Center, including 100 women.
At the same time, Ms. Mom Chandany also said that the number of cases of victims or victims due to drugs, it is small that return to the center. She emphasizes that the case of addiction or not, it depends on the young men and women who have suffered, whether they want to live in a good society that is civilized in this era of peace.
Ms. Mom Chandani, Director of the Department of Social Affairs of Phnom Penh, confirmed that in 2020, My Opportunity Center plans to integrate more than 500 drug addicts into society after receiving rehabilitation.
