According to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Cambodia currently has diplomatic relations with 174 countries and 63 embassies abroad.
In 2019, Cambodia also bought an embassy building in Ankara, Turkey, began renovating the embassies in Sofia, Bulgaria and Belgrade, Serbia, and opened a new consulate general in Haikou. The ministry has set up eight more bilateral political consultations, bringing the total to 34.
Expanding friendships, cooperation and relations is one of the priority tasks that Samdech Techo Hun Sen has set for the Ministry of Foreign Affairs to implement in 2020.
Samdech Techo urged the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia to continue to strengthen the existing friendship, cooperation, relations and good partnership with friendly countries. The Prime Minister also recommended efforts to restore cooperative relations with old friends and seek to build good relations with new friends, especially in Eastern and Central Europe, Central Asia, Africa, the Middle East and Latin America.
