The European Commission, on the grounds that Cambodia's implementation of democracy and respect for human rights is deficient, is in the process of removing Cambodia's tariff preferences. The final decision of the European Commission will be announced in February 2020. This measure is seen as one of the European Commission sanctions on Cambodia.
In front of the ambassadors and embassy officials of friendly countries who attended this morning's ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the policy of sanctions is the policy of big countries, oppressing smaller countries, not the right politics. No. In particular, they implement this policy in the name of values and principles that they use or do not use in accordance with the circumstances and interests that are favorable to them.
For Cambodia, a country that has suffered from the flames of war for nearly 30 years and has recovered to the current situation, the international community should help strengthen and unite rather than break the barriers to weaken their measures. This is the confirmation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, stated, "For Cambodia, the international community should help us to become stronger and more united, rather than dividing the barriers to weakening by measures that could become its third mistake."
Samdech Techo continued, "Our political, economic and social choices should be respected because since the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime until now, those choices have always met the real needs of the country and its people." That is the choice that has restored the Cambodian people to their basic rights: food, health care, education, shelter, housing, labor rights, culture and freedom. ”
For Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the international community's attempts to stifle Cambodia's development through sanctions could be the third time they have done so, as they have already done twice. The first mistake was to support the military in a coup to oust Norodom Sihanouk as head of state in 1970, and the second mistake was to support the Khmer Rouge seat at the United Nations after the regime was overthrown in 1979.
Although Cambodia is facing the removal of the preferential tariff system from the European Union, in this morning's ceremony, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reiterated that he does not allow anyone to come to Cambodia and does not take sovereignty The nation trades with any country's preferential tariffs or aid.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also stressed that it is worthless and cheap for a country that can not implement its laws and is required to follow the coercion of other countries.
