Samdech Techo stated that in the previous generation, Cambodia had economic blockades in all directions, leaving only the Soviet Union and Eastern Europe, plus Vietnam, Laos and India, which provided support for Cambodia to survive. But now we have many friends, many partners who do business together.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, so far Cambodia has diplomatic relations with 174 countries in the world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's statement was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen presided over the closing ceremony of the 2019 work review meeting and the work direction for 2020 of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs at the Peace Palace.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the coming years, the current tensions, challenges and challenges will continue to develop in a complex, difficult to predict direction in the areas of politics, economy, military and security.
He added that tensions in some areas could escalate to dangerous levels in South Asia, Latin America and Africa, especially in fragile areas.
Another challenge for Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, is the use of excuses for the promotion of democracy and human rights to double standards and inappropriate interference in the internal affairs of other countries through the use of political and economic instruments. Serious pressure on weak countries, including Cambodia.
The Prime Minister stated that given the above-mentioned situation, the challenges require Cambodia to adhere to a foreign policy that serves to promote and protect the national interest by concentrating on the following five major tasks:
The second big task: follow the motto "Increase external friends based on the spirit of national independence." Cambodia will continue to strive to strengthen existing ties of cooperation, good relations and good partnerships with friendly countries, restore cooperative relations with old friends and seek to build good relations with new friends, especially in Eastern Europe and the Middle East. Central Asia, Central Africa, the Middle East and Latin America.
Cambodia will further contribute to building the ASEAN Community by serving the people and taking the people as the core, maintaining and strengthening the unity and centrality of ASEAN, and through ASEAN promoting and strengthening relations with external partners for development and economic growth. Society is based on two fundamental principles: adherence to consensus in all decisions and non-interference in internal affairs.
Task 3: Promote economic diplomacy to contribute to professional institutions in attracting foreign investment, diversify investment sources, expand markets, bring Cambodian products abroad, attract tourists and promote national culture on the international stage. Contribute to efforts to sign the Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (RCEP), continue to negotiate new trade agreements, especially with China, the Republic of Korea and the EU-Asia Economic Union.
Final work 5: Improving the quality, efficiency and capacity building of diplomats to address human resource challenges facing the Ministry of Foreign Affairs as well as other ministries and institutions.
Senior Officials of the Ministry of Interior and Citizens Invite 259 Monks to Pray for Happiness and Dedication to Victims of Traffic Accident for 3 Days in Tapon Commune, Battambang Province
(Battambang): Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior and Chairman of the National Task Force for Sangke District, Battambang Province, Mr. Kol Vireak, Preah Chao Athikar Wat Tapon and Buddhists in the morning of January 31, 2020 Dedication of Kosal to the victims of traffic accidents at Basset Temple, Tapon Commune, Sangke District, Battambang Province.
The ceremony was also attended by leaders, civil servants, forces and members of the national working group of districts, communes, villages, students and Buddhists at three pagodas: Wat Tapon, Wat Rokar and Wat Nora, as well as many other relevant officials.
Mr. Kol Virak stated that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has maintained peace for the people and has pursued a win-win policy of uniting the Khmer nation to live under the shadow of peace with historical success.
Mr. Kol Vireak stated that along with the development of the base, there is a lot of progress, especially the roads are much better in the localities everywhere, all kinds of vehicles are also abundant, including respecting the traffic laws of the people who drive on the roads. The traffic law has not been fully complied with yet, which has led to an increase in the accident rate, leading to the National Road Safety Committee issuing an official declaration.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Interior said that in implementing the road traffic law, according to the situation of road traffic accidents in 2019, there has been a sharp increase in deaths and injuries and damage to public property, private property compared to 2018.
* Vehicle growth factor of about 37% * Infrastructure factors that are not yet balanced with vehicle growth * Factors of road users who do not respect and strictly enforce the law on road traffic.
Due to the high number of deaths and injuries due to the increase in traffic accidents, the national team to help local Sangke district and colleagues joined with the Chief Inspector of Wat Tapon and some other pagodas to hold religious ceremonies for 3 days. Blessings were made on the streets, chasing evils, incidents, and prayers for peace, protection of peace, and devotion to the dead, asking for more traffic accidents.
Mr. Kol Vireak called on all people to work together to protect and maintain this most difficult peace that has been achieved for a long and sustainable future for future generations under the slogan that January 7 Only peace, only peace, only everything until today, "Thank you for peace."
Speaking on the morning of January 31, 2020, on the occasion of closing the meeting of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that countries that have problems with Europe include: Malaysia, Indonesia, Cambodia, Myanmar, And the Philippines.
"Europe currently has bad relations with ASEAN," he said. There are already five countries with the most serious problems with Europe: Indonesia and Malaysia under the pretext of protecting the environment against deforestation. Europe has begun moving toward a halt to Malaysia and Indonesia's palm oil purchases, a response that will strain relations between the two countries.
"Europe has also reached out to Cambodia, Myanmar and the Philippines on human rights issues, not to mention some other countries where Europe has always threatened ASEAN countries." Samdech Techo emphasizes further.
Samdech Techo questioned that the strategic partnership can move faster between Europe and ASEAN if Europe has the attitude of interfering with ASEAN countries. According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, ASEAN has big countries, small countries, rich and poor countries, but ASEAN is not divided and ASEAN does not have big brothers.
Samdech continued that if you look at the reality, this experience shows that today, Britain has reached the date of leaving Europe. Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked the question, "After Britain, who else can leave Europe?"
Samdech reminded that a Rector in England asked Samdech which ASEAN members wanted to leave ASEAN? Samdech replied that the questioner should change this question by asking the question of which European countries will leave Europe, such as the United Kingdom, because in the ASEAN framework there is no provision for departure or expulsion.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that Europe after the departure of Britain, will there be any departure from other countries, while now there is a current of pro-Europe and anti-European current itself. Samdech stated that the problem of division in the European Union is a lesson to strengthen the ASEAN community.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that the British character is the co-founder of the European Union, but what we have seen in the last British election is the overwhelming support of the British people for an election that the director. The British minister set out to leave Europe with an agreement. This shows that the British people are tired of Europe.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen further stated that the principle of consensus is the fundamental principle for the strength of ASEAN. ASEAN needs to synthesize South Korea and India for its own strength.
