This memorial of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made this morning, January 31, 2020, on the occasion that Samdech presided over the closing ceremony of the 2019 Annual Meeting and the work direction for 2020 of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and Cooperation. International at the Peace Palace.
The announcement of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia was made at the closing ceremony of the meeting of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation held at the Peace Palace this morning, January 31, 2020.
On that occasion, Samdech affirmed about the foreign policy that Cambodia will continue to strive to strengthen the existing friendship, cooperation, relations and good partnership with friendly countries, restore cooperation relations with old friends and seek to build Good relations with new friends, especially in Eastern and Central Europe, Central Asia, Africa, the Middle East and Latin America.
After peace, Cambodia has begun to restore its foreign relations with other countries in recent decades after decades of war. According to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, Cambodia has so far had diplomatic relations with 174 countries around the world.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will contribute more and more to the building of the ASEAN Community by serving the people and taking the people as the core, maintaining and strengthening the unity and centrality of ASEAN, and through ASEAN will promote and strengthen relations with External partners for development and economic and social growth are based on two fundamental principles: adherence to consensus in all decisions and non-interference in internal affairs.
He added that Cambodia continues to support and strengthen multilateralism in global affairs and contribute to global efforts to address the challenges and dangers that threaten peace, security and international order. One based on law and sustainable development.
