Samdech Kittipritthbandit's message of thanks to His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia is as follows: Senior official of the Ministry of Economy: Cambodia's economy in 2020 will still be able to achieve around 6% despite the difficulties And more risks
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, affirmed that Cambodia's economic growth in 2020 will still be able to achieve around 6%, despite many difficulties and risks, both internal and external. More specifically, the case of the spread of the coronavirus in China, Cambodia's largest economic partner.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth's confirmation was made on January 30, 2020 in a public forum on macroeconomic management and the 2020 budget.
The public forum was chaired by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, with the participation of representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, Supreme Advisory Council, Development Partners, Civil Society, Research Institutions, Higher Education Institutions. , The private sector, the media and national and international journalists, as well as more than 300 researchers, students and youth.
He said that exports had a good growth momentum, with an increase of about 15%, and the inflow of foreign direct investment increased by 13% of GDP, which improved the balance of payments in general. International reserves have risen to more than $ 17.4 billion, which can guarantee imports for up to eight months.
The Permanent Secretary of State said that achieving high and strong economic growth and macroeconomic stability, Cambodia also achieved good results in the management of public finances, reflected by strong growth. And more sustainable in all types of revenue collection and more efficient in managing national budget expenditures.
This allows us to achieve a current account surplus of more than 8% of GDP, compared to the planned 2.81% of GDP, which increases the government's savings to about 18% of GDP. Expansion of budget space and reserve budget resources to prepare for crises and other risks eventually.
It should be noted that according to the IMF recommendation for countries with high economic status and dollarization like Cambodia, in order to ensure budget sustainability in times of crisis, fiscal space or savings should be maintained at only about 6% of GDP. At the same time, Cambodia's public debt situation remains stable and risk is low.
He pointed out that the target of 6.5% of GDP growth in the 2020 budget already includes the withdrawal of the EBA from the European Union, because we know it will come just before. Or later. Therefore, even if the EU removes this preferential trade system in whole or in part, the Cambodian economy will not collapse because we are already prepared.
