This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen closed the meeting to review the work of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, January 31, 2020, presided over the closing ceremony of the 2019 Annual Meeting and the work direction for 2020 of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs. The closing ceremony was held at the Peace Palace.
On the morning of January 30, 2020, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation held a meeting to review the work achieved in 2019 and set the work direction to be implemented in 2020.
The opening ceremony was presided over by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. The event was also attended by leaders and civil servants of the Ministry, Ambassadors, Permanent Representatives, Consuls, Honorary Consuls and representatives of relevant ministries and institutions of Cambodia.
Mr. Prak Sokhon at the opening ceremony of the conference presented many works that the Ministry has achieved in 2019. In particular, strengthening diplomatic relations with friendly countries.
According to Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Cambodia currently has diplomatic relations with 174 countries and 63 foreign missions.
The Minister of Foreign Affairs stated that the motto "Internal reform and increase of external friends based on the spirit of national independence" that Samdech Techo Prime Minister has set out is very appropriate to the work of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. .
He said that in 2019, Cambodia began to restore diplomatic relations and friendship with its old friends, including the Czech Republic, Bulgaria, Hungary, Romania, Serbia. Cambodia has even bought an embassy building in Ankara, started renovating its embassy in Sofia and Belgrade, opened a new consulate general in Haikou and is considering opening a new embassy in Budapest.
