Deputy Director General of Calmette Hospital: Treatment through Radiation Intervention is Safe and Effective
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Sanya, Deputy Director General of Calmette Hospital, stated that the field of radiological intervention does not require surgery and that the treatment is highly effective and reduces the length of treatment, especially the treatment of stroke and cancer, including Other diseases.
He made the remarks at a seminar on "Radiation Intervention and Its Role in Modern Medicine" at Calmette Hospital on January 30, 2020.
This workshop is designed to share the development of radiological interventions as well as raise awareness of the importance and effectiveness of new techniques in the treatment of various diseases.
This radiotherapy treatment is not harmful to health, and Calmette Hospital team of doctors is ready to bring all these radiotherapy intervention techniques to improve the quality of care and treatment for the people of Cambodia. International standards.
He said that the field of radiological intervention is a specialty in medicine that has grown rapidly in the last two decades, because new discoveries in the field of radiology have actively contributed to the treatment of many diseases. No need for more effective surgery with lower risk and less pain.
Kong Sanya said that the radiological intervention can help treat patients with stroke, a large number of cancers and many other diseases effectively if patients come for timely treatment.
