According to the Royal Government of Cambodia, the Cambodian economy is expected to grow by 6.5 percent by 2020, but due to the outbreak of pneumonia in China, there may be an outbreak, according to the Ministry of Economy. Impact on Cambodia, especially tourism, the economy may shrink to 6 percent.
In addition, there are other risks influencing Cambodia's economic growth, including the slowdown in global economic growth, uncertainty over the situation in the Middle East, Sino-US trade disputes and climate change. Original.
The senior official confirmed that the slowdown in economic growth affected not only Cambodia, but also countries in the region such as Thailand and Singapore.
