(Phnom Penh): In the debate regarding the activities of Mr. Kem Sokha between 2007 and 2012 in the hearing of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court on January 30, 2020, the accused Kem Sokha presented some new evidence that in There is also a photo of him shaking hands with the President of China and the Prime Minister of Japan.
Speaking at a press conference after Thursday's hearing, civil party lawyer Ky Tech described the photographic evidence presented by Kem Sokha as "irrevocable" during the handshake. As a senator only.
He told reporters: "We see the acquittal of the accused, such as filing a photo this morning, showing a lot of photos that we see that the evidence can not release him. "No, because he took the hand that he shook hands with the President of China, the Prime Minister of Japan, when he was a senator."
