Following today's adjournment, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court will resume hearings on Kem Sokha's peace deal with foreigners on Wednesday and Thursday next week, continuing to debate Kem Sokha's activities between 2007 and 2007. 2012.
It should be noted that Mr. Kem Sokha was arrested on September 3, 2017 in connection with the act of treason, conspiracy with foreigners to overthrow the Royal Government, and was detained in Trapeang Phlong Prison, Tbong Khmum Province for more than A year after a video was leaked in which he said he followed foreign guidelines for transforming Cambodia, following in the footsteps of Yugoslavia and Serbia.
He was later placed under judicial supervision, barred from meeting former CNRP leaders, foreigners, and unable to leave the court-designated border.
However, on November 10, 2019, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court decided to revise the inspection conditions, releasing Mr. Kem Sokha more freely, with the court banning only a few rights, including: not to be released. Outside the territorial boundaries of the Kingdom of Cambodia must not engage in political activity and must respond to summons from all authorities.
