The power of the "Coronavirus" made the lawyers of the accused and the public wear masks in the courtroom of Kem Sokha's treason case
(Phnom Penh): Although coronary heart disease "Korona" is not yet acute in Cambodia, concerns about the spread of the virus are plaguing the minds of Cambodians. To protect their health, many Cambodians start wearing masks, whether out in public or in the office. Mass has been selling like hot cakes until out of stock these days.
Not only ordinary people who are afraid of the "Corona" virus attacking the health in the courtroom "Peace with foreigners" or "treason" of Mr. Kem Sokha on January 29, 2020, which is In the third and fifth weeks of the trial, both defense lawyers, Kem Sokha, registrars, and the general public, both Cambodians and foreigners from embassies, mostly wore masks.
Wearing the mask may have caused some speech disturbance for Kem Sokha and his defense counsel. It has been observed that Kem Sokha, who is in a circle of horses in the courtroom, often removes his mask when answering questions from prosecutors as well as Plaintiff's lawyer and his defense attorney.
Separately, Mr. Kem Sokha's lawyers are the same, maybe the mask disturbs the speech, only when advocating or debating the story often see them remove the mask. When I stopped talking, I put on my mask again.
However, the three trial judges, two prosecutors and a government lawyer who were plaintiffs in the case did not wear masks. There is no explanation as to why he did not wear a mask, but perhaps they are aware of the transmission or spread of the virus, so they do not worry and do not wear a mask.
Due to the internal regulations, it is not allowed to take pictures in the courtroom, so there are no pictures to show readers.
It should be noted that the trial of Mr. Kem Sokha on January 29, 2020 has reached the end of the questioning of Mr. Kem Sokha's political activities between 1993 and 2007. Leading into questioning his political activities between 2007 and 2012.
From 2007 to 2012, when Kem Sokha resigned as the President of the Cambodian Center for Human Rights to form the Human Rights Party and to form the CNRP.
