In addition, Deputy Prime Minister Yim Chhay Ly also requested relevant ministries, local authorities at all levels, development agencies, NGOs and all people to support the implementation of the Ministry of Rural Development's 2020 plan to achieve new results. And all development partners, NGOs and the private sector continue to collaborate to support resources for the implementation of subsequent projects.
The Deputy Prime Minister said that with the results achieved by the Ministry of Development, it is an achievement that has greatly contributed to the successful implementation and development of rural areas, and he would like to note those results in conjunction with And some important recommendations as follows:
First, he would like to congratulate and appreciate these proud achievements, especially the four core strategic goals of the Ministry: to strengthen institutions, develop capacity and human resources, develop physical and communication infrastructure, improve living conditions and Improve the livelihoods of rural communities and diversify rural economic activities. These core goals are comprehensive, covering the entire jurisdiction of the ministry and the government's reform program.
Second, continue to support the Royal Government to ensure peace and political stability in Cambodia.
Third, continue to support and participate more actively in the implementation of the fourth phase of the Rectangular Strategic Reform Program of the Royal Government.
Fourth, continue to promote the development of the capacity of civil servants and the development of institutions to better improve the efficiency of work to achieve further growth.
Fifth, continue to study and research new technologies to process some materials instead of the drastic reduction of raw materials, including: red gravel, sand, mountains, etc. for the construction, rehabilitation, maintenance and repair of rural roads.
Sixth, continue to improve the quality of life of rural people and strive to achieve the vision of the National Policy on Rural Water Supply and Sanitation 2025, all rural people must have adequate water supply and sanitation services. And live in a hygienic and sustainable environment.
Seventh, continue to pay attention to change the attitude of living to understand health issues, clean living and stop open defecation (ODF) 2025 throughout the country.
Eighth: Continue to promote rural economic activity through village, one product, one product and entrepreneurial activities to support increasing household income and preventing risky migration.
Ninth: Continue to implement decentralization and deconcentration reforms by striving for the integration of civil servants, resources and assets at the sub-national level in order to maintain the stability of democratic local development at the sub-national level.
10th: Continue to strengthen and expand cooperation with private sector partners and friendly countries to mobilize new financial resources, techniques and technologies to support the development of rural development.
Twelfth: Collaborate with the Ministry of Public Works and Transport to develop procedures and methods for road master planning, project planning and project prioritization.
It should be noted that the Ministry of Rural Development has inspired and gathered ideas and experiences from leaders and officials at all levels to compile a five-year strategic plan for rural development (2019-2023) with the main goal is to continue. Improve the quality and value of life of rural people by focusing on four programs, including:
First, strengthen capacity and human resource development institutions to ensure effective management of the Ministry, support human resource development programs and good governance, sustainable development at both the national and sub-national levels, to contribute to the implementation of public administration reform programs. Public financial management reform, decentralization and deconcentration reforms and other reforms to be more effective.
Second, develop more physical and communication infrastructure to all areas of rural areas, especially areas with high economic potential.
Third, to improve the living conditions of rural communities, aiming to improve the quality of comfortable living. The rural areas will be covered by villages, communes, clean living environment, access to many essential services as part of promoting a modern lifestyle.
Fourth, diversify rural economic activities in the sense of creating jobs, entrepreneurship and economic activities to diversify from agriculture and non-agriculture in rural communities to solve the problems of daily life to increase the income of each family in rural areas. The Ministry of Rural Development issued a press release on the results of the meeting to review the work results in 2019 and work directions for 2020.
