(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health of Cambodia, requested the competent authorities to take legal action against those who exaggerate the facts on social media about the new type of coronary heart disease, which makes people There is fear.
On the morning of January 29, 2020, it was reported on social media that a Chinese patient with coronavirus had been taken to a Russian hospital, much to his surprise. While the Royal Government of Cambodia is taking action against those who fabricate information about the new respiratory disease, which is shared on social media, once in this province, once in that province, causing chaos.
In connection with this case, the director of the Russian hospital and the governor of Boeung Keng Kang district held a press conference at noon on January 29, 2020, confirming that there were no cases of corona patients in the Russian hospital, which is not like the rumors Do not post on social media.
Phnom Penh Municipal Administration spokesman Met Meas Pheakdey confirmed that so far no new cases of coronavirus have been found in Russian hospitals, as well as throughout Phnom Penh, according to online rumors. That society.
In connection with the distribution of false information about this new type of respiratory disease, the Minister of Health, Mr. Mam Bun Heng, also rejected the publication that there were two new cases of respiratory disease on the bodies of two Chinese people in the province. Koh Kong as well.
So far, according to the Cambodian Minister of Health, there has been only one case of coronary heart disease. The virus was found on a 60-year-old Chinese man traveling from Wuhan, Hubei Province, China to Sihanoukville on January 23, 2020. The Chinese man came with three other family members, but his family has not yet been diagnosed with the deadly disease.
In relation to the above Chinese medical condition, so far the medical condition is not serious and is returning to improve.
