The Cash Support Program for Pregnant Women and Children Under 2 in Poor Families has been implemented by the Ministry of Health since June 2019 to expand its coverage nationwide. The program has been transferred to the Ministry of Social Affairs Veterans And Youth Rehabilitation, led by the Department of Social Welfare, from January 1, 2020 onwards.
In order for women and children in poor families across the country to benefit from this program, the Department of Social Welfare, which is the leader in implementing this program, has trained more than 8,000 officials and facilitators in all capitals, provinces and communes across the country. Equipped and installed information management technology and provided more than 1,700 tablets.
