Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng: Police officers not only serve their party or family, but also serve the whole national interest
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, reminded that National Police officers do not only serve the interests of their party or their families, saying that National Police officers serve the interests of the nation and All the general population.
The remarks of Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng were made this morning, January 29, 2020, on the occasion of presiding over the handing over of vehicles to the 25 Capital-Provincial Police Commissions for the benefit of the unit to protect security and order. Citizens within their jurisdiction.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that as an officer of the National Police, he must fulfill his duties in accordance with the profession assigned by the management and with professional ethics, that is, be honest with his role to serve the nation for the people and not be an exception. To all individuals who make mistakes.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng stated, "Somehow the so-called professional work as a police officer means that he must be faithful to his role to serve the nation, serve the people, not to serve ourselves, our party, our family." We are serving the common interest, the national interest and the interests of the people and this is professional.
The prince noted that if the police officer helped to cover up what his relatives were doing illegally, he would not be called a professional police officer. However, Samdech explained that police officers can help protect their relatives legally by finding a lawyer to help defend themselves.
The head of the Ministry of Interior claimed that the word "national police" does not belong to any group, because the national police are involved in building an environment of justice and social justice, so the police leadership must look at this to praise any police officer. That does a good job and punishes any police who commit wrongdoing.
At the same time, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also reminded all provincial police commissioners to prepare water trucks to supply water to people who lack water in the coming dry season. Separately, the provincial police commissioner around the Tonle Sap Lake must investigate and crack down on fishing crimes that occur in their area.
It should be informed that by handing over the additional car to the 25 Capital-Provincial Police Commissioners, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng hopes and believes that this car will facilitate the work at the local level to be more efficient.
Four viruses in the coronavirus that can infect humans can affect our respiratory system in the same way as the flu virus, while most of the symptoms are not severe, both of which can cause pneumonia. Life threatening.
2: How dangerous is the new coronavirus compared to the flu virus?
For example, if 100 out of 100,000 people die, the mortality rate is still very low, similar to the flu virus, but if there are more than 100 deaths out of 6,000 cases, the mortality rate is very low. Quite high, and compared to each other, surely the second situation looks far more dangerous.
However, while most influenza viruses are not serious, the flu virus can cause up to 5 million serious illnesses each year worldwide, according to the World Health Organization (WHO). It is estimated that the flu virus can kill up to 650,000 people a year.
3: Why does the new coronavirus cause more concern than the common flu virus?
While the mortality rates and symptoms of the flu virus and the new coronavirus may be very similar, our ability to fight the two viruses is very different. For the human influenza virus, there is an immune system that can fight it, and scientists have developed a vaccine. For the new coronavirus, it is a mysterious new virus.
4: Is the new coronavirus as contagious as the flu virus?
Influenza viruses can be transmitted from person to person at a distance of up to 1.8 meters, mainly through the air and saliva molecules released through coughing or sneezing. People infected with the H5N1 virus can usually cause high levels of infection to others within three days after they start to get sick, but in some cases it can last more than two weeks.
