Cambodia, Mongolia agree to discuss direct flights
On that occasion, Minister Thong Khon reminded about the diplomatic ties between the two countries, especially Mongolia's support for Cambodia in the difficult phase of nation building after the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
The Minister highlighted the continued development of tourism in accordance with Cambodia's sustainable principles, especially the development of ecotourism and community tourism in accordance with the National Ecotourism Policy 2019-2030 under the inter-ministerial working mechanism that will contribute to improving people's livelihoods. Citizens as well as participate in achieving the 17 United Nations Sustainable Development Goals.
The Mongolian Minister also praised Cambodia's progress, especially the steady growth of tourism, and supported cooperation between the two countries on tourism.
The two sides agreed to draft a memorandum of understanding on tourism cooperation between the two countries, focusing on:
1. Promoting the sharing of experiences and joint development on heritage tourism, cultural tourism, urban and rural tourism, ecotourism, community tourism, religious tourism, etc.
2. Exchanging informational visits and official visits to the private sector, the media and national tourism officials to promote cultural awareness and tourism destinations between the two countries.
3. Discuss the possibility of direct flights between the two countries.
4. Promote mutual support for tourism events by encouraging the private and public sectors to participate in tourism events organized by each country.
Recall that Cambodia and Mongolia first established diplomatic relations in 1960, and after Cambodia went through a dark period, the two countries re-established diplomatic relations in 1979, supporting each other in the international arena.
