(Siem Reap): As part of the conservation of Khmer ancestral temples, Angkor Tiles, a handicraft made in Thmey Village, Kien Sangke Commune, Sot Nikum District, Siem Reap Province, produces ancient bricks for temple restoration. The craft has been making bricks since 1994 and adheres to the techniques provided by temple restoration experts.
Mr. Yin Lim, the owner of Angkor Tile Crafts, started this business in 1989 by recycling the ancient kilns left over from the old society for this business. He said that the production of bricks and tiles in his craft uses pure natural materials and techniques are also traditional.
For the production of bricks to supply the temple repair site in the Angkor resort, Mr. Yin Lim said that started from 1994 and 1995 because his handicrafts have old templates and get the trust of experts to repair the temple. He added that foreign organizations that cooperate with the APSARA Authority have ordered the ancient bricks to repair the Preah Ko temple, and the production is provided with the right techniques and studies from those institutions.
Mr. Saray Kimhoul, Technical Officer of the Department of Temple Preservation in Angkor Park and Preventive Archeology of the APSARA Authority, said that the reason why the APSARA Authority chose Mr. Yin Lim's handicraft to produce bricks to repair the temple was because it respects the technical conditions. Experts offer. He said that originally, before choosing this handicraft, experts went to the site, provided the technology and forbade the production of ancient hills nearby.
In addition, according to Mr. Saray Kim Huol, the ancient bricks used to repair the temple are larger, thicker and finer than ordinary bricks. The order is according to the size and annual plan at each site, and the site that the APSARA Authority to repair, such as the temple of Preah Ko, Prasat Bakong, Prasat Lolay, Prasat Ak Yum, Prasat Bat Chum, etc.
