Ministry of Land Management builds new office building on 3 hectares of land in front of Grand Phnom Penh in Sen Sok district
(Phnom Penh): Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, this morning, January 28, 2020, led the civil servants under the supervision of Krong Pali ceremony to lay the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the new Ministry building. Street 598 or Chea Sophara Street in Anlong Kgan Village, Sangkat Khmuonh, Khan Sen Sok.
The new ministry building is built on an area of 3 hectares with a height of about 5 floors. The building has about 450 parking spaces, a reception hall, a cafeteria for officers, staff and a garden center. The building also has small meeting rooms that can accommodate 300, 150 people, and a large assembly hall that can accommodate up to 1,584 people.
The new ministry building also houses cadastral and administrative archives, technology halls, national laboratories, construction, vocational training classrooms, libraries and sports facilities. The new Ministry building will be built in the Khmer style, decorated with seven floors, with a unique front roof, and a fine design, which the team wants to promote the work of decorating the traditional Khmer architecture, while the floor plan has a space. Indoor garden.
This building is an important part of showing the Khmer identity and the Khmer architectural form in the Techo era, which shows peace, stability, development and revival of this type of construction. This building is the construction of Rhoden for the next generation. The building is claimed to take about a year to build.
