The following is the message from Samdech Mey: Letter to readers: "The hearing in the case of Kem Sokha reflects the strength of Cambodia's national sovereignty!"
Why do I dare to claim a smooth and transparent hearing? There are a number of practical reasons that can be confirmed:
First, the hearing was open to national and international observers, as well as a wide range of journalists, including representatives of foreign embassies, representatives of national and international civil society organizations, representatives of political parties and journalists of all walks of life. All are allowed to enter the courtroom to observe directly, even though the courtroom is small.
Second, there was an assessment by observers, including politicians and civil society supporters of the opposition, that the trial went smoothly, in accordance with the procedures and was acceptable to the Trial Chamber. Full and sufficient time for the accused and the defense of the accused to explain widely.
Thirdly, what is more remarkable is that the lawyer representing the government, Mr. Kitech, even complained with a resentful face to the media that the court restricted the freedom of the plaintiff's lawyer and gave more rights to the party. Defendants, and observers in the courtroom also noted this.
Fourth, the proceedings took place in a Cambodian court in accordance with all procedures in force in Cambodian law on "Peace with Foreigners" committed by the accused Kem Sokha.
Fifth, Mr. Kem Sokha, the accused, also cooperated in participating in this trial, which made the proceedings of the trial proceed in full accordance with the legal procedure without any controversy. The cross-examination of the trial was also lively and lively.
It is true that the trial in the case of "Peace with foreigners" involving the accused Kem Sokha was carried out lively, with each side trying to find evidence to charge and acquit each other, which impressed the observers and observers. Concentrate on this courtroom. We can say that this is a hearing in which the court proceedings are conducted thoroughly and based on national law, which is acceptable and acceptable to all parties.
I believe that in order to build a country for sustainable progress, it is necessary to rely on building the foundations of national sovereignty and territorial integrity as a priority, because if a country's leader can not maintain its national sovereignty, he will not Can not free itself from the influence of foreigners. And indulging in foreign influence without consent is the greatest mistake of any leader or politician.
In this regard, I strongly support the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who has been on the right path through his firm commitment to safeguarding peace at all costs, and especially his strong commitment. Unwavering in maintaining national sovereignty through the slogan "Absolutely do not trade national sovereignty for foreign aid."
All in all, the case of Kem Sokha is a discipline that truly reflects many of the situations for Cambodia, including the protection of peace and the strengthening of national sovereignty and the economy, while the social and justice sectors are under attack. Reinforced gradually.
Overall, Cambodia is now showing self-sufficiency in all areas without relying heavily on foreign aid. But cooperation in partnership with all friendly countries continues on an equal footing and with equal rights. On the contrary, foreign-dependent politics is outdated and no longer acceptable to the people.
