(Battambang): The Royal Government has decided to organize the 6th River Festival in Battambang Province, in which the Minister of Tourism, Mr. Thong Khon, stated that the River Festival must be designated as an event to promote national and international tourism movement and to help strengthen Improve the quality of Battambang tourist destinations further.
This statement was made on the occasion that Minister Thong Khon, together with Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, chaired the first working group meeting to prepare for the River Festival at Battambang Provincial Hall on the morning of January 27, 2020.
The main activities to be implemented are the promotion of culture and tourism resorts, exhibitions showcasing local products, especially the continuous improvement of tourism services in tourism businesses in the province and at resorts.
In addition, there are some other work that the Minister of Tourism has introduced to the working group of civil servants under his supervision, including:
* Decorate the public beauty to be cleaner and greener.
* Arranging art and culture scenes, sports events and entertainment events during the event.
Preparation of booths for exhibitions of small and medium enterprise products, locally made products, especially plastic substitutes.
Liaise with foreign embassies and provinces, alliances with neighboring countries to mobilize participation as in previous ceremonies.
* As Battambang is a province rich in cultural heritage and rich in tourist attractions, Minister Thong Khon urged widespread dissemination.
* Encourage the competition movement, including striving to maintain national and ASEAN victories, which the province has been promoting activities in local tourism communities and tourist resorts, especially riverine tourism communities in Chiwang commune.
* Arranging the venue for the celebration and for organizing events in Battambang city.
* Accelerating the repair of roads and infrastructure in the city and the decoration of the city.
* Inspiring people from all over the province to participate in the river festival, clean up the environment, decorate houses and villages to help receive tourists.
Strengthening sanitation in the city.
* Educate all business establishments not to have excessive price increase, improve service quality, etc.
At the same time, the Minister also urged businesses in the province to reduce the use of plastic, instead of using materials made of rattan, bamboo, paper, etc. to reduce the impact on the environment and promote the implementation of "clean" standards. And green. ”
As the world is concerned about the spread of coronavirus, the number of international tourist movements may decline worldwide, so the Minister has set a goal to organize the river festival to attract tourists. Entertain in large numbers during the festival.
