(Central): An 8-year-old boy and other friends were playing with firecrackers when they were thrown into a gas tank and suddenly died at the scene. The incident happened at around 10 am on January 25, 2020 in Po Krom village, Troeuy Sla commune, Saang district, Kandal province.
According to the police report, the child victim who suffered eye injuries and died immediately was named Phannadaro.
After questioning and analyzing the scene, the police concluded that the victim took a firecracker with a POP sign (firecracker) and dropped it in the fuel tank, rubbing against the bottom of the tank, causing sparks, and the fuel tank had gasoline and ran. A small round, which leads to high combustion, exploded, pierced and hit the upper valve, causing the victim's face and eyes to die.
