(Phnom Penh): General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, has laid out six important plans to ensure better security, order and social security for the people to celebrate the traditional New Year. Chinese, Vietnamese and Korean people.
First, pay attention to collecting information related to the security situation, public order, especially to grasp the tactics of activities that cause insecurity or incitement to cause social unrest.
Second, take measures to maintain security and order in temples, temples, China, Vietnam, Korea, as well as some shrines and resorts with various celebrations, taking care to prevent all kinds of criminal offenses, especially acts of provocation. Gang harassment will require better order.
Third, pay attention to organizing traffic order, prevent congestion and increase the enforcement of road traffic laws, reduce traffic accidents and create conditions for people to visit relatives or go to resorts. With pleasure and safety.
Fourth, to cooperate with local authorities to warn people to be careful of fires, especially candles when offering fire, electric stoves, fire extinguishers, and to prohibit the burning of fireworks or other house noise. At the same time, must mobilize forces and means to be ready to intervene, extinguish and rescue fires that may occur eventually.
Fifth, to strengthen the work at all levels and provide information as soon as possible to resolve the situation that may occur in a timely and effective manner.
Sixth, to summarize the situation and the results of the implementation of security measures during the traditional New Year of the Chinese, Vietnamese and Korean people sent to the headquarters on January 28, 2020.
