(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Embassy in Thailand has come out to confirm that the application for the corpse or other documents demanding compensation and other benefits for Cambodian workers in Thailand in the event of a work accident is free of charge.
The statement from the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand came after a flurry of rumors and rumors on Facebook and in the media that the embassy was offering a fee on paper to claim compensation from relatives. Workers when there are cases of workers dying and occupational accidents.
In a press release issued on January 25, 2020, the Cambodian Embassy in Thailand rejected these allegations and considered them to be completely baseless and fabricated.
The Embassy claims that there is no service charge for applying for a cremation letter and other documents to claim compensation or benefits in the event of a work accident from the Embassy.
In this press release, the Embassy also introduced the faces and identities of 16 embassy officials so that Cambodian workers can contact for various services. The embassy further stated that anyone who claims to provide services other than the 16 officials shown is a fraud.
When someone claimed to be an embassy official, unlike the 16 officials who identified themselves, the embassy asked the workers to immediately report to the embassy at 094 092 5905 and 092 8050561 for legal action.
