Materials brought to mourn on this occasion include: 120 kg of rice, 5 cases of noodles, 5 cases of pure water, 5 cases of drinks, 5 cases of fish and 5 million riels. Telecom Regulator of Cambodia: Receiving a phone number from abroad does not make you lose money from the bank of the phone owner!
Without knowing the real technical causes and risks that affect mobile phone users in Cambodia from this call, some individual website owners and Facebook users have posted and clicked to share messages. Mislead and frighten the public who use mobile services: "Be careful! Very cruel, just raise this number immediately, all the money in the bank is really cruel.
In connection with the posting of the above message is really a false claim and completely deceptive and frightening. The real technical impact and the risk of this call not having an effect will be to lose everything as stated in the meaning of the message posted by the owners of those websites and social media accounts.
According to the research, interpretation and confirmation of all mobile operators in the Kingdom of Cambodia, it is technically shown that in picking up or calling back anonymous numbers, it does not affect the users in Loss of data stored on the phone or funds in the mobile service account or funds stored in their bank account, and what are the real risks:
* First: In case any mobile phone user in Cambodia picks up the anonymous number that Sino called, it does not cause any loss of that user, even the data stored in the phone or the budget stored in the service account. The phone or money in the bank account only causes the anonymous caller to lose his or her international calling charges, as no technology is yet available.
* Second: In the event that a mobile phone user in Cambodia calls back an anonymous number that Sino called, the user will lose money in his mobile service account for international phone calls or calls. Overseas based on the billing rate of the local mobile operator that the user subscribes to at a fixed rate based on the total number of minutes the user has a conversation.
Please note that this problem has already happened once in 2017, and the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia and telecom operators have already confirmed and interpreted once. This phenomenon has calmed down for more than two years and has just resurfaced in recent days.
On the other hand, from the clarification and incident in 2017 until now, there has not been any real case that shows that any Cambodian mobile phone users have been affected by this. No.
However, the Telecommunications Regulator of Cambodia and all telecom operators operating telecommunications services in Cambodia are taking this seriously to monitor the technical aspects to protect the interests of consumers from any eventual impact. No.
