Samdech Techo Agrees to Change the Ministry of Industry and Handicraft to "Science, Technology and Innovation Industry"
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has agreed to change the name of the Ministry of "Industry and Handicraft" to "Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation". The agreement came at the request of Senior Minister Cham Prasidh, the current Minister of Industry and Handicrafts.
According to a letter from the Office of the Council of Ministers to Senior Minister Cham Prasidh on January 24, 2020, it was stated that, in addition to agreeing to change the name of the Ministry, the Royal Government also agreed to amend all existing laws and legal documents. Involvement in the structure and functioning of the renamed ministry.
At the same time, the Royal Government also agreed to establish two new units, the General Department of Science, Technology and Innovation and the National Institute of Science, Technology and Innovation, which have the same level as the General Department. The establishment of these two units does not require the addition of a state framework, i.e. use of existing frameworks that are relevant to the work of science, technology and innovation.
The Royal Government also recommended inter-ministerial meetings with relevant ministries on the preparation of draft laws on the organizational structure, numbers and functions of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation to submit to the Cabinet.
The Royal Government also recommends the opening of key dignitaries, intellectuals with degrees in science and technology, as well as innovative initiatives and technical and scientific officials to serve or transfer volunteers from Ministries involved in science and technology work in the two new units that will be established.
The Royal Government also assigned the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts to prepare a draft law for the National Assembly and the Senate and a draft sub-decree on the organization and functioning of the Ministry of Industry, Science, Technology and Innovation. After preparation, it must be passed through both cabinets.
Please note that the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts was originally called the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy. In the fifth mandate, the Royal Government decided to create a new ministry called the Ministry of Mines and Energy, so the Ministry of Industry, Mines and Energy was renamed the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts.
