Royal Government of Cambodia announces restrictions on traffic laws after death toll rises
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia, through the National Committee for Road Safety, on January 24, 2020, issued a proclamation to tighten the road traffic law after the death rate due to traffic accidents increased in 2019. . This is according to the announcement of the National Road Safety Committee, which was received by Fresh News.
According to the proclamation signed by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Interior and Chairman of the National Road Safety Committee, he expressed his appreciation and appreciation to the authorities at all levels and the people who use the road. Actively involved in the implementation of the law on road traffic.
However, according to the traffic accident situation in 2019, there was a sharp increase in traffic accidents with deaths and injuries and damage to public property and private property compared to 2018.
In fact, the death toll increased by 220 or 12% and the number of injured increased by 1,371 or 29%. These are due to three main factors: vehicle growth (about 37%), infrastructure that is not yet balanced with the growth of vehicles and factors of road users who do not respect and strictly enforce the law on road traffic.
According to the announcement, in order to prevent and reduce the maximum number of road traffic accidents in 2020, follow the recommendation of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, "Today, tomorrow, no traffic accidents" National Committee Road traffic safety, please announce to the public as follows:
1: Ministries, institutions, competent authorities at all levels, companies, factories, enterprises and schools ... must continue and increase the dissemination of education on the law on road traffic to all types of civil servants, the armed forces, staff, workers, students ... to adhere Obedience to the law on road traffic. At the same time, the spirit of respecting the law on land traffic must be incorporated into the internal regulations of its ministries and institutions.
2: Drivers of all types of vehicles must adhere to the 10 points of ethics (excerpted from the Law on Road Traffic), which are as follows:
1: Must know how to drive 2: Must wear a helmet 3: Must wear a seat belt 4: Must be right 5: Must check the technical characteristics of the vehicle 6. Always be careful 7. Do not drive too fast 8: Do not drive under the influence of alcohol 9: Do not drive under the influence of drugs 10: Do not drive in a drowsy state.
3: The National Road Safety Committee would like to declare 2020 as the year of tightening the implementation of the law on road traffic.
