(Phnom Penh): Although the suspension of the preferential tariff system for Cambodian goods in the EU market is not yet known, Cambodia and the European Union are committed to further strengthen cooperation on this trade. Better.
Confirmation of strengthening trade between Cambodia and the European Union was made during a working meeting between Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, and Ms. Carmen Moreno, the newly appointed EU Ambassador to Cambodia. This afternoon, January 23, 2020.
In this meeting, the Minister of Commerce highlighted the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia through reforms for economic integration and the strong will to expand trade partners through the establishment of a free trade agreement.
He added that Cambodia now also has a permanent mission to the World Trade Organization (WTO), which helps promote Cambodia's trade sector.
Mr. Pan Sosak also mentioned that the EU has made a significant contribution to Cambodia's economic development through the provision of trade and education assistance and the implementation of various development projects that have created many job opportunities and helped Improve the lives of Cambodians.
In this meeting, Ms. Carmen Moreno noted the progress of Cambodia and noted some potential related to investment in Cambodia. She also praised the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The European Union is an organization of European countries that aims to accelerate economic integration and strengthen cooperation between member countries. The EU Secretariat is located in Brussels, Belgium. As of 2019, the EU has 28 members.
The European Union is a large market for Cambodian goods with duty-free access to all goods except arms. In the first nine months of 2019, Cambodian goods exported to the European market amounted to nearly 650 million US dollars.
Due to the controversy over the implementation of democracy and human rights in Cambodia, the European Union has been working to remove preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods. In February 2020, the European Commission will decide whether or not to suspend preferential tariffs on Cambodian goods.
