Senior tax official urges tax service agents to use their professional skills properly and effectively in accordance with professional ethics
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Oum Seiha, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Taxation, on January 23, 2020, requested the Tax Service Agency to use its professional skills properly and effectively in accordance with the Code. Professional ethics.
Mr. Oum Seiha's proposal was made on the occasion that he, on behalf of Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, handed over the certificates to the winners who had passed the final examination of the 10th generation "Tax Service Agent". 314th and 12th place, 314 people.
Mr. Oum Seiha also warmly welcomed the presence of the participants in this event and expressed his appreciation to the lecturers of the National School of Taxation who worked hard to teach and transfer knowledge and experience to the participants. Congratulations to the winners who took the time to work hard to study until they get the final result of the "Tax Service Agent".
Tax service agency exams are usually held twice a year for trainees trained at the National School of Taxation and the general public aspiring to become "tax service agents".
So far, the National School of Taxation has organized 12 generations of tax service agency examinations with a total of 1,174 candidates, of which 314 are 10th, 11th and 12th generation finalists. Who came to receive the certificate today for use in applying for a tax service agency license at the General Department of Taxation.
The tax service agency has the following important rights and obligations as stated in Article 9 and Article 10 of Prakas No. 455 MEF.PrK dated 12 April 2013 as follows:
* Service agents with a power of attorney have the right to sign and submit monthly and annual tax returns and pay taxes, provide documents to the tax administration, file complaints, be legally responsible, receive information, update regulations Various, cooperating with the tax administration to provide services, help prevent tax evasion and provide input for the preparation of tax regulations.
* Provide professional and honest tax services, declare and pay taxes correctly, provide correct documents as requested by the tax administration, keep the confidentiality of its clients except tax officials during work, update knowledge Taxes.
At the same time, he also mentioned the achievements of the past tax reform, the challenges, and the continuous reform measures of the General Department of Taxation require the contribution of tax service agencies.
