Ms. Vandin confirmed that this new type of malaria originated in Wuhan, China. So far, several countries have been diagnosed with pneumonia, including Thailand with four cases, Japan with one case, South Korea with one case and the United States with one case. Ever traveled to Wuhan, where there was an outbreak.
"As of this morning, according to the World Health Organization, there are a total of 571 cases in China, of which 17 have been fatal and 95 are in critical condition," the health ministry spokesman said. . "Please note that the deaths from this disease are not caused by pneumonia alone, the study of doctors in the past, the most serious cases that lead to death is that they have other diseases."
"The 17 dead were all from Wuhan, China," she said. According to the World Health Organization, four other countries have been infected: Thailand, Japan, South Korea and the United States, all of which, although they are abroad, It is a case of him having a history of traveling to Wuhan.
Ms. Vandin stated that after the follow-up of the Chinese medical team, it was found that close relatives, suspects, patients and patients with pneumonia, including doctors, were infected with the virus, including 15 doctors who have been treated. Infected from the patient.
The World Health Organization (WHO) claims that some human-to-human transmission of pneumonia is still limited and that there is no conclusive evidence that the disease is highly contagious. This is what Ms. O Vandin said.
"Please note that so far there have been no cases of coronavirus pneumonia in the Kingdom of Cambodia," she said.
She stated that for Cambodia, after receiving information about the first outbreak of pneumonia on December 31, 2019, the Ministry of Health has regularly taken action and issued a series of emergency response measures.
She stated that the Ministry of Health decided to install thermal scanners at the three airports and send health officials to passengers entering Cambodia, especially from Wuhan, China. At the same time, there are separate rooms equipped with medical equipment in Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap, which are also the locations of air travelers to Cambodia.
She added that at the same time, the Ministry of Health advised the 25 provincial health departments to strengthen procedures to monitor the suspected disease of this new type of pneumonia, especially in the provinces where visitors come and go. Additional thermal scanners at some of the main entrances as well. If there is a suspicion of pneumonia with this new virus, health officials will immediately take a blood test for the virus.
Ms. O Vandin stated, "I completely reject that so far no new type of pneumonia has entered Cambodia. "People should only receive information from the Ministry of Health or from a health official."
Meanwhile, Chea Oun, Permanent Secretary of the Secretariat of State for Civil Aviation, confirmed to Fresh News that there was a recent case of blocking passengers from Wuhan, China, to land at Cambodia's airport. That is not true because civil aviation has no policy to close this flight.
