(Phnom Penh): The Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, called on the people as well as the monks and all Buddhists to keep the peace together because there is peace and development of both the empire and the Buddha.
The Governor of Phnom Penh held this morning, January 23, 2020, on the occasion that he and she presided over the inauguration ceremony of the pavilion and achievements at Wat Ang Boeung Chak in Sangkat Kambol, Khan Kampol, Phnom Penh.
Mr. Khim Sunsoda, Governor of Kambol District, confirmed that Ang Boeung Chak Pagoda was built in 1789 and is now more than 200 years old. Before 1970, the pagoda was remarkably prosperous. But during the 1970s and '75s, with the nation at war, the pagoda was abandoned.
From 1975 to 1979, when the country fell into the hands of Pol Pot, the pagoda was used by Pol Pot as a military base. But after 1979, the pagoda was revived and built a series of achievements until today.
