In front of the indigenous "Sre E" community, Mr. Say Sam Al said: "The establishment of a school near the community is to provide opportunities for the children of the community have the opportunity to complete their education. "Self-choice for the future and for the people to know the Khmer language in the direction of more active integration with the whole society and get the fruits of peace and economic growth of our nation."
Along with announcing support for the ecotourism project, the Minister of Environment said that the Royal Government of Cambodia intends to turn the existing conservation area into a natural tourism area in response to the growth of tourism and the needs of the people in Excursions. Currently, domestic tourism has increased significantly due to the well-being of the people due to the growth of the national economy and the peace that pervades the whole country.
Mr. Say Sam Al stated that in addition to the peace and development that Cambodia has now, we help promote and increase the development of local communities. The official expressed hope that with the right policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia, the community will prosper in the future.
Please note that the community of "Sre E" protected area has great potential because the area is rich in forests, rich in wildlife, especially peacocks, which is attractive.
Sre E Primary School, now officially inaugurated, was built with the financial support of the Ministry of Environment and Caritas Cambodia, which is supported by Caritas Germany.
In addition, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to remind parents of students to encourage their children to come to school regularly, should not put travel trips on the day of school.
