(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Public Procurement of the Ministry of Economy and Finance on the morning of January 22, 2020, in collaboration with the Korea Development Institute of the Republic of Korea, organized a workshop on "Feasibility Study on the Initiation of Electronic Public Procurement." (e-Procurement) for managing public procurement in the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The workshop was chaired by Dr. Chhim Sareth, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Public Procurement, and Dr. Lee Sangyoon, Director General of the Public Procurement Agency of the Republic of Korea. Representatives of the Republic of Korea, representatives of development partners, representatives of relevant departments of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and civil servants of the General Department of Public Procurement.
Welcoming Dr. Ly Sang-yeon, he expressed his appreciation for the cooperation of the General Department of Public Procurement of the Ministry of Economy and Finance in organizing this workshop in order to exchange experiences and consult with each other in organizing public procurement. Electronic system (e-Procurement) in the Kingdom of Cambodia to facilitate more efficient and transparent public procurement management.
