(Kampong Cham): Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham Province, on January 22, 2020, ordered all police forces to increase and strengthen the most serious measures to ensure security, public order and safety. Society in the upcoming Chinese, Vietnamese, Korean traditional festivals.
The commissioner's order was issued during a meeting to disseminate the plan for the protection of security, public order and social security during the Chinese, Vietnamese and Korean New Year and the plan received from the meeting at the Ministry of Interior.
The meeting was also attended by the Deputy Commissioner, the Deputy Chief of Planning, the Deputy Chief of the Office, the Chief of the Heritage Police, the Inspector General of the 10 District Police, the Chiefs of the 109 Administrative Police Stations, a total of 351 people.
The security plan of General Neth Savoeun, the National Police Commissioner General, has been launched, including:
* First, pay attention to collecting information related to the security situation, public order, especially to grasp the tactics of activities that cause insecurity or incitement to cause social unrest.
* Second, take measures to protect security and order in temples, temples, China, Vietnam, Korea, as well as some shrines and resorts with various festivals, taking care to prevent all kinds of criminal offenses, especially activities. Caused by gangster aggression and must be organized in a good order.
* Third: Take care to organize traffic order, prevent congestion and increase the enforcement of road traffic laws, reduce traffic accidents and create conditions for people to visit relatives or go to resorts. Go with fun and safety.
* Fourth, to cooperate with local authorities to warn people to be careful of fires, especially candles when offering fire, electric stoves, fire extinguishers, and to prohibit the burning of fireworks or other house noise. At the same time, must mobilize forces and means to be ready to intervene, extinguish and rescue fires that may occur eventually.
* Fifth: Strengthen the work at all levels and provide information as soon as possible to resolve the situation that may occur in a timely and effective manner.
