(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nong Veasna, President of Kol Veasna Investment Company, a well-known local investor in Cambodia, talks about the opportunities and challenges of investing in agriculture and agro-industry in Cambodia.
He said that the agricultural and agro-industrial sector in Cambodia still has many opportunities to attract investors.
The president of Kol Veasna Investment Company also pointed out that the potential for agricultural and agro-industrial investment in Cambodia remains due to the large domestic demand with the supply of international markets.
Regarding the challenges of investing in agriculture and agro-industry, Mr. Veasna thinks that one of the most important factors is the water supply, which is the biggest factor that makes the agricultural sector strong and the second factor: Cambodia's output is still moderate. Yet that is not very competitive compared to neighboring countries.
The investor also said that the cost of Cambodia is high because Cambodia imports such fuel and electricity prices are not lower than neighboring countries, while in the agricultural sector, the use of fertilizers and pesticides is almost 100 percent imported and expensive. One of the biggest costs in the production of agricultural and agro-industrial products.
"If we do not have the ability to produce large quantities of pesticides and fertilizers at affordable prices, the income of the people from agriculture and agro-industry will definitely decrease because "We spend a lot on imports."
In addition, Mr. Veasna said that the shortcoming is that in the field of agriculture and agro-industry, Cambodia is very weak in finding markets because Cambodia is not very good at promoting products that try to produce themselves in the international market. .
