(Kampong Speu): In the closing ceremony of the road traffic skills training course at the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship Police School this morning, January 22, 2020, General Him Yan, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, instructed all traffic police officers to work. With professional ethics and high responsibility, while 2020 is the year to tighten traffic laws.
General Him Yan emphasized to the newly graduated police officers that when returning to work, they must strive to improve security and public order in line with the country's progress, including focusing on traffic order.
"At this point, we must follow the noble recommendation of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, today, tomorrow, not to have traffic accidents more effectively, and Samdech Krala Hom," he said. "In addition, 2020 is the year of law enforcement."
General Him Yan also noted that the core duties of traffic police officers are twofold, namely: to organize order and secondly: to prevent traffic accidents. He strongly hopes that traffic police officers throughout the country will perform their duties with professional ethics and high efficiency to reduce traffic accidents.
Throughout 2019, there were 4,121 traffic accidents nationwide, killing 1,981 people and injuring 6,141, with an average of 5.4 deaths per day. Most of these accidents occurred in Phnom Penh, killing 348 people, followed by Sihanoukville with 149 and Kandal with 143.
It should be informed that according to the report of Lt. Gen. Un On, Deputy Chief of Staff and Director of the Cambodia-Vietnam Friendship National Police School, the current road traffic skills training course has a total of 89 participants from the Capital Police Commission. 23 provinces and departments. Open a 3-month road traffic skills training course from October 28, 2019 to January 22, 2020.
According to Lt. Gen. Un On, so far, the school has opened 19 refresher courses for the National Police Force nationwide, with a total of 2,415 participants, 101 of whom are female.
