Golden FX Link Capital Company Successfully Concludes Workshops Across Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Golden FX Link Capital has successfully completed seminars throughout the provinces of Cambodia, also educating more than a thousand participants on the importance of the derivatives market.
This completion made Golden FX Link one of the first derivatives brokerage firms to make great strides, and more importantly, a historic event in the field of marketing. Derivatives not only in Cambodia but also globally.
Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, who attended the workshops in the provinces, made the process smooth. He also encourages the public to be prepared for investment in the sector, as the sector has individual and collective benefits.
He said that in this sector, there are many benefits, although small, but can provide many benefits such as job opportunities, investment opportunities and other options. There are also foreign investors and national income growth through taxation.
Mr. Sok Dara, Deputy Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, expressed his pleasure to cooperate with Golden FX Link and to achieve this proud result.
He added that educating and meeting the investment needs of the public is the key to getting started in derivatives market investing. As a regulator, SECC is committed to carrying out its mission to further develop with transparency and efficiency.
Golden FX Link Capital is pleased to have made these achievements happen at all provincial seminars, which have achieved the goal of promoting the derivatives market and improving the quality of financial instrument education. Things even in remote provinces.
Chea Sothea, CEO of Golden FX Link, said: “I am thrilled that we have completed this beautiful, fruitful journey, a journey that everyone dreams of. Therefore, I would like to thank (SECC) and the provincial administration for this special guidance and cooperation.
He said that raising awareness of investment regulations and methods could enable thousands of participants to better invest in derivatives products for personal financial growth and to contribute to national economic development.
This also shows that the derivatives market is in a safe position and will continue to push towards a more promising future.
He added that as a connector of the derivatives market of Cambodia, as well as a global derivatives ambassador, we are proud to continue to contribute directly and indirectly to the development of other sectors of Cambodia. We are strengthening our roots on the international stage, especially through various large-scale exhibitions.
With continuing education, it is common for the derivatives market to be safely in the hands of investors and to move towards a more promising future.
"Since 2016, Cambodia's derivatives market has grown steadily and I think things are still going well," he said.
