Man steals new wife, leaves four children with mentally retarded mother
(Kampong Chhnang): A man stole to marry a new wife, leaving four children to live with a mother who is mentally retarded, to the surprise of people living in the same village, especially the news reached The authorities summoned both parties for questioning at the Kampong Tralach District Police Inspectorate on the evening of January 21, 2020.
This incident happened on the morning of January 19, 2020 in Svay Krom village, Ta Ches commune, Kampong Tralach district, Kampong Chhnang province.
At the Kampong Tralach District Inspectorate, a 60-year-old woman named Sar Sothoeun, the mother of Kang Sam Heng, the mother of four children, described her daughter Kang Sam Heng and son-in-law Teng Phan, 40. They married in 2003 in Koh Thom district, Kandal province, and now they have four dependent children (two girls and two boys), the eldest is 16 years old and the youngest is 7 years old.
Later, at the end of 2019, he fell in love with a woman who was a widow with four children living in Svay Krom village, Ta Ches commune together and organized a sacrifice on the morning of January 19, 2020, but the authorities Come and stop at once.
Meanwhile, 33-year-old Soeung Chenda, a widow with four dependent children and second wife, said she divorced her husband two years ago and married another woman. Leaving him four children to raise. He then fell in love with Teng Phan and volunteered to marry her, realizing that Teng Phan's ex-wife was mentally ill, so he decided to marry her.
In front of the police, the newlyweds volunteered to donate 400,000 Riels, which is food allowance to their four children every month, but the mother-in-law demanded a $ 15,000 down payment to Raising grandchildren in exchange for not disturbing the newlyweds.
After hours of debate, the mother-in-law decided to file a lawsuit to seek justice for her daughter and grandchildren, refusing to accept the payment. Shape every month.
Therefore, this couple who do not have a marriage certificate, the authorities only mediate, but in case of mediation, only both parties file a complaint to the court to leave the court to decide at its discretion.
