Minister of Post: Digital Government Policy Framework to be Completed by June 2020
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Tram Iv Tek, Minister of Posts and Telecommunications, confirmed that the digital government policy framework that the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been cooperating with inter-ministerial is scheduled to end in June 2020.
Digital government is the use of electronic means to manage the work system and infrastructure of service delivery in a transparent, convenient, fast and better way to connect with people and businesses, as well as increase the efficiency of government work through the creation and use of digital infrastructure. Integrate digital platform, share digital services, based on the "once created, ubiquitous" mechanism and capacity building program for all stakeholders.
The Minister informed the Japanese Ambassador about the priority work of the Royal Government of Cambodia in preparing to take advantage of the fourth industrial revolution for socio-economic development to achieve the Royal Government's vision.
He said that the main tasks that have been focused on include the development of digital government policy framework, digital economic policy, security protection, information technology, e-commerce, building legal standards, support and so on.
"The Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications has been working with the inter-ministerial government to develop a digital government policy framework, which is scheduled to end in June 2020," he said. "Out of this digital government policy framework, we will develop a master plan and an investment plan."
Regarding the growing e-commerce in Cambodia and the world, the Minister also mentioned the Ministry's efforts to develop the postal transportation system to support the sector, as well as the creation of digital signatures that will play an important role. In e-commerce as well.
