Meanwhile, in the coastal provinces, there may be light rain. Royal Academy of Judicial Professions: The results of the 10th generation of judges of 6 candidates were not irregular
(Phnom Penh): After reviewing the results of 6 candidates who participated in the competition to select the 10th generation of judges, the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions on January 21, 2020 announced that there are no irregularities related No, according to their results, the sum of the scores of the six candidates is 100% accurate.
This announcement was made after the Minister of Justice and Chairman of the Board of the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions on 26 December 2019 assigned a working group composed of the Ministry of Justice and the Royal Academy of Judicial Professions to review related applications. Will be transparent of the results of 6 candidates who did not succeed in the 10th generation student judge competition.
The Royal Academy of Judicial Professions (CIT) has confirmed that the process of selecting the 10th generation of judges is conducted in accordance with the rules and procedures of the competition to ensure accuracy, transparency and trust in principle. Stuck). The whole competition process has been observed by the Anti-Corruption Unit at all stages, including:
1: The issuance and selection of writing disciplines is based on confidentiality principles that ensure that this writing discipline does not leak.
2. The writing exam process is conducted in accordance with the regulations and is strictly and thoroughly inspected to ensure that there is no plagiarism and any entry into the examination room.
3. The retention of the candidate's worksheet is based on the principle that ensures good security, no exchange or additional writing on any worksheet.
4. The process of correcting the candidate's worksheet on the writing subject must ensure that the worksheet is not identified through the decapitation of the worksheet and the coding. In addition to the anonymity principle of this worksheet, the worksheet should be edited by a panel of two different corrections (Double Correction) to ensure the accuracy of the scoring of candidates and in accordance with the principles of independence and discretion of teachers. Each version.
5. The Oral Testing process ensures that each candidate is not identified in the interview room by drawing lots and entering a password for each candidate. At the same time, in order to ensure the accuracy of the evaluation, the jury must be composed of 3 and 5 members in each subject, and the jury must be based on the principles of independence and discretion of each member of the jury. .
6: Quoting, adding and releasing the results must ensure that there is no increase or decrease of any candidate's score by following the principle of quoting and adding points immediately after the exam is completed without delay and Ensure anonymity during the process of extracting and adding points. Meanwhile, the results of the competition will be announced immediately after the summation is completed.
The Royal Academy of Judicial Professions appreciates the efforts of all the candidates who participated in the 10th generation of judges and encourages the candidates who did not win this competition to continue their efforts to participate in the competition. Later exam sessions.
