(Henan-China): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, brought more proud news from the visit of the Ministry of Tourism, Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation of Cambodia in Henan Province, People's Republic of China by the Cambodian side. China has agreed to create more tourism, culture and sports events together.
Mr. Thong Khon said that with the approval of the Royal Government of Cambodia and the support of the Chinese Ministry of Culture and Tourism, the Cambodian-Chinese side has chosen 2019 as the Year of Joint Tourism and Culture, which held its opening ceremony in January 2019 at Phnom Penh will hold a closing ceremony in April 2020 in Shenzhen, Henan Province, a large province with a population of over 100 million and a high standard of living.
In order to attract quality Chinese tourists, the Minister stated that in response to Cambodia's request, the Chinese side supported Cambodia in promoting and promoting Cambodian tourism, as well as strengthening cooperation in line with the spirit of the common destiny of the nation. Cambodia-China:
1: Co-sponsor the closing ceremony of the Cambodia-China Tourism and Culture Year, which will be held in early April 2020.
2. Support the announcement of the opening of the annual Cambodian Culture and Tourism Festival in Henan Province.
3. Facilitate direct flights of Cambodia Angkor Air and other Cambodian airlines to open direct flights between Cambodia and Shenzhen in time for the upcoming closing year of tourism and culture.
4. In the future, the Chinese side will cooperate with the Cambodian Tourism Representative Office in Shenzhen, and the Chinese side will support the cooperation to promote the initiative to establish the Cambodian Consulate General in Shenzhen.
5: Since Henan Province is the origin of the site of Shaolin Pagoda, which has kung fu training (Wushu), the provincial governor promised to help train Cambodian athletes and coaches as well.
