How is the Senate hearing going?
According to the US Constitution, the Senate decides whether or not to remove a US President who has been indicted and removed by the House of Representatives.
The Senate will play the role of October: All 100 senators will have to decide whether or not to remove Donald Trump as president, but in this hearing, the senators will not be allowed to speak and will have to sit and watch. Quiet. However, contrary to ordinary courts, the Senate decides how to conduct a hearing, including allowing additional witnesses.
Donald Trump, on the other hand, needs the support of only 34 senators to escape his dismissal proceedings, and according to Axios, 36 Republican senators from the states where Trump remains. Popularity has already shown a tendency to vote against the procedure to remove Tram, while in the House of Representatives, no Republican lawmaker voted against Donald Trump.
The hearing on the removal of Donald Trump in the Senate will begin at 1:00 pm Tuesday (Washington time) and may end on February 21 or sooner. Depending on the Republican senator. In the event that Donald Trump is elected by the Senate, he will step down immediately and Vice President Mike Pence will replace him.
But that does not mean it can prevent Tram from running for office or running for president again in November 2020. According to the US Constitution, federal government officials, including the ousted president, will not be able to hold office or run for re-election until the Senate holds a separate election by a majority vote. Normal by blocking first.
