With the posting of a picture of Cambodia in a difficult situation after the overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, Samdech Techo, the leader who sacrificed a lot for the cause of peace in Cambodia, said that the peace that the Cambodian people strive for Hardest must be protected to last a long time.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all the blood relatives who sacrificed everything for the cause of peace.
It should be noted that Cambodia was almost reduced to ashes due to the crisis of the fires of war for about 3 decades from the late 1960s to 1998. After 1998 was the time when Cambodia achieved complete peace after a successful political victory overthrew the Khmer Rouge resistance movement.
That peace has given Cambodia the opportunity to develop from a poor country to a low-middle-income country like today. Provide opportunities for Cambodians to build a family economy out of the poverty of the past.
For the past 21 years, Cambodia has made progress in almost all areas of infrastructure, construction, and building. These developments cannot be achieved if peace is not maintained.
General Department of CamControl and an International Organization in Cambodia Hold a Training Course to Strengthen the Promotion of Infant and Child Care Products
(Takeo): The General Department of CamControl in collaboration with Helen Keller International Cambodia on January 21, 2020, held a two-day training course on the implementation of Sub-Decree No. 133 on the promotion and sale of products for infants and children at Takeo CamControl Branch under the chairmanship of Mr. Phan Oun, Deputy Director General of CamControl General Department.
This second training course for Camcontrol branches in 5 provinces: Kandal, Battambang, Kampong Speu, Kampong Chhnang, Phnom Penh after completing the first course in Battambang, which has Camcontrol branches in Pursat, Banteay Meanchey, Oddar Meanchey, Pailin and Siem Reap in October 2019. .
Mr. Phan Oun stated that the purpose is to strengthen knowledge and capacity building on strengthening the implementation and monitoring of Sub-Decree No. 133 and Inter-Ministerial Joint Prakas No. 061 on the promotion of products for infants and children.
He added that governments around the world have adopted these strategies and international codes on the promotion of breast milk substitutes in order to promote, promote and support breastfeeding.
Therefore, in order to protect and promote the health and survival of children, only the promotion of prevention and the need to support breastfeeding and the promotion of infant and child feeding products must be controlled. To be in accordance with Sub-Decree No. 133 and the International Code on the Promotion of Breast Milk Substitute Products.
Mr. Phan Oun hopes that this training will provide inspectors with the knowledge and skills to implement the enforcement of sub-decree 133 and report violations to the executive team of sub-decree 133 to take further action.
