Khieu Kanharith Appoints New Director of Kep Provincial Information Department, Mr. Ros Oudong to Replace Mr. Leav Sunsary
(Kep): Mr. Ros Oudong was announced as the new Director of the New Kep Provincial Information Department this morning, January 21, 2020, replacing Mr. Leav Sunsary, who has retired and was appointed as an advisor to the Ministry of Information.
The inauguration ceremony was held in the presence of Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, and was attended by Mr. Sam Sarim, Chairman of the Provincial Council and Mr. Ken Satha, Governor of Kep Province, as well as members of the Provincial Council, civil servants. , 230 armed forces of the three types.
Mr. Ros Oudong, who has just been appointed, stated that he is committed to leading this institution to be highly effective, have good internal unity, and cooperate with various experts and provincial authorities. He is determined to be loyal to the King and to serve the government as well as the people wholeheartedly.
The provincial governor also instructed the newly appointed department heads to continue their efforts to cooperate with departments and units around the province and local authorities at all levels to contribute to the implementation of the policy of the Royal Government of Cambodia. In particular, the strategic framework related to the information sector to be more effective.
Mr. Khieu Kanharith advised and reminded all the directors of the Department of Information that the information work 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, there is no time off. Therefore, officials and directors of the Department of Information need to work harder and pay more attention.
The minister said that the media has a very important role to play as a bridge to transmit information from the people to the leaders and from the leaders to the people about the social situation at the local level, needs and requests.
