(Takeo): A group of 41 workers at the Wunami Garment Factory in Samrong village, Sophy commune, Bati district, Takeo province fainted this morning, January 21, 2020.
Bati District Governor Phuon Chhim said that some workers fainted this morning, but the exact cause of the fainting is not yet known.
"Forty-one workers fainted this morning without knowing the exact cause, and authorities are questioning the factory to find out why," he said.
According to the district governor, after the incident, the workers who fainted had to be transported to a private clinic from Bati district, which had signed an agreement with the National Social Security Fund, and so far all the workers have been relieved. They are big and some have already left home. A company splitting a plot of land in Andong Snay commune, Kampong Chhnang province, digging illegal land in 2 areas was temporarily stopped by professional officers
(Kampong Chhnang): Flooded land in Area 2, more than 1 hectare in Pahi Village, Andong Snay Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province Fisheries officials temporarily banned the activity on January 20, 2020, having to wait for the owner of the company to show a permit to show skills before continuing to act.
After failing to show the letter, the district chief told the chief to suspend the excavation activities in the two areas first, and the permit must be presented to the Fisheries Administration District at the office tomorrow, but without a permit to dig the land. This means that the company will not have to dig this land again, but if they continue to violate it, the fisheries authorities will carry out the procedure by seizing all the machinery and trucks to build a legal case.
Regarding the excavation of fish ponds in these two areas, according to the law, the size of the pond is 50 square meters, the right to decide at the provincial level, beyond this size, the right to decide is the Department of Fisheries Administration and the Ministry of Agriculture.
