(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, on January 21, 2020, confirmed that on February 14 and 15, 2020, the Ministry of Environment will organize a tent program. Environment and tree planting in Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary.
According to the plan, the program will involve local authorities, communities of protected areas living in and around Prey Lang, as well as a total of 500 young men and women of the Ministry of Environment to increase love and participation in the protection of natural resources. Biodiversity and ecosystems in Cambodia in general and especially in Prey Lang.
He said, "The purpose of this environmental tent and tree planting ceremony is to cultivate a love of natural resources, biodiversity and ecosystems among the Cambodian people, especially the youth, and to encourage more active participation in "Protecting and conserving the natural resources we have."
He said that due to the factors of complete peace and development, Cambodia has had sufficient opportunities to consider the protection and conservation of natural resources, biodiversity, environmental protection and sustainable development to build a Cambodian society with a clean, resourceful environment. Nature is protected and comfortable for people to live, and environmental quality and environmental sustainability are guaranteed.
It should be noted that Prey Lang was established by the Royal Government as a Prey Lang Wildlife Sanctuary in 2016 under the management and conservation authority of the Ministry of Environment with a total area of over 430,000 hectares in four provinces: Stung Treng, Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom. And Kratie Province.
In 2019, the Ministry of Environment recognized 19 protected area communities that have the legal right to participate in activities to protect and conserve natural resources in this important wildlife sanctuary.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra emphasized that the official recognition of the protected area community by the Ministry of Environment was made in order to increase the participation in the management and sustainable use of natural resources, as well as to contribute to improving the livelihood of local communities in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government. Government of Cambodia.
"The establishment of this protected area community is a democratization of sharing control and responsibility to the local community on the management of the protected area, as well as to allow the community the right to "Use and enjoy natural resources in accordance with the law on protected areas."
During the Chinese-Vietnamese New Year, CamControl officers confiscated about 140 kilos of defective goods at Thmor Koul market and stored them ready to be burned.
(Battambang): On January 21, 2020, Battambang Provincial CamControl officers, in cooperation with the officials of the Department of Commerce and local authorities, inspected the products on display to find out-of-date goods and food. 140 kilograms of banned goods found during banned Chinese-Vietnamese New Year
Thmor Koul market in Thmor Koul district and stored at the branch office to be destroyed later.
Mr. Hak Sokrin stated that in order to take into account the health of the people living daily during the upcoming Chinese-Vietnamese New Year, our professional officers have strengthened and inspected regularly and continuously in the inspection. In the actual market, today our joint team found 140 kilograms of defective goods to be stored at the branch waiting to be burned.
He called on the people, sellers and consumers to help prevent the influx or placement of defective goods and mix chemicals banned from the market to avoid harm to our health.
Mr. Sok Touch has been appointed President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia with the rank of Minister.
(Phnom Penh): His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, has issued a Royal Decree appointing and appointing Dr. Sok Touch as President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia with the rank of Minister.
The new Royal Decree appointing Dr. Sok Touch as President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia also raises questions. I wonder why Dr. Sok Touch is currently the President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, why was he re-appointed by the King?
Mr. Kin Phea, President of the Cambodian Institute of International Relations of the Royal Academy of Cambodia, told Fresh News that the re-appointment decree was nothing new, just to comply with the Royal Decree on the Establishment of the Royal Academy of Cambodia into a Public Administration Institution. December 26, 2019 ago.
Pursuant to Article 18 of Royal Decree No. NS / RKOT / 1219/1962 dated 26 December 2019 on the Establishment of the Royal Academy of Cambodia as a Public Institution of Public Administration, the position of President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia shall be re-appointed and this appointment Must be done no later than one month after the entry into force of the above Royal Decree.
Please note that the Royal Academy of Cambodia officially became a public administrative institution on December 26, 2019. The Royal Academy of Cambodia (PRC) is a public administrative institution under the technical guardianship of the Office of the Council of Ministers and under the financial guardianship of the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
According to the new Royal Decree, the Royal Academy of Cambodia (CPC) has a mission to lead, manage, develop, study, research, science, technology, technology, training and develop the nation's senior intellectual resources. The Royal Academy of Cambodia has the following responsibilities:
- Manage and expand scientific research in all fields
- Collaborate on research with ministries, institutions, national and international organizations, as well as development partners with the same objectives.
- Organize scientific forums in all fields to provide input to contribute to the development of the country
- Training to develop human resources in all fields
- Collect, compile, publish and keep documents, research works and discoveries
Concentrate national and international intellectual forces to promote national development
- Proposing medals or scientific honors to outstanding national and international dignitaries
Preserve and develop the sustainable use of the Khmer language and script and maintain the Khmer national identity.
- Research, conservation and development of natural and cultural resources
Contribute and cooperate in the protection of intellectual property in all fields of science
- Review and evaluate senior scientific research works
Perform other duties assigned by the Office of the Council of Ministers and the Royal Government.
