Two Children Killed and One Survived in a Boat Flood in Ba Phnom District, Prey Veng Province
(Prey Veng): A young man and a boy were killed when they were crossing a river when the boat sank in the middle of the river.
The incident happened at 2:10 pm on January 20, 2020 in a small river in Thmey village, Sdao Kong commune, Ba Phnom district, Prey Veng province.
The two victims are: Bo Reaksmey, male, 12 years old, residing in the village where the incident took place, and Seng Bun Kheang, male, 14 years old, residing in Phnom Penh.
According to police sources, the victims were friends and before the incident, they, along with another friend, Ponlok Meng, a 15-year-old male resident of Phnom Penh, took a boat from The north bank of the small river crosses to the south bank to visit there.
However, when they reached the middle of the river, their boat sank, causing the two victims, who could not swim, drowned and died. The victim, Ponlok Meng, was able to swim. Trying to swim to the shore, he survived the panic and ran to call the locals to help his friend who drowned immediately.
According to the authorities, however, the locals came to find out that they were dead and just brought the bodies to be handed over to relatives to prepare for the traditional ceremony. Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: The air quality situation in Cambodia is still good
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, stated that according to the results of the air quality monitoring of the Ministry of Environment on January 21, 2020, the air quality situation in Cambodia is better. Same.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra continued that the Ministry of Environment would like to thank all environmental officials and relevant authorities, especially the sub-national authorities, the Department of Environment and the people who participated in implementing some measures at the call of the Ministry of Environment.
According to the Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment, the increase in PM2.5 inert particles in the air is not still present in Cambodia, but this trend is increasing in other countries in the region due to the dry climate of the Mekong sub-region. Exhausted.
