In order to prevent and reduce the rate of traffic accidents, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng sees that restricting the implementation of the road traffic law is an important measure that all relevant law enforcement officials need to pay more attention to. Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also saw that the current level of fines seemed to be loose, leading to less fear of traffic offenders.
In the meeting to summarize the results of road traffic safety work in 2019 and work direction in 2020 this morning, Tuesday, January 21, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng wants to amend the Law on Road Traffic or amend the sub-decree to Increase the fines for driving offenders more severely than at present, leading to the revocation of drunk driving licenses and drug addicts to be banned from driving for life.
Samdech Krala Hom emphasized that this practice is not only for car drivers, but also for motorcyclists. Samdech Krala Hom advised to start reviewing the sub-decree on this fine from tomorrow.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also stated that the implementation of strict legal measures is not to want the money of the people as the driver, but as a measure to protect the lives of the people.
Samdech Krala Hom reminded the law enforcement authorities that 2020 must be the year of law enforcement, which can no longer be ignored, as the rate of traffic accidents has reached the emergency level.
It should be noted that throughout 2019, there were 4,121 traffic accidents nationwide, killing 1,981 people and injuring 6,141 people. On average, there are 5.4 deaths per day. Most of these accidents occurred in Phnom Penh, killing 348 people, followed by Sihanoukville with 149 and Kandal with 143.
Most of the fatalities were motorcyclists, who accounted for 1,542 out of a total of 1,981 fatalities, accounting for 78 percent. Of those, 1,186 were not wearing helmets, accounting for 77 percent.
In 2019, a truck carrying workers was involved in 14 traffic accidents, killing five people and injuring 334 others.
