(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training on January 21, 2020, held a meeting to review the implementation of Prakas No. 086 and No. 194 and Guideline 008 organized by the Tripartite Commission (TCC) under the chairmanship. Dr. Huy Hansong, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and Chairman of TCC.
The meeting was attended by representatives from the Royal Government, including the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the Ministry of Tourism, the Anti-Drug Institution, the AIDS Party, employers' representatives, union representatives and partner organizations.
Dr. Leng Tong, Advisor to the Ministry and Director of the Department of Labor Medicine, stated that the purpose of the meeting was to review the results of the implementation of the regulations of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, the plan to continue the mechanism of response to HIV and drugs and challenges.
Dr. Veng Yanath, Representative of the National AIDS Authority, spoke about the progress of the implementation of the 5th National Strategic Plan on HIV / AIDS in order to achieve the goal of 95 95 95 by 2025-2030, which Cambodia currently has more than 7 Tens of thousands of people came to receive antiretroviral drugs, but only about 60,000.
On that occasion, Dr. Huy Hansong, Secretary of State, also thanked all stakeholders of the Tripartite Coordinating Committee for HIV / AIDS in the workplace for their cooperation and continued to work smoothly. The Commission's plan to achieve our goal of drug and AIDS prevention in the workplace.
