The General Department of Taxation and the Ministry of Land Management are working together to solve the problem of congestion in the systematic registration of land for title deeds with zero tax stamp.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, and Mr. Sor Sovann, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, chaired a meeting on January 20, 2020 to discuss the resolution of congestion documents. In land registration work, there is a system for title deeds that are stamped with zero tax.
The meeting was also attended by the Deputy Director General of the Central Department, all provincial tax branches and relevant professional officers of the General Department of Taxation, as well as the presence of the Director General of the General Department of Cadastral and Geography, Department of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. And all provincial cadastre.
The meeting aims to solve congestion and inactivity to strengthen the efficiency of providing public services to the people to promote the issuance of title deeds to the people.
In the past, it has been suggested that there is a blockage of documents in the tax administration in the case of zero tax stamp on the acquisition of title deeds obtained from the gift of parents, grandparents, children, siblings through gift or succession through Letter No. 3514 Don / SDP dated October 28, 2019 and in the press release of the meeting to review the work results in 2019 and the work direction for 2020 dated December 25, 2019.
After some practical discussions, after reviewing, it was found that the jammed documents had not been sent to the tax administration and there were about 130,000 documents.
It should be noted that the strategy of the Royal Government of Cambodia is to launch a systematic land registration program for Phnom Penh and other provinces in Cambodia, at the same time to implement the Royal Government's revenue collection strategy. The government, too.
Under the guidance of His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance, and His Excellency the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, and General Department of Cadastral and Geography of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction. Discuss and prepare the following settlement mechanisms:
* The two institutions must work together to solve the case of congestion at the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral by setting within one month by sending officials from both institutions to campaign for the congestion in the province. And continue to implement coping mechanisms like the early rains.
* Both institutions will prepare a joint report to report to the leadership of the two ministries.
