Tbong Khmum CamControl Officers Detected and Confiscated 70 Cans of Deteriorated Orange Juice, 10kg of Assorted Cake and 9kg of Dried Fish with Chemicals from Chicken Market in Ponhea Krek District
(Tbong Khmum): In order to strengthen the quality of goods and food safety, Mr. Meas Mora, President of Camcontrol Branch, Tbong Khmum Province, on January 20, 2020, led the CamControl officials in cooperation with the Provincial Department of Commerce to continue to inspect the quality of goods, promote the selection and Keep food safe for people and traders at Chi Moan Market in Ponhea Krek District, Tbong Khmum Province.
Mr. Meas Mora stated that during that activity, CamControl officers inspected the quality and safety of the food that is being displayed for sale, such as inspecting the date on the packaging and testing the dried trout, swollen fish, prahok, beans, shrimp and squid. Dry.
As a result of the inspection, they found and immediately confiscated some expired and damaged goods, including 70 cans of orange juice, 10 kg of assorted cakes and dried fish containing 9 kg of boracic chemicals to be destroyed. . 24 samples of products, including 14 samples of vegetables and 10 samples of fruits were sent to CamControl for further analysis of pesticide residues.
Kampong Thom Provincial Governor Calls on All Relevant Institutions to Disseminate the Tricks of Perpetrators and Deceptive Traffickers to Localities and Schools
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sok Lou, Governor of Kampong Thom Province, calls on all relevant institutions to help disseminate the tricks of the perpetrators to deceive and deceive human trafficking to the local level and schools.
He said this at the celebration of the 13th National Day Against Human Trafficking on December 12, 2019 on the morning of January 20, 2020 at Kampong Thom Provincial Hall, with the participation of heads of units around the province, government officials and Nearly 500 students.
Mr. Sok Lou, as the Chairman of the Anti-Human Trafficking Committee of the NCDD, stated that human trafficking is a crime in which perpetrators use all kinds of tricks to exploit and abuse people. Irrespective of the suffering and life of the people, which creates concern for the Royal Government, the authorities at all levels and the people everywhere.
He added that the Royal Government of Cambodia still considers the fight against human trafficking as one of the priorities for promoting social security and safety, as well as promoting respect for human rights and dignity. Images of human trafficking include not only trafficking or exploitation of labor and sex, but also organ trafficking and smuggling or cross-border infant trafficking.
"We must not tolerate them. We must work hard to find targets to carry out legal sentencing. We must consider human trafficking as a matter for all of us, especially parents. To their children.
At the same time, Mr. Sok Lou thanked all law enforcement forces and relevant professional officers who worked together to solve the problem without fear of exhaustion, struggling to fight against the actions of criminals in line with the direction of the policy. Of the Royal Government for the cause of security and safety of the people and the nation.
