(Phnom Penh): The Boeung Keng Kang Criminal Police of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission on the afternoon of January 20, 2020, sent a young American Intercontinental School student to court in a case of violence that caused the death of the same student in Boeung Keng Kang District. This was confirmed by an official from the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to Fresh News Unit.
According to the official, the suspect, a 15-year-old male student of the American Intercontinental School (AIS), was sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to be handed over to the prosecutor's office for investigation and indictment. According to the law related to the case of violence that caused the death of the same student.
Two American Intercontinental students fought and died on the way to the hospital. This incident happened on the evening of January 18, 2020 at the intersection of Street 430, Village 2, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, Phnom Penh.
According to the police report, prior to the incident, the victim and a friend rode a motorcycle from the American Intercontinental School to meet the suspect on Street 402, Sangkat Tumnup Teuk, Khan Boeung Keng Kang, having an appointment with the suspect. Because they have a conflict with each other, the story is called Ameng.
Police said that after the meeting, the suspect hit the victim with one hand in the middle of the chest, causing the victim to fall off the motorcycle, and immediately the suspect fled on a Today motorcycle. The victim was then taken by friends to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, but doctors pronounced him dead.
Ministry of Education issues press release to strengthen and improve discipline, internal regulations and moral education in educational institutions
1: School Management Committee: School Support Committee, school principals and teachers must disseminate and strengthen the most thorough implementation of the "Guidelines dated 20 January 2020 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports on strengthening Implement internal regulations in public and private schools. ”In particular, strengthen the mechanism of the disciplinary council in each institution.
According to the same press release, the Ministry of Education also requested the competent authorities at all levels to continue to strengthen the implementation of the law, the implementation of safe village-commune policy to maintain public order, security and safety for all communities and educational institutions. Across the Kingdom of Cambodia.
The following is a press release from the Ministry of Education:
At the same time, the Ministry observes that a small number of educational institutions are not yet fully implemented, especially the management of students on campus without disseminating and implementing the internal regulations of educational institutions widely and responsibly. Still, violence and inactivity have occurred.
The seven main points raised by the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports include:
* First, the management of educational institutions must strengthen the implementation of the duties of teachers in charge of teachers, teachers in the subject to guide students to implement internal regulations in every class and strengthen the role of Youth Council, Disciplinary Council, Education Council to There are measures to prevent and address any abnormalities of students on campus.
* Second, the management of the educational institution must meet to introduce the duties of the students, such as: discipline, ethics, ethics, dress, grooming, hygiene, discipline level, applying for leave, promotion, promotion and participation in various activities inside and outside. Institution for students every time saluting the flag or before starting teaching in accordance with internal regulations.
* Third: The management of the educational institution must communicate and cooperate closely with the parents, guardians of the community to provide information related to abnormal phenomena committed by students in order to cooperate, educate, guide and improve in a timely manner.
* Fourth: The management of educational institutions must work closely with the competent institutions such as: National Police, Gendarmerie, Local Authorities to provide information in case of gangs, violence, aggression, riots by students or gangs in Near or on campus.
* Fifth, the Office of Education, Youth and Sports of the Municipal, District and Khan Administration shall set the agenda on the effectiveness of the implementation of the internal regulations, guidelines and regulations related to the strengthening of discipline in every monthly meeting with the management of public and private educational institutions.
* 6th: The Department of Education, Youth and Sports of the Capital and Provinces shall disseminate, guide and monitor the implementation of the law, especially the internal regulations of the educational institution by setting the agenda for every monthly meeting with the Office of Education, Youth and Sports of the Municipality, District and Khan. And private under the supervision.
* Seventh: Learners must implement the internal rules, guidelines and regulations issued. In the event that a student commits a misdemeanor, the student shall be punished in accordance with the applicable internal regulations. In particular, criminal offenses inside and outside the campus, the student must be responsible before the law and under the authority of the authorities in the hierarchy.
