General Nem Sovath Calls on Officers to Keep Peace Under Win-Win Politics
(Phnom Penh): General Nem Savuth, Director General of the General Department of International Relations of the Ministry of National Defense and Chairman of the Win-Win Monument Construction Team, reiterated his call for all subordinates to work together to maintain peace. Existing today, while the construction of this win-win monument is also a testament to Cambodia's peace.
Speaking at the program to summarize the work results for 2019 and the direction of work to continue on 2020 on January 20, 2020 at the construction site of the Victory Monument, General Nem Sovath said that all working groups clearly understand And about the meaning of the construction of a win-win monument, and the fact that we built this monument because our country has peace and continuous development. Therefore, we must all be grateful for this peace.
At the same time, the general also told the officials that the peaceful country is due to the leadership of the current government, as well as the good international relations of Cambodia as a whole.
Please note that the construction of this win-win monument has 5 main goals, such as:
First, to remind the importance of peace, achievements and processes that have led to peace through win-win policies and national unity. Demonstrates the harmonization of Cambodian society through religion, epoch, history and achievements.
Second, respect and write down the dedication, leadership and creativity of Cambodia's leading guides and operators who have brought national reconciliation and an end to the bloodless civil war that has brought prosperity and peace to Cambodia.
Third, establish a center that provides learning for people of all generations to continue to study and gain an understanding of the true history of Cambodia and continue to implement Techo Sen's win-win policy and values of integration in The process of building, leading and developing the country in the future.
Fourth, to show the values of Khmer culture, civilization and architects in the style of art, symbols, symbols, sculptures and other infrastructure for people of all generations to understand.
And 5: Establish a tourist destination in Phnom Penh that is characterized by tourism, history, culture, as well as a destination for research visits.
