Senior official of the Cambodian National Council for Youth Development: Educating a child for knowledge is not just about schooling
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Sroy Socheat, Director General of the General Department of Youth, Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Secretary General of the Secretariat of the National Council for Youth Development of Cambodia, said that educating a child to have knowledge is not just education in In that school, parents should also be involved.
This statement was made on the occasion of Ms. Sroy Socheat presiding over the awarding ceremony for outstanding staff-leaders, certificates of study and scholarships for outstanding students of 2019 of ASEAN International School, which was organized At the National Institute of Education on January 19, 2020.
During the ceremony, Ms. Sroy Socheat said that there are many proverbs related to education, but there are some proverbs related to investing in education, it is said that if you want to do business, you may not open a school. No, because the job of opening a school is not just for personal gain.
The director general of the General Department of Youth of the Ministry of Education also pointed out that a proverb says that if someone opens the door to school, he closes the door of ignorance, so parents's investment in their children for education. This is a very good investment, a very wise investment and a long-term investment.
Ms. Sroy Socheat said that under the provision of education of public schools under the direct leadership of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, because there is not enough for all students, so the participation of private schools, she also called for For parents, do not think only of private schools or public schools.
She said that she takes care of the students, but when there is a school program or inviting parents to listen to the results or progress of their children, parents always say that my teacher is busy, I am busy to do business. Make money for teachers, pay school fees for me to come and listen, what if I bring my children to school, I want teachers to look after my children, if I see the same, why should I bring them to school?
Ms. Sroy Socheat stated that this is a very narrow thinking, an English proverb said, "To develop a child to have a future" requires the participation of all levels, teachers, parents and those around them. Make the child grow well, so please all parents pay attention to this work as much as possible.
In addition, Ms. Sroy Socheat added that the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has paid close attention to an education reform that is specific and provides quality to all students. "Educating a child to be educated is not just about schooling," she said.
