Mr. Ky Tech: Journalists who need Samdech Techo's volunteer lawyer to defend themselves must request through the Ministry of Information (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Ky Tech, President of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's volunteer lawyer group Work according to professional ethics, but be sued. If you need a lawyer to volunteer for Samdech Techo to help defend, you must ask through the Ministry of Information before reaching the group of lawyers.
Mr. Ky Tech made this statement on the morning of January 20, 2020, when he led a group of Samdech Techo volunteer lawyers to meet with Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information, to plan the defense process for working journalists. According to professional ethics.
According to the leader of the Samdech Techo Volunteer Lawyers Group, the journalists who have the right to defend themselves are journalists who are properly registered and recognized by the Ministry of Information. Journalists who live on Facebook and are not legally recognized are not eligible for this right.
"But just now, the Minister also mentioned that some people applied to be journalists, but they themselves did not register, did not get the right to be journalists, just had a phone call to pretend to be journalists," he said. They are not called journalists, they are called Facebook players. So our service is not provided to all of them.
During the meeting, Mr. Khieu Kanharith stated that the provision of Samdech Techo's volunteer lawyer to defend such journalists is not to encourage journalists to insult them, but only to professional journalists. . The Minister of Information said that in the near future, the Ministry will organize a workshop to raise awareness about the provision of services by Samdech Techo volunteer lawyers.
