(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, this morning, January 20, 2020, presided over the opening ceremony of the training course for new officers in 2019 with the participation of Mr. Secretary General, His Excellency Delegate, Chairman, Deputy Director of the Department and civil servants under the supervision of the Ministry of Agriculture.
According to the report of Mr. Ty Channa, Director of the Department of Personnel and Human Resource Development, for 2019, the Ministry has received 120 officers who have just passed the new framework exam, divided into specialized units and departments.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Ty Channa also briefed the participants on the results achieved in 2019, the challenges and the direction of implementation in 2020 for this department.
Minister Veng Sakhon held talks with the new officers, praising and evaluating the victories they have just received due to the transparent and fair examination on October 27, 2019.
The minister continued that this is another new page for the journey of life that will become a public official, and the fruits that you get this is a bridge to cross the lifeline from students to public officials who are truly professional. Clear and able to build a future with honor and dignity as a good official, good citizen in the future society.
At the same time, Minister Veng Sakhon also told the children that in order to develop the agricultural sector, it is necessary to have human resources with knowledge and skills, including high professional ethics. Therefore, the presence of the 120 children will share the strength, knowledge and spirit to serve their own units that have the potential to accelerate the process of agricultural development.
Therefore, in order to become a full-fledged human resource with potential and to become the successor of bamboo in the near future, Minister Veng Sakhon has given some recommendations to the officials of this new framework, which are as follows:
Taking this opportunity, Minister Veng Sakhon further advised the specialized units under the Ministry to pay attention, consider and implement more actively and effectively on the following points:
First, all units under the Ministry must strengthen and improve the process of human resource management and development in order to turn human resources in the public sector to be more professional, clear and efficient in their work.
Second, continue to make effective reforms by setting out a strategic framework, action plan, and setting up a comprehensive and consistent interconnected monitoring system. Continue to cooperate well with local authorities, relevant professional institutions at all levels and agricultural development partners.
Third, to strengthen the high internal unity while performing the duties, as well as assign the work according to the ability and prevent all our internal divisive activities, as well as the management of civil servants with justice. Avoid internal divisions and do not take advantage of individuals. Always remember the 11 recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which always reminds that the nation is a good official, what to do?
Fourth, to increase the attention and high responsibility in promoting the ranks and medals to civil servants under his supervision. At the same time, all units must strive to encourage civil servants who have worked hard to continue their studies.
Fifth, the heads of all units must pay attention and monitor all the circular letters or letters of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries that have been issued for implementation, especially all units, every year to prepare a training plan for human resources and Make statistics report of civil servants attending training courses at home and abroad.
Please be informed that this 4-day training course will cover important topics and present to the new civil servants about:
* Role and Mission of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries * Leadership and Management Structure of the Ministry * Duties and Responsibilities of Each Unit under the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries * Rights, Duties and Administrative Hierarchy * Laws and Regulations Other things that civil servants must understand and strictly respect.
