Drink responsibly! Sorry! Baby Elephant Found in Phnom Prech Forest Dies
(Mondulkiri): A baby elephant, about 1 week old, was found lying on the ground in Prey Sakrit, Mondulkiri province, died at 3 am on January 20, 2020 due to But serious conditions can not be saved. This is according to the announcement of the Department of Environment of Mondulkiri Province.
Please be reminded that the Phnom Prech Wildlife Sanctuary rangers spotted the baby elephant on the morning of January 17, 2020 in a state of exhaustion and disease in the limbs, abdomen and mouth under the environment and Hot weather.
The Ministry of Environment said that the rescue team immediately intervened with the participation of partner organizations that can make this baby elephant stand up and walk. From the night of January 17-18-19, 2020, the team worked hard to rescue by continuing the most careful care to enable this baby elephant to recover quickly from the disease.
Unfortunately, on the night of January 19, 2020, this baby elephant began to become tired, unable to move, no longer receive food and water until 3 am on January 20, 2020, the condition and symptoms of the disease. The baby elephant died tragically.
The Mondulkiri Provincial Department of Environment and the rescue team have expressed their condolences for the loss of one of the baby elephants. According to experts, the reason why the mother and herd of the baby elephant decided to leave the baby elephant because the condition and development of the baby elephant disease is very serious and can not be cured. Yes.
Seven drunken men stabbing each other in Monivong Bokor National Park, killing one, will be sent to court this evening
The General Commissioner confirmed that this evening, the seven perpetrators will be sent to court on the evening of January 20, 2020 for legal action.
The incident happened on the night of January 18, 2020 at 20:40 in the waterfall restaurant on Monivong Bokor National Park in Rolous village, Boeung Touk commune, Teuk Chhou district, Kampot province.
According to the commissioner, a group of suspects drank and quarreled until they stabbed the victim, Thy Sothea, a 31-year-old male resident of Neang Kongheng village, Sambo Meas commune, Kampong Cham city, Kampong Cham province, with two serious injuries. The victim died on the way to the rescue.
After the incident at 23:00, the police detained a group of 7 suspects.
