Taking this opportunity, the Governor also expressed his deep gratitude to the Government and people of Japan, who have always provided substantial assistance in contributing to the rehabilitation and development of Cambodia from the beginning to the present.
It should be noted that the gravel road, which is a grant from the Royal Government and the people of Japan through the Small-Scale Human Security Project (Kusanoni) has opened a repair site is now 6,300 meters long and 5 meters wide. 7 places and some traffic equipment with a population of 4 villages: O Suosdey village, Otavao village, Koun Phnom village and Pang Rolim village equal to 6,972 people.
