Phnom Penh Governor Cancels "Chicken Wings" Card by January 22 and Continues to Distribute Real Estate Identity Certificates to Land Owners in Sangkat Tuol Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo
(Phnom Penh): An announcement from Phnom Penh Governor Khuong Sreng, obtained by Fresh News on January 19, 2020, indicates that the Phnom Penh Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs will issue a certificate identifying real estate owners. (Title) to the owner of the plot of land located in the judgment area of Bak Touk village, Sangkat Toul Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo from January 17, 2020 onwards.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng's announcement, land use rights (chicken wings) or immovable property titles issued by the Cadastral Administration in the judgment area will expire. From the date of issuance of the above real estate owner identification certificate.
This announcement was made with reference to Sub-Decree No. 122 dated 9 June 2016 on the revision of Article 6, Article 7 and Article 11 of Sub-Decree No. 46 dated 31 May 2002 on Procedures Of the construction of cadastral maps and land registers under the systematic process of land registration.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration would like to appeal to the creditors who have received collateral or pledged the relevant plots of land in the judgment area, please bring the title deeds to the Cadastral Administration for regulation to guarantee your money.
As mentioned above, Phnom Penh Capital Administration would like to ask the owners of plots of land with land use rights or immovable property titles in the past to hand over the land to the Cadastral Administration Officer in Bak Touk Village, Sangkat Toul Sangke I, Khan Russey Keo. From January 17 to 22, 2020 is mandatory.
