(Phnom Penh): On January 19, 2020, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior, led a delegation of the Ministry of Interior to return home to Cambodia after a three-day visit from January 17-19, 2020 at the invitation of Lieutenant General Tolem, Minister of Police of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
According to the posting on Samdech Krala Hom's Facebook page, on the occasion of his visit to the Socialist Republic of Vietnam, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng led a senior official of the Ministry of Interior of Cambodia to hold a meeting to evaluate the results of cooperation in 2019. And signed the 2020 Cooperation Plan with the Police Ministry counterpart of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam led by Lt. Gen. To Lam.
Meanwhile, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng and Lt. Gen. Tolim also praised and appreciated the cooperation between the police forces in the border provinces of the two countries, which have closely cooperated and maintained a secure environment. Along the border line well contributes to creating favorable conditions for the livelihood of the people of the two countries.
The two sides also exchanged greetings from His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of Cambodia, Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President. Minister to Mr. Nguyen Hu Chong, President of the National Assembly, Mrs. Nguyen Thi Kim Ngin, President of the National Assembly and Mr. Nguyen Sun Hoc, Prime Minister of Vietnam.
On that occasion, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng also congratulated Vietnam on the opportunity to assume the rotating chairmanship of ASEAN in 2020 and the election of a non-permanent member of the UN Security Council. In the mandate 2020-2021.
Vietnam's Minister of Police To Lam also congratulated Cambodia on hosting the 13th Asia-Europe Meeting in 2020. Both sides are committed to supporting each other in all possible ways to make these historic events a success as planned.
During the visit, the Government and the Ministry of Police of the Socialist Republic of Vietnam awarded medals to the Ministry of Interior of the Kingdom of Cambodia, as well as leaders and officials of relevant agencies who have made significant contributions to good cooperation between the two countries. Both Ministries in the cause of maintaining security for the nation, motherland and people.
(Svay Rieng): Mr. Men Vibol, Governor of Svay Rieng Province, this morning, January 19, 2020, led a delegation from Svay Rieng Province to participate in the celebration of the Vietnamese New Year in Tay Ninh Province of the Socialist Republic. Vietnam.
Speaking on that occasion, the Governor of Svay Rieng Province noted the progress of cooperation resulting from the contribution of the authorities and stakeholders of Svay Rieng-Tai Ninh Province.
He believes that in the new year 2020, this relationship and cooperation will be doubled for the peace and prosperity of the people's livelihood and economy, as well as wishing the leaders, civil servants, forces and the people. People in Long An province on the occasion of the new year as well.
72 Unexploded Ordnance Found in Oddar Meanchey Farmers' Field in Banteay Ampil District
(Oddar Meanchey): 72 unexploded ordnance was found by farmers in Banteay Ampil district, Oddar Meanchey province in two different plantations this morning, January 19, 2020.
Banteay Meanchey District Police Inspectorate said that today, two farmers living in different villages of Kork Mon commune, Banteay Ampil district, found 72 unexploded ordnance in two different fields.
Police confirmed that at 08:30 in the morning, the police received information from Heang Hoeum, male, 53 years old, the chief of Nam Thom village, Kork Mon commune, Banteay Ampil district, found 10 unexploded ordnance of 68 mines when He is plowing.
At 10:18 a.m., police received information from Mao Thearo, a 49-year-old man from Thmor Daun sub-village, who reported that an unexploded ordnance had been found in a potato field in Hanuman village, Kork Mon commune, Banteay Ampil district. 62 rounds, including 43 types of 69 type mines, 16 rounds of 80 mm rounds, 3 sets of mines, 9 boxes of 80 mm cubes, 6 boxes of 69 mines and 2 boxes of mines. Also.
Immediately after the inspection, the authorities contacted the Cambodian Mine Action Organization to accept and destroy, and the authorities also confirmed that the unexploded ordnance is left over from the war.
