Legal Awareness: Missing Announcement
(Phnom Penh): In the event of the death of a person due to a specific cause that can be determined, it is easier for the person with legal benefits to benefit from the deceased person.
But in some cases, if the person has been missing for a long time or there is no information from the person, it is not known whether the person was in a fatal accident or not, such a situation is difficult. To conclude that a person is indeed dead or alive is indeed an issue for a person with legal interests.
Therefore, the Legal Awareness Program of Fresh News in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation would like to raise the topic of "Missing Declaration" to the following students:
Declaration of disappearance is a provision to presume that a person has died legally so that the person concerned can receive legal benefits.
Pursuant to Article 41 of the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia, the conditions for making a declaration of disappearance are as follows:
1. If there is no clear information that the absentee is alive or dead within 5 (five) years, the court may declare that the person is missing at the request of the spouse who is presumed to be the heir. Insurance, authorities, parents, guardians, parents or others with significant legal interest in declaring disappearance.
2: The provisions of the first paragraph above shall also apply to the case of a person entering a war zone, a person present in a sunken ship, or a person who has encountered other dangers that may lead to To die and it is not clear whether the absentee survived or died within one (1) year after the end of the war, after the ship sank or after another accident has passed.
In addition, the announcement of the disappearance shall be made through the procedure of public warning, in order to provide an opportunity and allow the person who knows about the death or life of the person to be declared missing to report to the person concerned. In accordance with the spirit of Article 42 on the public admonition of the Civil Code.
The public warnings provided for in Article 54 of the Law on the Procedure of Non-Civil Cases are as follows:
After a proper application and a public warning until the decision is finalized, the effect of the disappearance is as follows:
In short, the announcement of the disappearance is a benefit to the Confederation of the Descendants, the authorities and the legal entities involved.
