* First: Environmental factors: Can smoke from the brick kiln behind the high school about 200 meters away and the incinerator in the school and hot weather * Second: Health factors: poor students, irregular diet, insufficient rest, among 41 patients 5 cases of lack of sugar, 3 cases of lack of calcium, in addition, related to the feeling of shock after seeing a friend faint.
According to the deputy governor, so far the situation of the students has improved and there are no serious problems due to the emergency assistance from doctors, authorities and authorities at all levels.
In the afternoon of the same day, Mr. Hak Sok Makara inspected the high school and supported the construction of a four-story school fence at a cost of $ 620.
Chinese Embassy Competition Article: "My Short Story on China"
(Phnom Penh): Due to the good relations and cooperation between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the people of China for a long time until now and with the constant support of China in all areas. I was lucky enough to get to know this great and ancient country with a great culture by attending two training sessions.
At the end of 2018, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia received 40 mobile ambulances, all equipped with modern equipment and expensive equipment for Cambodian doctors to provide basic to the people. These are all grants from the Chinese government to Cambodia.
Through these two training sessions, I really gained good knowledge and experience that should be pleasant and unforgettable. Both training courses have provided tremendous benefits for the development of the employment sector in my unit and have contributed greatly to the development of Cambodia as a whole.
The annual expenditure on health (6.39% in 2018) is less but more efficient. 95% of Chinese people have state health insurance. Due to effective and sustainable reforms in all areas and rapid economic growth, the morbidity and mortality rate of the population has decreased significantly. The living standards and average life expectancy of the people are also gradually improving.
However, in order to effectively address the above issues, the Chinese government has initiated a new strategic policy, which has been in force since 2016. The plan is called the "Strategic Plan for a Healthy China by 2030."
This strategic plan is implemented based on five main goals, including:
* First: Promote comfortable living to the general population. By train, by bus, by supermarket, public and private institutions, and by public transport, health education posters are posted, as well as radio and television broadcasts.
* Second, improve the best health services by improving the quality of health services, increase the capacity of human resources, increase health facilities in all populated areas, and equip medical facilities in all health facilities as needed, increase coverage. 100% health insurance service provides quality, effective, high quality and affordable treatment.
To reduce chronic diseases, which are a heavy burden on the state, the government has made efforts to research all forms of cancer and other chronic diseases everywhere. Research the daily diet that affects chronic diseases and measure the nutritional status to find the determinants of chronic diseases. Educate and prevent all kinds of infectious diseases everywhere by eliminating all sources of disease and providing all kinds of vaccines 100% and highly effective.
* Third: Development of modern health industry and equipped with modern technology such as 5G (5G) system that specialists can operate on patients via satellite.
* Fourth: Create a comfortable environment (improve the environment, reduce air pollution) by stopping the use of gasoline-powered bicycles to battery-powered bicycles. The government encourages people to use tax-free cars.
Buses and trains are all powered by electricity. I observed everywhere I went to see that all the roads were clean, no rubbish, no dust and no stench. If there is a road that is under repair, it should be covered with tarpaulins or rubber tarpaulins to prevent dust. On the streets everywhere, trees and flowers are planted on both sides of the road to beautify the city and reduce air pollution.
* Fifth: Improve the social health insurance system by providing health insurance to all people to receive equal treatment with quality and virtue.
All in all, I am very proud and excited that the leaders of Cambodia and China have such strong ties and solidarity that you, the people of both countries, have the opportunity to learn from each other and to learn from each other. Construction assistance in all areas for Cambodia from the Chinese government.
