The General Department of Taxation further explained that the abolition of slaughter tax is one of the types of tax relating to the slaughterhouse business (slaughterhouse, cattle, pigs) only, does not mean that the slaughterhouse business is exempt. From the obligation to pay all kinds of taxes.
Pursuant to the Law on Finance for Management 2016 promulgated by Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 1215/2016, the tax regime of the Kingdom of Cambodia is defined as a self-declaration regime that divides taxpayers into three. The categories are small taxpayers, medium taxpayers and large taxpayers.
According to Prakas No. 025 MEF.PrK dated 24 January 2018 on the adjustment of taxpayer classification according to the self-declaration regime:
For taxpayers whose turnover is in the above three categories, they are obliged to declare monthly and annual taxes related to their business, such as:
First, the obligation to file a declaration and pay monthly taxes, including: * Income tax relief, income tax, special tax on certain goods and services, public comment tax and other taxes * Salary tax * Deductible tax General * Value Added Tax
The General Department of Taxation emphasizes that "all types of businesses, including slaughterhouse businesses, as long as they have an annual turnover of 250 million riels or more, are required to pay monthly and annual taxes in accordance with applicable tax laws and regulations." In particular, businesses with an annual turnover of less than 250 million riels are not required to pay monthly and annual tax obligations.
