(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, noted that "peace" and stability in Cambodian society has become a major factor in increasing the confidence of investors to invest more in Cambodia.
Minister Pan Sosak made the remarks while presiding over the inauguration ceremony of the newly constructed Toyota (Cambodia) headquarters on January 17, 2020.
During the ceremony, Mr. Pan Sosak praised Toyota, which has been continuously expanding its branches since 1995, and more importantly, in 2020, the company inaugurated its headquarters to meet the needs of its customers.
The Minister said that the development and growth of Toyota as well as the private sector in general reflect the correct implementation of the Royal Government's policies to maintain peace, political stability, security and public order.
On that occasion, on behalf of the Royal Government and the people of Cambodia, the Minister expressed his gratitude and appreciation to the Government and people of Japan for their significant contribution to the quest for peace, national unity and the restoration and development of the Cambodian economy. To date, through financing, cooperation, infrastructure construction, technical assistance and human resource development, as well as Japanese private sector investment in Cambodia.
In the framework of foreign direct investment from Japan from 1994 to the first quarter of 2019, the Council for the Development of Cambodia registered 137 investment projects of Japanese companies with a total investment capital of approximately 2.5 billion US dollars. Mainly engaged in the production of electrical and electronic components, auto parts and technical equipment, agro-industry, food processing, hotels, tourism, hospitals and supermarkets.
To strengthen trade and investment cooperation, Cambodia and Japan have signed an agreement on liberalization, promotion and protection of investment by establishing a mechanism for a joint meeting of the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee.
