Two Cambodians were sent back to Cambodia by the Thai authorities after being sentenced to almost 2 years for crossing the border illegally for logging
(Oddar Meanchey): Two Cambodian citizens were sent back to the Cambodian authorities by the Thai authorities through the Choam Sangam international border crossing in Cheung Phnom village, Trapeang Prey commune, Anlong Veng district, Oddar Meanchey province, after serving almost 2 years in Thai territory for crossing the border. Illegal logging of rosewood.
At 12:22 on January 17, 2020, the Thai authorities sent two Cambodians through the Choam Sangam international border crossing after being detained for almost a while, according to the Oddar Meanchey Provincial Police. Two years in Kantalak district, Sisaket province, Thailand, for illegally crossing the border to cut rosewood through the Ghost Mountain Pass.
Authorities said that the two Cambodian citizens were arrested by Thai soldiers on January 26, 2018 for illegally crossing the border to cut down trees. According to the police, the two Cambodian citizens are: Sieng Sros, male, 42 years old, living in Sambo village, Prey Kuy commune, Kampong Svay district, Kampong Thom province, and Nuon Sopheak, male, 31 years old, living in O village, Sangvei commune, Chi Kreng district, province Siem Reap.
After educating and concluding a contract to stop illegal immigration, the authorities allowed them to return to their respective homes.
