I still remember that the leaders of the "Khmer Patriot" party are all former CNRP officials and former lawmakers who have pro-Kem Sokha tendencies, such as Mr. Chivakat, Mr. Sim Sovanny, Mr. Kang Kimhak and so on. Etc. Therefore, even though the new party they plan to form has not yet been legitimized, the group's opposition to the law dares to issue arbitrary statements to protect and support Kem Sokha.
So I can say that the former opposition group that formed this new party is a good fig tree, but the shell, apart from the fact, is a party that violently violates the law, following the example of the party that the court has clearly dissolved.
