At the 7th ASEAN-US Summit, only three ASEAN Prime Ministers attended, including the Prime Ministers of Thailand, Laos and Vietnam. For the other seven ASEAN member countries, including Cambodia, only the foreign minister will participate. Senior official of the Ministry of Environment: So far, the air quality situation in Cambodia has not reached alarming levels
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Net Pheaktra, Secretary of State and Spokesman of the Ministry of Environment, on the evening of January 17, 2020, stated that so far the air quality situation in Cambodia has not reached a critical level. Concerned yet, although the results of air quality monitoring show that PM 2.5 inert particle concentration fluctuates.
He said that officials of the Ministry of Environment have been closely monitoring the changes in the concentration of PM10 and PM2.5 in the air in Phnom Penh and in provinces throughout Cambodia.
The Secretary of State added that according to the results of air quality monitoring from the air quality monitoring stations installed by the Ministry of Environment in the capitals and provinces across the country, the air quality situation is declining, especially the PM 10 inertia particle parameter concentration. And PM 2.5 exceeds the standard, which poses a risk to public health and measures need to be taken to prevent air pollution.
To protect the health of the Secretary of State, the Ministry of Environment recommends that people who travel on the streets or who work outside the building for long periods of time should wear protective masks.
Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment Neth Pheaktra said that the Ministry of Environment will keep abreast of recent developments related to the air quality situation so that people can easily implement preventive measures in a timely manner.
He added that the Ministry of Environment has set up several air quality monitoring stations in Phnom Penh and in the provinces of Cambodia, which are equipped with modern technology and effective in providing accurate data on air quality.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the concentration of PM2.5 in Phnom Penh until the evening of January 17 varied between 49 and 80 and in some provinces below 100, while the quality standards. Air limited to 50.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment stated that the dissemination of information related to the air quality situation in Cambodia, which does not come from the Ministry of Environment, is unofficial information.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra stated that the increase in PM2.5 inertia in the air is not limited to the Kingdom of Cambodia, but the trend of growth in other countries in the region due to the climate of the Mekong sub-region. There is dryness.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the main sources and activities that caused the increase in PM2.5 particulate matter concentration were emissions from industrial plants, vehicles from diesel and fuel. Others include wildfires, forest fires, grassland fires, wall cremation, rubbish burning, open solid waste and landfills, construction sites, and more.
In view of such problems and to improve air quality in the capital and provinces on the evening of January 17, 2020, the Ministry of Environment issued a notification to the Department of Environment of the Capital and Provinces to cooperate with the sub-national administration to implement a number of measures, including :
1. Take measures to prevent wildfires and burning of solid waste in the open, fires at landfills. 2. Take measures to prevent dust from construction sites and infrastructure improvements and dust on the roads. 3. Clean the streets and public places. 4: Educate people not to burn garbage, solid waste, burning grass, roots, walls and other agricultural waste.
