(Kandal): The Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kandal Province, on January 17, 2020, brought materials, food and some money to help two families in Peam Village, Roka Kong 1 Commune, Muk Kampoul District, Kandal Province. The house burned down a while ago.
This humanitarian activity was led by Mr. Kong Sophoan, Chairman of Kandal Provincial Branch of the Cambodian Red Cross, accompanied by the Cambodian Red Cross Sub-Branch, local authorities and many other youths.
Mr. Kong Sophoan expressed his deepest sympathy to the two families of the victims of the house fire that no one wanted to happen.
Taking that opportunity, he also brought a message from Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross to the families of the victims.
He continued that the Cambodian Red Cross, which has Samdech Kittipritthbandit, always thinks about the well-being of the general population, especially the vulnerable people from disasters and victims of various incidents, regardless of caste, race, religion, color. Or any political trend.
He encouraged the families of the two victims of the house fire not to be discouraged and desperate to continue to work hard to support our families.
It should be informed that the humanitarian donation that the Cambodian Red Cross Branch in Kandal province distributed to each victim received 330 kg of rice, 1 box of noodles, 1 box of pure water, 1 box of fish sauce, 1 can of fish, 1 can of rubber, 1 tent, 1 kitchen equipment. Suite and budget 70,000 Riels.
