Below is the video report of the Ministry of Culture: A girl living in Saang district, Kandal province won the grand prize of 100 million Riel from Echitan green tea
(Kandal): The grand prize of 100 million Riels of Echitan Green Tea continued to fall into the hands of another girl named Nget Srey Lin, 11 years old, who is currently studying at Samdech Krom Preah Primary School, Kraing Yov Commune, Saang District, Kandal Province. Ask mom for money to buy a bottle of echinacea green tea from a vendor next door.
Speaking to the team that handed over 100 million Riel to the house in the presence of Mr. Ichitan Pasaknathi, Ms. Chak Leav, 34 years old, the girl's mother described that this lucky daughter named Nget Srey Lin The 11-year-old is currently studying in the third grade of Samdech Krom Preah Primary School in the above commune village.
She added that at present, the standard of living of the family is very poor because there is no business other than farming and weeding for the villagers, who can earn almost enough to supply daily food. On the other hand, there is an elderly mother with a terminal illness who is in urgent need of medical treatment.
Ms. Chak Leav added that in order to win the grand prize of 100 million Riel from Echitan green tea, last weekend, after returning from school, her daughter asked for money to buy Echitan green tea from a seller who Next to each other, a bottle to eat, but when you turn the bottle, you suddenly see a prize of 100 million riels.
She stated that when she first opened the bottle cap, her daughter did not know that it was a big prize, so she asked the seller to help her, and the seller shouted that it was a prize of 100 million Riel. Only once. After receiving 100 million riels, she will use some to build debts and treat her mother, and leave some to create a business to support her daughter's family life and education.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kun Kim, Senior Minister in Charge of Special Missions and First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, and General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, presided over a workshop on search and rescue of building collapses. In the past, with the participation of relevant ministries and units.
During the meeting, the working group also presented the results of search and rescue of previous building collapses and evaluated the strengths, shortcomings, gained experience and set the operation procedures of the search and rescue team to the meeting.
After listening to the presentation, General Vong Pisen praised the search and rescue team for their good cooperation in the past search operations. In addition, he reminded the commanders in charge of each force to prepare their teams well and orderly in the operation.
At the same time, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the total strength of both public and private forces involved in search and rescue operations in the past.
The Senior Minister added that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as the Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, attaches great importance to saving the lives of the victims, and has always been in direct search operations without the leadership of any country. Got it like this.
Senior Minister Kun Kim noted that for the response team to ensure safe and secure response work, there will be no interference from outsiders, cooperate with the national response team leader to identify disaster-affected areas on security and Security.
In addition, prepare guidelines and measures on security in the area, study the actual situation and assess the needs, analyze, map, locate headquarters, prepare response and distribution programs, search and rescue forces, mobilize resources and assistance for Response, monitor and evaluate the response, adjust the plan and be flexible according to the situation.
Ending one's life has a long history in Japan, with some people using it as a way to avoid embarrassment or damage to honor and some problems. Japan remains at the top of the G7 with the highest suicide rate, but thanks to the efforts of Abe Shinzo Abe's government, suicide rates have dropped by 40 percent in the last 15 years. .
The number of suicides dropped to 881, bringing the total number of suicides below 20,000 for the first time since the high suicide rate, according to preliminary data released by Japanese police on Friday. Most notably in 1978. The suicide rate dropped to 15.8 per 100,000 people, the data said. In terms of gender, 13,937 men and 6,022 women committed suicide.
The suicide rate in Japan peaked at 34,427 in 2003. On the other hand, although the Japanese police did not specify the reason for the decline, economic growth, suicide prevention programs, increased mental education services and hotlines, as well as volunteer teams were needed. Believed to be a contributing factor in reducing the number of suicides.
Three trade unions jointly sign a memorandum of understanding to establish a "union union"
(Phnom Penh): Three out of four trade unions have jointly signed a memorandum of understanding to establish a large "Union of Trade Unions (YYKC)" aimed at establishing ties of solidarity and cooperation on behalf of professional organizations. Protect the interests of the same workers in factories across the country.
The signing ceremony took place on the evening of January 16, 2020 at Pochentong Restaurant in Phnom Penh, with Mr. Mom Seak, President of the Union of Youth Spirit Unions for Cambodian Labor, Mr. Long Sophat, President of the Cambodian Youth Union for the Protection of Workers' Rights and Mr. Sok Ravuth, President of the Khmer Union Union. Din Sam Ath, president of the Union of Labor Development Unions, is absent, but will sign later.
Mr. Long Sophat stated that the establishment of the Union of Trade Unions (YYKC) aims to establish a relationship of solidarity and cooperation on behalf of the same workers' protection organizations registered with the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to Protect the rights and interests of trade unions in alliances, federations, unions and local unions, as well as members of factories.
Mr. Mom Seak called on the leaders of the federation and all members to unite as a whole and actively participate in advocacy to safeguard the interests of workers even more.
Mr. Sok Ravuth also said that the unification of forces from these unions will make the Union of Trade Unions (YYKC) stronger to be able to help workers. Joining forces now does not mean wanting to oppose anything, but together implementing the Royal Government's policy on workers and will reduce conflicts. Cambodian woman wins Best Chinese Businessman Award
In that program, Ms. Lok Sovanna, General Director of Keniron Company, received the award as the best businessman and also the first young woman from Cambodia for 2020 before the Chinese New Year under the initiative of the President of the Republic. Chinese people.
Ms. Lok Sovanna stated that this event is held every year before the Chinese New Year to provide opportunities for business people to participate. In 2020, she became the winner of the Best Business Award, selected from among the top 10 business people.
Ms. Lok Sovanna claimed that this award is implemented with a focus on doing business from the past to the present and has built many good works. She considers this award a great honor for her.
At the same time, she added that the award was widely broadcast on China's national television for three months, while the friendship between the Chinese government and the Royal Government of Cambodia is very close.
Ms. Lok Sovanna stated that she was very happy to receive this Outstanding Businessman Award, and that her efforts to be honest and responsible to her business partners were successful, especially in the real estate business in Cambodia. With Chinese businessmen and so on.
Finally, she would like to thank Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen for their thoughtful leadership that has made the country prosperous in almost all areas full of peace. She has just had the opportunity to receive the Best Businessman award now.
