Cambodia, for example, received $ 4.375 billion in revenue from tourism in 2018. After Cambodia received a total of more than 6.2 million international tourists. Among total international tourists, Chinese tourists ranked first with 1.9 million, accounting for 30% of the total international tourists.
In 2019, Chinese tourists are still in the top 10 most visited Cambodia and can reach 2.5 million. While the most international tourists visiting Cambodia after Chinese tourists include Vietnam, Thailand, Laos, South Korea, the United States, Japan, Malaysia, France and the United Kingdom.
The two main factors that motivate the number of Chinese tourists to visit Cambodia from year to year are: cultural, natural and investment tourism destinations. This is according to Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism of Cambodia.
This large number of international tourists has helped Cambodia create 620,000 direct jobs and millions more jobs. The tourism sector will contribute 12.7 percent of GDP in 2018.
After all, Chinese tourists are the type of guests who prefer high-quality, high-standard goods. In line with the new policy of the World Tourism Organization in 2013, all countries should implement the China Ready policy to attract more Chinese tourists to visit their country. This policy ranges from hotel reception to hotel.
The receptionist must be able to speak Chinese and all forms of application, in addition to the national language of each country, must also be available in English and Chinese.
Of course, in addition to attracting a considerable amount of national income every year, tourism can also bring three negative effects in the world: drug problems, crime and sex trafficking. But what Cambodia can do is tighten existing laws in the country. As well as the development of various ethics to promote to tourists visiting Cambodia. This was confirmed by the Minister of Tourism.
And they also educated their people to respect the laws of our country. And we must strive to set this code of conduct for all purposes. "We try to do this work, but if it is a job that negatively affects our year, we must strictly control the law without hesitation."
At the same time, Wang Winthean also encouraged more Chinese tourists to visit and invest in Cambodia. "And I urge them to respect the law as well as the traditions and religion of Cambodia to be a good missionary between China and Cambodia even better."
In addition, the Chinese Embassy has set out a policy to attract 3 million Chinese tourists to visit and invest in Cambodia by 2020. The number of international tourists of all nationalities, and especially Chinese tourists, has made Cambodians working in the tourism sector very happy.
According to a report from the World Tourism Organization, due to China's economic growth and large population, China has become the world's largest tourism market. And all countries should not be overlooked or unprepared to attract this huge number of tourists.
