Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Leads a Delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia to Return safely to the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Annual Meeting in Australia
The APPF held its meeting under the theme "Parliamentary Partnership for 2020 and the Next Year", with more than 350 delegates from 20 APPF member countries and 10 observer countries.
The President of the National Assembly was honored by the Australian Parliament to attend the Executive Committee meeting and delivered a keynote address at the official opening ceremony. The Australian Parliament and the participating delegates praised Samdech for leading the Cambodian Parliament to the 27th APPF Meeting in Siem Reap last year, and the success in Cambodia made the APPF Meeting even more successful. Improved characteristics.
During the meeting, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei met with the President of the National Assembly of Australia to promote parliamentary relations and asked Australia to promote Cambodia's potential in trade, investment and tourism. Samdech also asked Australia to provide more scholarships to Cambodian civil servants and students.
In addition, the National Assembly President met with the Speaker of the National Assembly of Laos, the Vice President of the National Assembly of Vietnam to strengthen cooperation between the two parliaments and exchange information on each other to promote friendly relations. Good cooperation on behalf of neighboring countries.
Minister of Information Explains Why There Are No Questions in the Meeting between Journalists and Samdech Techo PM
(Phnom Penh): The fourth annual meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and nearly 6,000 journalists on January 14, 2020, made most of the journalists happy. From receiving some messages of reminder and improvement from Samdech Techo Prime Minister. In particular, the decision to provide Samdech Techo's volunteer lawyer to defend the media.
"Ly Na" described his difficulties when he went to cover the news that when he went to cover the land dispute, he was threatened by a group of traders who agreed with the authorities. The journalist also mentioned that if she just went to listen to Samdech Techo Prime Minister and eat, she would not participate in the next meeting.
The Minister of Information, Mr. Khieu Kanharith, who was responsible for organizing the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the media, came out to explain that the reason for not preparing to raise questions in this because of concerns and requests. Journalists are collectively referred to through him.
The Minister stated that before the meeting every year, the Association of Journalists always discuss the points to be submitted to the Prime Minister for decision, and the Ministry of Information to review the points that should be submitted to the Prime Minister to decide in principle. The problem is, in general, not just the individual journalists.
At the request of the media requesting a lawyer to assist in the defense, Samdech Techo decided to provide the Samdech's volunteer lawyer to help defend the media as well. This is the additional confirmation of the Minister.
It should be noted that on January 14, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen recently had the opportunity to have a solidarity meal for the fourth time with nearly 6,000 journalists. During the meeting, Samdech Techo Hun Sen not only praised the development of the media sector in Cambodia, but also improved the awkwardness and shortcomings of journalists.
In order for journalists to maintain the value of their professional ethics, avoid lawsuits and criticisms, Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked reporters to memorize a sentence: "Do not violate the rights of others, do not distort the truth." Samdech Techo considered this sentence as a mechanism to protect journalists.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded government officials not to consider journalists as enemies, to be considered as a good cooperation partner.
Samdech Techo's more than two hours of speech at the meeting was seen as an important part of improving the media in Cambodia and helping to improve your professional ethics. The press as well.
