(Koh Kong): Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense and Chairman of the Central Working Group for Koh Kong Province, said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, is an outstanding guide in developing human resources in the country. Cambodia remnants of the Khmer Rouge massacre.
This confirmation of Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh was made this morning, January 17, 2020, on the occasion of Samdech celebrating the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day in Koh Kong province with the participation of Mrs. Mithona Phu Thong, Governor of Koh Kong Province, including officials under all institutions, departments, units, teachers, monks, students and a large crowd.
Samdech Picheay Sena said that through all the sacrifices of Samdech Chacho Hun Sen, the people of Cambodia must believe in Samdech who led the country to grow and develop in all areas and increase human resources to grow. To promote the nation to progress on the international stage.
Samdech Picheay Sena asks all compatriots to unite under the roof of peace, preserve the nation, religion and the King for the future of the nation and future generations.
Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh continued that January 7, 1979 was the day that saved the lives of Cambodians from the dark regime to resurrect from the massacre of more than 3 million innocent Cambodians under the brutal work of the genocidal regime. "Pol Pot."
Samdech Pichey Sena Tea Banh stated that January 7 is not only an event to commemorate the day of the liberation of the country from the genocidal regime, the patriotic force of December 2 and the support of friendly countries, but also an event to show the great The solidarity and determination of the Cambodian People's Party in maintaining lasting peace to bring the Cambodian ship to prosperity faster.
This evening, Samdech Techo Hun Sen attends a dinner to celebrate the Vietnamese New Year
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the evening of January 17, 2020, will attend a dinner to celebrate the Vietnamese New Year. This traditional Vietnamese New Year dinner will be held at Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The event will be attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Vietnamese Ambassador to Cambodia Vu Quang Minh, Cambodian and Vietnamese businessmen, as well as some Vietnamese people living in Cambodia.
This is the first time for Samdech Techo Hun Sen to attend the traditional Vietnamese New Year dinner. During his visit to Vietnam in 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen announced that he would attend a traditional Vietnamese New Year dinner to enhance the relationship between investors, businessmen as well as the people of Cambodia and Vietnam.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, enhancing the relationship between investors, businessmen and the people of the two countries also contributes to boosting investment and trade between the two countries.
Cambodia and Vietnam established diplomatic relations on June 24, 1967, and were severed in March 1970. The two countries reconnected in January 1979. Vietnam and Cambodia are countries with villages and fences with a common border of about 1,270 km.
At present, the country relations have lasted for more than half a century. Currently, the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Vietnam are seeking to promote better relations between the two countries, especially to increase investment and trade between the two countries.
In 2017, the two countries achieved a trade volume of about 2.13 billion US dollars, an increase of about 30% compared to 2016. But Cambodia's exports to Vietnam are still small. In fact, Cambodia's exports to Vietnam in 2017 amounted to 342 million US dollars, compared to Cambodia's imports from Vietnam in 2017 was about 1.8 billion US dollars.
In 2018, the trade volume between the two countries will reach 4.7 billion US dollars. Cambodia and Vietnam plan to boost trade to 5 billion US dollars.
As of November 2018, the Council for the Development of Cambodia has registered 75 investment projects of Vietnamese companies with a total investment of 2.4 billion USD, focusing on agriculture and infrastructure. .
