In addition, the Koh Kong Provincial Police confirmed that the drone crashed in the middle of the forest in Koh Sdach commune, Kirisakor district, Koh Kong province, causing no damage. Ministry of Agriculture: There are no cases of pigs imported from Vietnam to Cambodia, between 3.5 thousand and 7,000 pigs a day from Thailand through Cambodia to meet the needs of Vietnam
(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on January 17, 2020 issued a press release confirming that there is no increase in the import of pigs from Vietnam to Cambodia.
The reaffirmation comes after it was discovered that a number of foreign-language newspapers and radio stations in the Khmer language had published and disseminated untrue information accusing the competent officials, especially the Takeo provincial authorities, and Vietnamese traders. Prepare to import pigs without inspection before the Chinese New Year.
In this regard, the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture explained:
Since the beginning of 2019, Vietnam has suffered from an outbreak of African swine fever and has spread almost across the country, resulting in a decrease in pig production and a shortage of pork supply to meet market demand. In order to require the import of pigs from abroad to meet the shortage.
Cambodia is a country that imports pigs from Thailand to Vietnam in accordance with Cambodian law, where the legal company has received a permit from the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries and a transit permit issued by the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production. Also have animal hygiene certificates from exporting countries to supply in foreign markets, Vietnam.
