Mr. Say Sam Al and Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province led a working group to inspect the living conditions and development of Koh Rong City
(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of Environment and Chairman of the National Task Force for Preah Sihanouk Province, together with Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, led the working group to inspect the living conditions and development of Koh Rong City.
The inspection of living conditions and development of Koh Rong city took place on January 16, 2020, and on that occasion, the Minister of Environment Say Sam Al led a public forum with the participation of people, government officials, the Armed Forces. And nearly 300 local authorities.
The forum raised a number of challenges and suggestions by the mayor, commune chief and residents, including:
In response to the above request, the Minister of Environment raised the following important points:
First: Accept land disputes, land ownership issues to resolve with relevant institutions Second: Resolve requests and mechanisms for waste management, provision of additional means of transportation and incinerators on Koh Rong City Third: Inspire the movement to participate in maintenance Protect the environment and natural resources. 4: Promote the development of urban development plans with relevant institutions; and 5: Strengthen local villages, communes, especially for tourists.
(Phnom Penh): The Secretariat for Prevention and Suppression of Theft in Phnom Penh of the General Commission of the National Police this morning, January 17, 2020, held a meeting to assess the situation of theft in Phnom Penh in December this year. 2019 and raise the direction to continue.
The meeting was chaired by Lt. Gen. N. Bora, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and was attended by the Heads of Relevant Departments, Deputy Heads of Departments, Deputy Commissioners of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police, Heads of Offices of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police and 14 District Inspectors. Many other relevant officials as well.
According to the report of Major General Suy Sokunthea, Deputy Director of the Criminal Police Department and Director of the Secretariat for Prevention and Suppression of Theft of the General Commission of the National Police, the total number of crimes committed in December 2019 was 56 cases, an increase of 2 cases, including 27 cases of theft and 29 cases of electric shock.
According to Major General Suy Sokunthea, as a result of the operation, with the efforts of all forces, all units cooperated in cracking down on a total of 41 cases, arresting 52 suspects, of which the suspects were cracked down after drug testing. There were 48, or 92 percent.
Speaking on that occasion, Lt. Gen. N. Bora continued to warn and issue strict orders, with the relevant specialized forces must cooperate with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to prevent the occurrence of crimes and if the crimes have already occurred. And must work together to crack down to reduce crime in Phnom Penh.
The Deputy Commissioner of the National Police also praised the forces of all units that have cooperated well in cracking down on crimes. In addition, he also advised to find out what are the challenges that lead to crime.
