(Phnom Penh): On the night of January 16, 2020, the police of Chamkar Mon district brought the four students who kicked a female student at Phsar Doeum Thkov High School to the Phnom Penh Municipal Police for legal action.
At the same time, the young victims were also brought in for further questioning in order to seek justice. This is according to the report from Fresh News Agency from Phnom Penh Police.
On January 16, 2020, local police in Chamkar Mon district arrested four female students for interrogation and took legal action after they kicked and insulted a female student at Phsar Doeum High School. Thkov, Khan Chamkarmon, Phnom Penh.
On the afternoon of January 16, 2020, the people and the family of the victim girl took their child to ask the police to intervene and stop the provocative girl to be questioned about the incident at Phsar Doeum Thkov High School. This was confirmed by the authorities to Fresh News.
According to the authorities, the victim was a 8th grader named Srun Keo Morakot, 16 years old, living in Sangkat Phsar Doeum Thkov, Street 3430. As for the perpetrators, there were four of them, each in the ninth grade, calling three other high school girls from outside to attack the victims.
According to the victim's family, the incident took place on the afternoon of December 25, 2019 at Phsar Doeum Thkov High School. After beating his body with his feet and head, the perpetrators threatened the victim. The victim did not go to school because his body was completely covered.
Please note that after the publication and distribution of a video clip that shows the activities of a group of students kicking a female student and swearing like animals, the police found that the violence occurred at Phsar Doeum High School. Thkov in Chamkarmon district and sought the victims and perpetrators to solve and take legal action.
Such gangster activities of girls make social media users request the authorities to arrest the perpetrators and punish them according to the law.
Provincial Governor Pledges to Celebrate the 2nd ASEAN Clean City Award in Takhmao City
(Brunei): After participating in the competition, Takhmao city of Kandal province won the second ASEAN Clean City and Governor Mao Phirun promised to hold a solemn celebration for this great honor.
The award ceremony took place on the evening of January 16, 2020 in the capital, Bandar Seri Begawan, Brunei Darussalam.
During the event, Mr. Mao Phirun took to the stage to receive the ASEAN Clean Cities Award, much to the delight of thousands of guests from ASEAN countries.
According to the provincial governor, the commission has studied many of the statutes, while Takhmao has done well in the desired areas, among the major cities in the ASEAN region, Takhmao won the city award. This beautiful ASEAN, which is valid for 2020-2022.
The provincial governor said that upon his return to Cambodia, the Kandal provincial administration will organize a solemn celebration to celebrate the glorious victory of Takhmao City.
It should be informed that in order to win the award in the ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities Competition, all 10 communes in Takhmao City participated in organizing and cleaning up the environment in accordance with the 7 basic indicators, 28 detailed indicators and 108 criteria of the ASEAN Clean Tourism Cities standard.
