(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ky Tech, Royal Government Lawyer and Civil Party, in the press conference at noon on 16 January 2020, after the end of the third hearing in the case of Mr. Kem Sokha, reaffirmed that the nine countries The name in the letter from the Royal Government's lawyer submitted to the Trial Chamber is only relevant to the names in the case file, it is not related to all the crimes against Mr. Kem Sokha.
Ky Tech's lawyer claimed that the public was confused by seeing in the media that those countries were involved in Kem Sokha's treason case. In fact, the names of the countries listed in the letter to the Trial Chamber only indicate the source of the relevant documents, the names of the countries do not mean that all of them are involved in Kem Sokha's crimes.
At the same time, Mr. Ky Tech also claimed that the written representation of those countries in the verdict is for the purpose of maintaining good relations between states.
