A man driving a motorbike collided with the steering wheel of another motorbike in the middle of the road and was crushed to death by a car in Dangkor district
(Phnom Penh): A man died tragically in the middle of the road while riding a motorbike with another motorbike and was hit by a car coming from behind the brakes, not breaking the head, died immediately at 12 noon on the 16th January 2020, located along National Road 3, Sangkat Kraing Pong, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
According to the police, the man who was crushed to death by the car was named Chan Vichet, 39 years old, a cabbage seller living in Prek Stong village, Ro Prek Koy commune, Saang district, Kandal province. The driver of the car was not identified because he got out of the car and fled the scene.
After the accident, the car tried to drive away for about 300 meters, then Taikong got off the car and fled, leaving the car behind.
After the incident, the local authorities cooperated with the professional police to measure and drag the car and motorbike to be stored at the Land Traffic Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Police Commission, waiting for the next time. The body was handed over to relatives to be taken to a traditional ceremony in the hometown. Unusual! Up to "20,000" women apply to be the girlfriend of Japanese billionaire to ascend to the moon together!
