He also sent a message to the people in the province to participate in maintaining the belt, the number one clean city, please clean the environment to be a city inscribed on the World Heritage. Senior official of the Ministry of Agriculture: No pig imports from Vietnam to Cambodia, pigs in Vietnam are more expensive than in Cambodia
(Takeo): The Royal Government of Cambodia delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, Mr. Tan Phannara, confirmed that there is no import of pigs from Vietnam to the Cambodian market because the price of pork in Vietnam is more expensive than pork in Cambodia.
Speaking to reporters after a meeting with veterinary officials and pig traders in Takeo province on the afternoon of January 16, 2020, Mr. Tan Phannara said that Vietnam is experiencing a shortage of pork. Much to supply its domestic market after the outbreak of African plague, which led to the import of pigs from Thailand to Vietnam, passing through Cambodia from 3,500 to 5,000 head per day.
Mr. Tan Phannara stressed that the price of pork in Vietnam is from $ 3.5 to $ 4 per kilogram, while the price of pork in Cambodia is only 11,000 to 12,000 riel per kilogram. According to reports, from now until the end of March, Vietnam needs another 100,000 tons of frozen pork, so there is no reason to import pigs from Vietnam to the Cambodian market.
In addition, Mr. Tan Phannara also warned that if the company does not follow the instructions, he will close the license to import pigs from Thailand to Vietnam through Takeo.
