National Police: More than 200 deaths due to traffic accidents in 2019, while more than 1,300 injured
This is according to General HIM Yan, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, speaking to the media this morning, January 16, 2020, after the meeting to review the results of road traffic safety work in 2019 and work directions. 2020 of the Second Subcommittee of the National Committee for Road Safety, headed by General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General.
General Hem Yan emphasized that for 2019, the traffic activity was very busy, with the growth of vehicles increased to 37%, in which the development of the country and the economy has progressed, thus increasing the rate. Traffic accidents increased by 26% and the number of fatalities increased by 220% or 12% and the number of injuries increased by 29% compared to 2018.
General Him Yan claimed that the factors that led to the increase in the number of traffic accidents, firstly, due to the traffic congestion factor, and secondly, the awareness of the people is still limited, including speeding. Limitations, disrespect for priority rights, overtaking problems, careless turns and drunk driving problems.
On that occasion, General Santibandit Neth Savoeun, as the Chairman of the Second Sub-Committee, took the example of the negative points causing traffic accidents in 2019 as a practical key to prepare for the implementation of measures to implement the direction. In 2020, reduce traffic accidents.
In addition, General Santibandit Neth Savoeun warned to tighten the traffic law, the role of each unit in the Second Sub-Committee of the NCDD. To participate in the implementation of the direction of 2020 to reduce traffic accidents, measures to find people who cause traffic accidents, hit and run for legal punishment and many other suggestions to help prepare the direction report of the Second Sub-Committee for the National Committee Road traffic safety.
Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia demonstrates the strength of the banking sector in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, expressed the strong position of the banking sector in Cambodia after the full peace, the banking system has developed rapidly and has contributed significantly to support and promote Economic and social development.
The Governor stated that in 2019, the National Bank of Cambodia also officially inaugurated the Museum of Economics and Currency of Preah Srey Isan Ivarman, also known as the Museum of the United States, which shows the history related to socio-economic development and Cambodian currency since the first century, especially in the last 40 years.
Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia, made the remarks at the opening ceremony of the National Bank of Cambodia's 2019 Annual Meeting and Work Orientation 2020 on January 16, 2020.
He added that the banking system in Cambodia continues to develop strong, healthy banking and financial institutions and risks are effectively managed.
Mr. Chea Chanto said that in order to boost economic activity, countries have increasingly relied on domestic and regional consumption and investment, with the strengthening of economic stability and resilience, which can face external shocks due to economic uncertainty. The world.
In addition, it has been observed that the central bank has played an important role in supporting growth and stabilizing the economy by implementing monetary policy, deflation, by lowering the benchmark interest rate or injecting capital into the market while inflation is in full swing. Low yet.
According to the report of the National Bank of Cambodia, the deposit accounts of banking and microfinance institutions have increased to 7.5 million accounts, loans provided by banking and microfinance institutions to about 3 million people, leasing companies Finance provided loans to 102,000 customers, and rural credit institutions provided loans to approximately 194,000 customers.
For MFIs, the interest rate on KHR and USD is similar to the previous year, with less volatility at an average rate of 8% and 7.8%, respectively. Meanwhile, the loan interest rate in KHR and USD decreased to 15% and 16% respectively in 2019 after the issuance of Prakas on the 18% loan interest rate ceiling, which has been positive. More to microfinance clients.
