The second phase of the 20th Century Conservation Project is funded by the US Department of State's Ambassador for Cultural Preservation Fund, with a budget of $ 75,000. The signing of this agreement took place at the Tuol Sleng Museum this morning, January 16, 2020.
Ms. Pheung Sakona said the project would focus on textiles on the ground floor of the K building, where the garments had been piled up for more than nine years. In addition to conservation and registration work, the team will consider new installation techniques by creating a special cabinet that can help reduce damage from pests and moisture from the weather.
She stressed that the activities of the United States in supporting the textile conservation project at the Tuol Sleng Museum are very important for the ministry as well as the Cambodian people throughout the country, as all of this evidence is historical evidence for the study of crime. What the Khmer Rouge did to millions of innocent people between 1975-1979.
In addition, the Minister of Culture also said that after the completion of this conservation, some textiles will be selected to be displayed to the national and international public in the permanent and non-permanent exhibition in 2022.
Ms. Phoeung Sakona said that the textile conservation project not only saved the historical artifact, but also provided another important benefit to the Tuol Sleng Museum, namely the training of human resources for the sustainability of the restoration of the sector in the future.
According to the press release, the project on "Preservation of 20th Century Artifacts at the Tuol Sleng Genocide Museum, Phase II in Phnom Penh" highlights US efforts to preserve Cambodia's heritage and demonstrate cooperation. Between the United States and Cambodian authorities in documenting the atrocities of the Khmer Rouge.
The textile conservation project will focus on training workshops, conservation, identification of objects for conservation, maintenance of general objects, documentation, cataloging and selection of more than 5,000 long-standing textile exhibits.
In 2017, the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts received US $ 55,500 for the first phase of conservation projects. This project is the first achievement that demonstrates the team's efforts in documenting and preserving S-21 victims' clothing, which has been kept at the museum for decades. NCX takes Ratanakkiri as the starting point for the ADV150 motorcycle parade to Mondulkiri
Mr. Khan Chai Kia Sri Thanakan said that the purpose of this celebration is to raise awareness of road traffic laws and driver safety on the road to contribute to reducing traffic accidents on the road.
In addition, NCX has donated 3 tons of rice, 3 million Riels and 83 hats to the Ratanakkiri Provincial Administration for actual use.
Please note that NCX (NCX) is one of the most famous and largest companies and a leading company in the motorcycle manufacturing and distribution industry in the Kingdom of Cambodia. NCX was first established in 1992 to import Honda finished products to market.
Due to the popularity and fast and strong support from customers, the company established its small production line in 1999, located in the center of Phnom Penh, assembling motorcycles in IKD format, and in 2004 the company continued Expanded into a new large-scale production line, located along Veng Sreng Blvd., Sangkat Choam Chao, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Today, NCX not only has a production line for assembling motorcycles, but also a production line for the production of some motorcycle parts in the IKD1.5 format, enabling the company to create a lot of jobs for Cambodians. . In fact, NCX currently employs 1,300 people.
Today, NCX has become one of the most successful and large companies in Cambodia and a leader in the motorcycle manufacturing and distribution industry, with hundreds of major branches and sub-branches in Cambodia. Nationwide distribution of its products.
