Production chains - Services for the benefit of workers, job opportunities and investment are points that need to be amended
(Phnom Penh): Issues related to providing additional benefits to workers, increasing employment opportunities, increasing production and service chains, as well as attracting investment are important points in reviewing and discussing amendments to the Labor Law.
A total of 85 workers 'representatives, trade unions, employers' associations, relevant ministries, relevant national and international organizations, representatives of diplomats and development partners, as well as experts from the International Labor Organization (ILO) came together to review and discuss input. In favor of amending the Labor Law, which is more than two decades old, to continue to respond to the country's socio-economic development.
Speaking at the opening of a tripartite consultation meeting on the amendment of the Labor Law at the Sunway Hotel on the morning of January 16, 2020, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that in line with the sharp reform measures. The Prime Minister of the Ministry of Labor has set up a working group to study the possibility of amending the labor law in accordance with the economic and social context.
After completing a preliminary study on the necessity and benefits of the Labor Law Amendment, the Ministry, in collaboration with ILO experts, organized the first Tripartite Consultative Workshop to discuss the feasibility of:
2. The abolition of the next day's leave for the Sunday holiday, as applicable to general public officials and practice in some countries in the region. This adjustment is in response to the socio-economic development of Cambodia, aiming to increase labor productivity and strengthen the economic competitiveness of Cambodia, both regionally and globally. The Ministry will thoroughly examine and ensure that the interests of all workers are not reduced.
In this regard, in order to strengthen the effectiveness of labor dispute resolution mechanisms and respond to the needs of the parties to disputes, as well as to ensure harmony in industrial relations, opening the Arbitration Council to resolve individual labor disputes is the best solution.
The above three points are the priority points that the working group studied and prepared to submit to the workshop to review and discuss together to reach a consensus to come up with better solutions to promote labor rights and maintain Achieve Cambodia's competitiveness.
The Minister encouraged and encouraged all parties to have a professional discussion in a spirit of shared responsibility to ensure harmony in industrial relations. At the same time, the Ministry of Labor is ready to continue to cooperate with social partners and stakeholders to contribute with the Royal Government in achieving the vision of Cambodia 2030, a high middle income country and 2050. It is a high income country.
