(Phnom Penh): The second trial of former opposition leader Kem Sokha on the afternoon of January 15, 2020, ended smoothly at more than 5 pm.
During the hearing, the Royal Government of Cambodia, led by Mr. Ky Tech and the Civil Party lawyers, requested the Trial Chamber to include letters from the nine countries involved in Kem Sokha's case on the minutes and verdict.
The Trial Chamber approved the request for a letter of representation from these nine countries at the request of the Royal Government's lawyers on the judgment, but the "court records" did not allow the lawyers' request to be named directly.
Speaking to reporters after the second hearing on January 15, 2020, Mr. Ky Tech confirmed that the hearing on the afternoon of January 15 has an important point that connects to the first hearing this morning. January 15, 2020 is the application for the use of words representing some foreign states, some organizations and the names of some relevant foreign individuals.
This afternoon, the Trial Chamber took up the case, and after the discussion, the lawyers representing the Civil Parties and the lawyers representing the Royal Government of Cambodia noted that the request to use the word representative Of those countries in order to avoid affecting the good relations between Cambodia and the countries involved in the case of the accused Kem Sokha.
"The important thing is that we ask the whole tribunal to consider the national interest, because the relationship between countries is for the national interest," he said. "After this discussion, the Trial Chamber accepted the application, accepting the use of a representative word in the verdict of this case, while the record still retains the name of the country because it is an internal administrative document of the court."
The nine countries to be represented in the verdict in Kem Sokha's verdict are Indonesia, Yugoslavia, Serbia, Australia, the United States, Canada, the European Union, Taiwan and India.
Please be informed that the first day of the hearing on the peace case of Mr. Kem Sokha, on January 15, 2020, ended smoothly, while the security issue was also tightened. On January 16, 2020, this hearing will continue. 50 Million Riel Award of Cambodian Beer Contributes to Solving Medical Expenses for a Poor Family in Kampong Speu Province
