As of 2019, Singapore's investment in Cambodia is $ 1.355 million, senior Cambodian officials continue to work hard to showcase Singaporean business opportunities
(Singapore): As of December 2019, Singapore's investment in Cambodia totaled about 1.355 million US dollars, creating more than 150,000 jobs. This is according to the record of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
Along with the size of the investment, senior Cambodian officials have continued to make efforts to present business opportunities in Cambodia to attract Singaporean investors to expand their investment.
On the morning of January 15, 2020, at the invitation of the Singapore Business Federation, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary-General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia, participated as the guest speaker at the seminar on "Cambodia-Singapore Business Dialogue". With the participation of about 100 Singaporean investors.
The workshop was organized to share information with Singaporean investors on key developments in Cambodia in relation to business and investment opportunities, as well as the introduction of new measures by the Royal Government of Cambodia under the wise leadership. Of Samdech Techo Prime Minister aims to improve the business and investment environment in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea briefed the workshop on the achievements that Cambodia has achieved over the past two decades after achieving complete peace in the country through the win-win policy of the Prime Minister.
The Minister thanked Singaporean investors for giving confidence to the Royal Government of Cambodia through past investments and encouraged Singaporean investors to increase their investment in Cambodia.
He said that in order to promote bilateral investment, the two governments signed an agreement on the avoidance of double taxation and the prevention of fraud involving income tax on May 20, 2016. It is Cambodia's first agreement with a friendly partner.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea recalled the entry into force of the ASEAN Economic Community, which is a driving force for trade and investment in the region. In this regard, he urged Singaporean investors to consider investing in Cambodia in activities that participate in the regional value chain.
At the same time, he urged investment in agricultural processing and support activities in the tourism sector to take full advantage of Cambodia's rich potential in these areas. Mr. Thian Tai Chew, Executive Director of the Singapore Business Federation, praised the remarkable economic growth that Cambodia has achieved in the past, reflecting the efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
He added that Cambodia is a major investment destination for Singaporean investors, with the latest survey by the Singapore Business Federation showing that Cambodia ranks seventh among countries in which Singaporean investors are interested in investing.
Amid the reform measures that the Royal Government of Cambodia has been putting in place, Mr. Thien Taichiv expressed optimism about the decisions of Singaporean businessmen and investors to invest in Cambodia, which offers opportunities in many areas. NASA's new spacecraft to explore Mars this year will be officially named in March
