CSX: Growth momentum in securities sector will attract more companies to list
(Phnom Penh): The growth momentum of the securities sector in Cambodia will attract more companies to list, while by 2020, seven companies are expected to enter the securities market, four of which will Listed for sale of equity securities and 3 companies listed for sale of bonds. This was stated by Mr. Hong Sochua, Director General of the Cambodia Securities Exchange (CSX).
Mr. Hong Sochua claimed that the factors that make the securities sector grow because in 2019, the securities sector achieved high growth, reaching 870.65 points, while the market capitalization (company share price decreased. Listed in all stock exchanges) peaked at $ 802 million.
At the same time, he said, the trading volume jumped to a record high of $ 30 million, while the trading volume was 9.45 million shares, the highest ever on the Cambodia Securities Exchange.
"These factors indicate that the securities sector is starting to grow and attract companies to list," he said. In fact, in 2020, with favorable conditions such as economic growth continues to increase, tax incentives in the securities sector, the growth of companies aiming to register the market penetration of major local banks. "Like a positive sign of the participation of the Cambodian people in investment."
Mr. Hong Sochua made this remark while attending a press conference on "Perspectives of the Securities Sector in Cambodia 2020" on January 15, 2020.
