The President of the National Assembly of Cambodia and Laos supported the cooperation between the two governments in the past and continued to strengthen cooperation.
(Australia): After receiving a hearing with the Vice President of Vietnam, on the morning of January 15, 2020, Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly, met with Mrs. Panya Toto, President of the National Assembly of the Lao People's Democratic Republic. At the 28th Annual Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum in Canberra at the Australian Parliament.
The two National Assembly presidents expressed their support for the cooperation between the two governments in the past, especially the results of the recent visit of the Lao Prime Minister to Cambodia, which have borne fruit. For the benefit of both countries and peoples.
The Prime Ministers of Cambodia and Laos agreed to enhance relations to the level of comprehensive and long-term strategic partnership in the fields of politics, security, economy and socio-culture.
Samdech Akka Moha Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin informed his Lao counterpart that the National Assembly of Cambodia recently approved a project to purchase 2,400 MW of electricity from a coal-fired power plant from Laos. The project has contributed to the economic and social development of both countries.
Ms. Panya Toto asked the National Assembly President to further promote relations and cooperation between the two parliaments, especially the exchange of experiences between the two parliamentary groups.
Dr. N Channy: Investment with ACLEDA Bank will become the largest institution in Cambodia
This statement was made on the occasion of Dr. N. Channy's participation in the seminar on Dissemination of the process of public offering of securities to clients and investment partners organized by ACLEDA Bank Plc. The ceremony was held at the head office of ACLEDA Bank this morning, January 15, 2020.
According to the plan, the issuance of ACLEDA Bank's equity securities is expected to be completed in April 2020.
Dr. N. Channy said that in the past, the benefits of ACLEDA were limited to a small number of shareholders who had a stake in ACLEDA Bank, so the bank wanted to extend its benefits to more customers. Sell securities to the public.
Dr. N. Channy stated that the benefits that customers as well as investors get from investing with ACLEDA Bank through the public purchase of securities on the Cambodia Securities Exchange are many, but please mention the big benefits that customers will receive. Receive dividends from ACLEDA.
In addition, the client will be able to trade shares with ACLEDA and the investor with ACLEDA will become the owner of the largest institution in Cambodia and can order to that institution according to his wishes. This is an additional emphasis of Dr. N. Channy.
The President and CEO of ACLEDA Bank added, "The four major benefits that he received from his share can be traded, he becomes the owner of the largest institution in the Kingdom of Cambodia and can order the Executive Committee to follow the orders of He through the board.
Dr. In Channy said that before ACLEDA officially announced the sale, the bank held a series of seminars to help customers and investors better understand the investment decision, as well as customers to open a trading account before trading. Officially. ACLEDA prefers to be traded individually rather than as a company or institution.
At the same time, Dr. N. Channy said that after organizing a series of workshops, it was found that potential customers have already joined and opened trading accounts to be ready to invest with ACLEDA when ACLEDA announced trading in Coming soon.
Dr. N. Channy added that ACLEDA Bank wants to buy public equity securities from all individuals at once, and this is what ACLEDA desires and is noteworthy, there is more interest from individuals than expected. Leave well.
