Samdech Techo Hun Sen made this announcement during a meeting with about 6,000 Cambodian journalists for the fourth time on the night of January 14, 2020 at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "This is the point where our journalists should contribute more and more to the fight against inactivity, because we need a clean, transparent society and we "Recognize that social injustice is part of social instability and can lead to armed conflict or violence."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued: "Therefore, I urge our journalists to dare to disclose without distortion, but to dare to put on the table in relation to inaction, irregularities, corruption and injustice. "We are not afraid of this."
Samdech Techo Prime Minister's reaction came after Samdech saw that the journalists who used the social network Facebook insulted others and did some unethical activities, such as reporting cases of spouses arguing or going to the parking lot. Cars on the sidewalk, rest when drunk, and so on.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated, "But with progress, we should also talk about some of my frustrations with a small group of Facebook reporters who are self-employed, self-employed, self-employed." "Shoot yourself as a broadcaster and start swearing, which is a violation of the rights and dignity of others."
Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, said that in Cambodia, there are many online media institutions that better respect professional ethics. Except for the Facebook social media, there is still a shortage. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered you to go to the grass, reeds or straw in the flower garden, which will be worthless one day.
In today's meeting, in order to strengthen the implementation of the ethics of journalists better, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also put out a slogan, "Do not violate the rights of others, do not distort the truth."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces January 14 every year to meet journalists (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): In the fourth meeting with journalists in Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia January 14 every year for a meeting between the prince and the media.
During the ceremony held on January 14, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked journalists from all walks of life who participated in the solidarity meal organized by the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said, "And we will hold an annual ceremony that we should determine. "Now I would like to announce that January 14 every year is a meeting between the Prime Minister and Cambodian journalists."
The head of the Royal Government of Cambodia emphasized that during the next meeting, he will review the progress of the development of the media in Cambodia. The prince also instructed each association to hold its annual meeting before the meeting.
It should be informed that during the invitation to honor this solidarity meal, Samdech Techo Hun Sen always evaluated the performance of Cambodian journalists and also provided various recommendations to improve the work of this information to contribute more effectively. More to help improve and develop Cambodian society.
The media sector is considered to be one of the sectors that has contributed significantly to the building of Cambodian society along the path of democracy, contributing to the improvement of society, eliminating corruption and inactivity. Information has also become a messenger and a sacred bridge between the people and the government. In addition, the news also played an important role in presenting Cambodia's image on the international stage.
This statement was made by the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia on the night of January 14, 2020, on the occasion that Samdech presided over the gathering and solidarity meal with more than 5,000 journalists. At Koh Pich Center.
On this occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed some online journalists to respect the media profession properly, respect the rights of others, not just broadcast at will. In that, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also posted an important message for journalists: "Journalists should not violate the rights of others, do not ignore the truth."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech was made on the occasion of Samdech's fourth meeting and solidarity meal with a total of nearly 6,000 journalists at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
At the same time, Samdech Techo, the head of the Royal Government, also advised reporters not to insult others, which caused the audience to lose confidence in the work of the newspaper collapsed due to lack of sponsors.
Samdech Techo expressed his belief that if journalists can adhere to the slogan "Journalists do not violate the rights of others, do not distort the truth", then journalists will be free from lawsuits and fulfill the journalism profession well. .
At the same time, Samdech Techo called on all journalists to join in maintaining peace, because maintaining this peace is not only the work of Samdech or officials in the Royal Government, journalists also need peace because if the country is at war No news coverage because radio and television stations face closure and must wear helmets. Therefore, we must all join in maintaining peace.
Meaningful speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with nearly 6,000 journalists
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, on the evening of January 14, 2020, had the honor of meeting and having a solidarity meal with nearly 6,000 journalists. The fourth Solidarity Dinner with journalists took place at the Koh Pich Convention and Exhibition Center.
This year's Solidarity Dinner is no different from previous years, apart from the media, senior leaders of the Royal Government, provincial governors, officials, spokespersons and government officials involved in the media are allowed to participate. The ceremony, too.
The following are the meaningful remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen during a meeting with nearly 6,000 journalists:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that today's meeting to strengthen the information sector, which is an important part for the development of the country.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked for celebrating his birthday as Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the meeting on January 14 was not intended to coincide with his birthday as Prime Minister. Is just a coincidence.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that for January, it is related to the life history of Samrech and the nation up to 38.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia does not have a regime of transfer of power from father to son, it must be done through elections.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that if it is time to change the Prime Minister, it is not yet time for Hun Manet to become the Prime Minister.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked to stop talking about the effort to transfer power to his son, because Samdech must hold the position of Prime Minister for at least the next 10 years.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that all media can survive is dependent on advertising.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all the companies that helped make the media work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asked companies to support the dissemination of information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all the media for their efforts in disseminating and participating in maintaining peace and political stability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the participation of all media contributed to the maintenance of peace, political stability and macroeconomics.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that bombs can destroy a house and a village, but if the information is distorted, it will affect the functioning of the whole nation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that during the conflict between the United States and Iran, the first thing he did was to order the Minister of Commerce to control the price of oil in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that political stability and macroeconomic stability are two-tiered ties that must be maintained.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also thanked all journalists' associations for their efforts to promote the press.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked all ministries and institutions for their efforts to promote their work.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Senior Minister Sun Chanthol for answering directly to the media. * Samdech Techo Hun Sen wants to see all senior ministers follow the example of Senior Minister Sun Chanthol.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that officials who do not know computer must also know how to use smartphones to work effectively.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen calls on journalists to join in maintaining peace. If the country is at war, it can not open the media.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that everyone needs peace, so let's keep the peace together.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the media to participate in maintaining stability and social security by participating in promoting the policy of safe villages and communes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that participating in preventing drug use, preventing traffic accidents is participating in promoting the policy of safe villages and communes.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that retaliation against false information is a contribution to maintaining social stability.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the media to participate in maintaining peace, stability, social order and macroeconomic stability.
* Samdech Techo stated that in order to maintain peace, social stability, social order and macroeconomic stability, all journalists must work together to prevent false information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen asks national and sub-national institutions to have a clear mechanism for information issues.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Minister, the Governor, the Provincial Governor must be the highest responsible person in releasing information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Senior Minister Sun Chanthol and some provincial governors for their active response to the media.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the media to understand the Minister, the Governor, who are too busy to respond to the reporters during the meeting.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen tells officials not to consider journalists as enemies, but to consider them as indispensable partners.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech has been considered a star on the news page since 1982.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that journalists are the ones who made Samdech known in the world.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech was a little relieved after his mother-in-law recovered from his illness.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the Minister and the Provincial Governor, if necessary, to come forward and explain directly.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen requested the media and journalists to act as a bridge between the Royal Government and the people.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that journalists should not only help disseminate policies, but should also monitor the implementation of those policies.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges more and more journalists to participate in the fight against inactivity, corruption and social injustice.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that social injustice affects social stability and armed conflict.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that he had ordered Mr. Keo Remy and General Sao Sokha to investigate the death in Banteay Meanchey province, which was claimed to have been the result of torture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that if people are tortured to death, they must be arrested and punished.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that a society without injustice is a society that leads to harmony.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the perpetrators of injustice will be reduced when there is publicity.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continues to call on journalists to join the fight against fake news by releasing true information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that it is necessary to prepare for the completion of the online broadcast to the digital system by 2023.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the law on the right to information will be issued in 2020.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen proposes to train human resources in the field of information, both knowledge and professional ethics.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that when Samdech ends his political life, he will become a professor of journalism.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has decided not to charge for the use of frequencies at the request of the Minister of Information.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to provide Samdech's volunteer lawyer to help defend the media, but to examine the facts appropriately.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the journalists from all walks of life who participated in the solidarity meal.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has declared January 14 as the day of the meeting between Samdech and journalists every year.
