Samdech Prime Minister: Hun Manet, despite his ability to become Prime Minister, must wait for the time and go through the election (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, said that although Hun Manet, who is The eldest son of Samdech is qualified to be the Prime Minister, but also has to wait until 2028, 2029 or until 2030 and will have to go through elections.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's remarks came after some media outlets reported that Samdech Techo Hun Sen was preparing for his son, Hun Manet, to take over the post of Prime Minister soon.
Speaking at the Solidarity Meeting and Dinner with a total of nearly 6,000 journalists in Koh Pich on the night of January 14, 2020, Samdech Techo Hun Sen "I need another 10 years to be the Prime Minister of the Kingdom of Cambodia Therefore, Manet, if qualified, must wait until after 2028 or 2029 or until 2030 to be able to participate in the role of Prime Minister.
At this point, Samdech Techo Prime Minister asked that if the father is already the Prime Minister, where can the son come to seize power from the father?
Samdech continued that Cambodia is a democracy, not a country that transfers power from father to son in one way or another, as in some countries it is through elections.
According to Samdech Techo, Mr. Hun Manet is still young compared to his colleagues. "So, of course, we have to think about how to solve our internal problems, so commentators, analysts, give common sense and do not turn this issue into something else," he said.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also mentioned the intentions of the wicked who intended to slander Hun Manet's reputation to the point of daring to insult him as the son of a Vietnamese leader. Samdech has announced that he will not tolerate those who insult his wife and children.
"Hun Manet, despite the possibility, has to go through an election. "Even in the government, I do not let them in the government, their ability to be a minister or secretary of state, but I leave them outside." Samdech underlined further.
