The guarantee for this work comes after criticism from residents and tourists over the view of the grassland around the Angkor Wat temple, which is drying up.
APSARA Authority spokesman Long Kosal confirmed that the APSARA Authority will set up an automatic irrigation system that will water the grass green throughout the rainy season and this work will be completed in 2020.
In addition, APSARA Authority will set up a hospitality center for tourists, proper parking, security, order and replanting of trees to improve the environment there to be a World Heritage Site.
He said that, in fact, the team is cutting branches that affect the landscape of the temple as a criticism of tourists to improve the green landscape in the south of Angkor Wat, water in the south pond and so on. Therefore, what the APSARA Authority is doing is to improve the beauty of public order and increase the attractiveness for tourists not only Angkor Wat, but Angkor as a whole.
