(Phnom Penh): A man known as a factory worker killed the victim, his girlfriend, in a rented room, then the suspect hanged himself, but did not die. The incident happened at 8:00 AM on January 14, 2020 in Room 7 near Boeung Salang Market, Boeung Salang Village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
The assailant was named Hoy Phalla, alias Ta Chek, male, 26 years old, factory worker, living in a rented room with the victim and was born in Thla Prachum commune, Koh Andet district, Takeo province. The victim, Sok Sim, alias Apov, a 20-year-old female factory worker, lived in Room 7, Boeung Salang Village, Sangkat Russey Keo, Phnom Penh, and was born in Udom Village, Udom Commune, Peam Chor District, Prey Veng Province.
Later, my cousin left the factory and came back to this room when she saw that the room was locked. Suddenly, the cousin shouted to the neighbors for help, and then a man, a motodup driver who lived next door, pulled out a stick to hit the door of the apartment above. Seeing the victim lying next to the suspect, seeing the above suspect hanged himself.
The victim was taken by his family on a three-wheeler to Calmette Hospital, but unfortunately the woman died. The suspect was rushed to Calmette Hospital as his condition worsened.
At present, the body of the victim was handed over to the family by the authorities to be taken to the traditional funeral in her hometown. The suspect was guarded at the hospital. General Sao Sokha Opens a Training Course for Gendarmerie at Phnom Chum Reay Gendarmerie Training Center in Kampong Chhnang Province
