(Kampong Cham): A sand barge driving carelessly crashed into a fishing boat, injuring one person and losing some property. This incident happened on the evening of January 12, 2020 along the river in the first village, Koh Sotin commune, Koh Sotin district, Kampong Cham province.
According to the local police officer, the accident occurred on the Mekong River on the shores of Koh Thmey, and after the provocation, the driver of the stone ferry ran to Chi Roth I commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province, but was forced to do so. Kampong Cham Provincial Waterway Traffic Office detained at the waterway traffic station.
After receiving the information, the specialized force of Koh Sotin District Police Inspectorate arrived at the scene in cooperation with the Koh Sotin Administrative Police Force to investigate the case of a water traffic accident between a ferry carrying stones and a fishing boat. Naroth, 16 years old, in Russey Char village, Thmey Kre commune, Chit Borey district, Kratie province.
According to the police, the driver of the ferry was careless and caused the accident. The victim, Matt Sakiros, was injured and taken to Kampong Cham Provincial Hospital, where a small fishing boat was damaged and some property was lost. Currently, the specialized force has taken the ferry to be stored at the waterway traffic station for legal settlement.
