(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, said that compared to the social security system in ASEAN countries that follow the social security management system, the social security contribution rate in Cambodia is still lower than other countries. Other in the region, which is a special factor for attracting investment for Cambodia.
This statement was made by Mr. Ith Sam Heng at the opening ceremony of the meeting to review the work results of 2019 and the work direction for 2020 of the National Social Security Fund (NSSF) on the morning of January 14, 2020 at the hotel. Airport star.
On that occasion, Mr. Ith Sam Heng said that the Royal Government has made continuous efforts to develop and expand the social protection system with solidarity and social equity for the people to prevent financial risk, ensure stability and sustainability, income and health promotion. Globalization and reduction of social inequality.
In this spirit, the promulgated Social Security Law covers four areas: pensions, health care, occupational risk and unemployment, for individuals in the public sector and under the Labor Law. Including air force, seafarers and housemaids, as well as self-employed individuals.
In fact, the Ministry of Labor has already launched a social security system for occupational risk and health care, which from 2019 will cover both workers and public officials.
The Minister said that the implementation of the social security system in each sector is very important to contribute to the achievement of national economic growth, including:
* Provision of medical treatment and care, including measures to protect the health of workers and their family members. Occupational health, safety and hygiene measures are also developed to prevent workplace accidents through prevention and outreach programs.
* Provision of maternity leave, which is one of the goals in promoting the rules for the development of human resources that can sustain the economy as well as stabilize economic growth.
* Provision for permanent disability benefits for workers at risk of employment is a mechanism to prevent all persons with disabilities from falling into the poverty line, which is the sole responsibility of the government.
* The provision of rehabilitation services through the social security system is also promoted for workers with disabilities who may have the opportunity to re-employ or be able to engage in any work according to their disability status.
Establishing a social security system for pensions for the private sector is about maintaining the stability of the transitions between the public and private sectors through the establishment of a system that can maintain seniority. Retirement benefits are also a mechanism to ensure income sustainability as they reach old age, without relying on the support of family members.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng added that these achievements reflect more clearly the development of the Cambodian social protection system to a system that is universal and consistent, which maintains the effectiveness of the above work. Regular.
