(Phnom Penh): The police of the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police on the morning of January 14, 2020, sent 2 suspects, the first: Kim Va and the second: Keo Sothea and drugs. Confiscated 9.6 kg of methamphetamine (ICE) to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court to be handed over to the Prosecutor's Office for investigation and legal charges.
It should be noted that the Anti-Drug Department of the General Commission of the National Police launched a large-scale operation to crack down on drug dealers in Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh and Thpong District, Kampong Speu Province, confiscating more than 9 kilograms of drugs.
A senior official of the Anti-Drug Department told Fresh News that the operation took place on the evening of January 10, 2020 at the point of house no. Omlaing Commune, Thpong District, Kampong Speu Province.
The crackdown took place on the orders of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner General, Gen. Mak Chito, Deputy Commissioner General, and Lt. Gen. Lek Vannak, Director of the Anti-Drug Department, under the coordination of Prosecutor Kham Sophary and led the operation. Directed by Major General Kheng Sarath, Deputy Director of the Anti-Drug Department.
The official added that as a result, the police arrested two suspects, Kim Va and Keo Sothea, and confiscated 9.6 kilograms of methamphetamine (ICE), two vehicles, and a scale. 2 units and 2 telephones.
A police officer revealed that in the case of a large-scale crackdown of up to 10 kilograms, the two people were arrested and were trying to run to help the suspects.
