(Sihanoukville): Building a clean government is essential to create a better investment climate. The Anti-Corruption Unit and the Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Sihanoukville on January 13, 2020 jointly organized a lecture on "Anti-Corruption Law" for Chinese enterprises and administrative officials of the Special Economic Zone in Preah Sihanouk Province. Sihanouk to create a better investment climate.
Senior Minister Om Yentieng, Head of the Anti-Corruption Unit, addressed the gathering, which was attended by officials from the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone Administration and nearly 100 factory representatives.
Chen Jiangang, President of the Cambodian-Chinese Chamber of Commerce in Sihanoukville and Chairman of the Board of Directors of the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone Company, said that the lecture was very valuable for promoting and improving the business environment. Of members of Chinese associations and enterprises investing in Cambodia.
The president of the association also emphasized that the association will actively support the work of the Cambodian Anti-Corruption Unit. He believes that under the leadership of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the efforts of the Anti-Corruption Unit, Cambodia will soon have a clean environment for Chinese enterprises.
In his speech, Senior Minister Om Yentieng said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen pays great attention to the work of the Office of Administration and Development in the Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone. Sihanoukville Special Economic Zone has absorbed 30,000 workers and the number is expected to increase to 40,000 by 2020. Especially after the completion of construction will provide 80,000 to 100,000 job opportunities.
The senior minister said that this year's anti-corruption work plan is important to raise awareness about the services of civil servants and fight corruption and bribery.
At Hun Sen's urging, the Anti-Corruption Unit will focus on the development of Chinese companies in Sihanoukville and protect their legitimate rights and interests in order to attract more Chinese investors to invest in Sihanoukville. Sihanoukville Province. This was further confirmed by the head of the Anti-Corruption Unit.
