The following is the full text of the Royal Government's decision: Minister Pan Sosak: Support the political message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen: "Thank you for the peace" that has invaluable value in the past, today and in the future.
(Kampong Cham): Speaking at the Inauguration Ceremony of the School and Achievements at Wat Komarach, Boeung Nay Commune, Prey Chhor District, Kampong Cham Province this morning, January 13, 2020, Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and Chairman of the Working Group The local people in Prey Chhor and Batheay districts have expressed their full support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's political message, "Thank you for the peace," which is invaluable in the past, today and in the future.
Taking this opportunity, Minister Pan Sosak thanked and highly appreciated the efforts of the Boeung Nay Commune Working Group, which spent a lot of time and resources to support and develop the commune, including supporting postpartum women and their families. Disability, old age, lack of hope, repair of road systems, canals, schools and pagodas.
At the same time, the Minister also highlighted the many great achievements that emerged from the efforts of the Royal Government to implement the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Political Program and Strategy for the Sixth Legislature, which was launched in September 2018 by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Director The Minister of Cambodia has made such proud achievements:
Peace, political stability, security and public order are firmly guarded, so that the people can live in peace and harmony.
* The deep and comprehensive process of state reform is being pursued with a sharp and more effective will, especially public administration reform, public financial management reform, decentralization and deconcentration reform, legal and judicial reform, and the fight. Anti-corruption.
* Peace and political stability have laid a solid foundation for Cambodia's economic development process to achieve high growth of about 7.1% in the context of low inflation, stable exchange rates and continued international reserves.
* Based on the achievements of the economic sector and the distribution of the fruits of equitable growth in the whole social framework, improve the living standards of the people, which is reflected by the increase in GDP per capita from 1, $ 548 in 2018 to about $ 1,679 in 2019. The poverty rate has been reduced to below 10 percent and the unemployment rate is only 0.3 percent.
Minister Pan Sosak added that peace only guarantees sustainable development and the peaceful and prosperous life of the people, peace only guarantees the stability and growth of democracy and freedom, and the success of the development process and resilience. Of democracy will have a return effect, ensuring the sustainability of peace. If we lose peace, we will lose everything.
On that occasion, Mr. Pan Sosak called on civil servants, the armed forces and all the people to participate in the protection of peace, which we have achieved with the utmost difficulty, to be strong and stable, not to allow any reaction force Can be destroyed, no matter what the price.
