High-level delegation from the National Assembly of Cambodia attends 4-day APPF Women's Committee Meeting in Australia
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ban Srey Mom, Member of the National Assembly and Vice Chairwoman of the National Assembly's Committee on Education, Youth, Sports, Cult, Religious Affairs, Culture and Tourism, attended the 28th Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Women's Committee Meeting at the Australian Parliament in Canberra this afternoon. January 13, 2020.
The Australian Parliament is hosting the 28th APPF Annual Meeting under the theme "Parliamentary Partnership for 2020 and Next." The Women's Committee Meeting is one of the meetings of the APPF Annual Meeting, such as the Committee on Economic Security, Regional Cooperation. These meetings will run from January 13 to 16, 2020.
The Women's Committee discussed three draft resolutions to promote gender equality. Ms. Ban Srey Mom highlighted the efforts of the Royal Government and the Cambodian Parliament to promote women. The Royal Government has encouraged the participation of women in all fields, including politics, society and the economy.
The 27-member parliament includes Australia, the Kingdom of Cambodia, China, Japan, the Republic of Korea, Mongolia, the Russian Federation, Indonesia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam, Fiji, Macedonia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, the Marcel Islands, Canada, Chile, Colombia, Ecuador, Costa Rica, and the United States.
