New Swedish Ambassador vows to further improve labor cooperation with Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): In a meeting with Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, this morning, January 13, 2020, Mr. Björn Häggmark, the new Ambassador of Sweden to Cambodia, expressed his commitment to continue cooperation. Better operations and vocational training, especially on the many development projects underway in Cambodia.
At the same time, the two sides praised the past good cooperation in the field of employment and vocational training and pledged to further strengthen this good cooperation to help develop employment and training. Profession, which is an important area to ensure the harmonization of professional relations and social development.
The new Swedish Ambassador has pledged to continue labor and vocational training projects between Cambodia and Sweden, including development projects carried out through SIDA that have assisted the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, including the establishment of a job center. In the capitals and provinces.
Cambodia has been actively supporting the Swedish Government's Global Deal, a global initiative that aims to jointly address challenges in the labor market and promote universal access. Benefits of globalization.
Mr. Ith Sam Heng stated that after Cambodia provided support for the Global Agreement Initiative on February 16, 2018, the Ministry of Labor:
* Continue to strengthen effective implementation and amend labor laws to meet the need to ensure better working conditions and harmony in professional relations.
* Strengthen the implementation of the Law on Trade Unions to ensure the rights and freedoms of professional organizations that represent the true voice and will of workers and employers to protect their legitimate rights and interests and be an effective dialogue partner in Social dialogue.
Strengthen the implementation of the Minimum Wage Law, which is a strong legal framework for the sustainable protection of workers 'wages and ensures the democratic use of tripartite negotiation mechanisms in determining workers' minimum wages based on Scientific criteria for progress together.
Strengthen the mechanism for resolving labor disputes more effectively, both in the reconciliation phase of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training and out-of-court settlement by the Arbitration Council, to ensure fairness of work, reduce challenges between employers and workers, or Their representation also enhances trust in the system of dispute resolution between stakeholders, which further strengthens the culture of social dialogue.
* Continue to strengthen the labor inspection mechanism of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to be more effective, transparent and credible from all stakeholders to ensure respect for working conditions and labor rights of workers and employers to prevent as well as prevent other problems. Leading to disputes and protests.
* Promote the implementation of policies to protect the rights and interests of migrant workers, both within the national as well as regional and with relevant countries to protect Cambodian workers working abroad.
