A 50-year-old woman was killed in an apartment in Borey in Chak Angre Krom Sangkat, Meanchey District, the suspect was arrested
(Phnom Penh): A 50-year-old woman was found dead in her house on the evening of January 12, 2020 in a Borey in Chak Angre Krom commune, Meanchey district.
Sources from the family of the body said that before the incident, they called the victim on the morning of January 12, 2020, but no one picked up, suddenly at around 3 pm the same day, someone called to tell the owner Lost in the house and made them go home. When they arrived, they found the real body, making them, the family very sad.
The family was not satisfied because they saw that the woman's death was suspicious, so they immediately reported to the police force. Take something and hold it over your face until you suffocate to death.
After learning that the woman had been killed, the victim's family suspected that the friend who was with the victim was the perpetrator because the two often had quarrels with each other. Died for questioning at Chak Angre Leu police station to arrest the perpetrator.
The deceased was identified as Ngin Sokly, 50, a moneylender and coffee seller around the Depot Market, who also lost some of her property.
After the autopsy, the body was handed over to the family for a traditional ceremony. The friend who was staying with her was detained by the police and taken to Chak Angre Krom police station for questioning to find out who the real killer was.
Victims of Khmer civilization: Why do the US and Iran have no diplomatic ties?
In this conflict, in terms of diplomatic relations between the two countries do not exist. Why do the US and Iran have no diplomatic ties?
Khmer civilization expert Rath Sandab said that the conflict between the United States and Iran, which currently has no diplomatic ties, is due to many different issues, but the main objection is from the oil interests. In 1979. This means that before 1979, the United States and Iran were good allies and had good diplomatic ties.
Because at that time, all of Iran's oil products were privately owned by the private sector, and the United States was the most lucrative shareholder in these oil companies.
Mr. Rath Sandab stated that based on this oil revolution policy and affected all oil companies have lost all benefits since then.
If so, it is at this point that the United States and Iran will not look at each other until the severance of diplomatic ties from 1980 to the present.
