Promote the spirit of loving and caring for trees! National Bank of Cambodia and CIMB Bank Plant 100 Koki Trees in Kampong Thmor High School, Kampong Thom Province
The planting of Koki trees on the campus was led by Ms. Chea Serey, Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, and several staff members of Kampong Thmor High School in Kampong Thmor Commune, Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province on January 11, 2020.
Ms. Chea Serey said that the tree planting gathering is now a joint effort to raise the spirit of loving and caring for trees and forests through new plantations to make the school grounds more beautiful and shady. To the school as well as provide shade for students to take refuge and relax.
"Trees are very useful for all living organisms on the planet, people, animals, and plants, and to sustain the forest, if all people take advantage of these natural forests with care and attention," she said. Responsible for the loss and survival of forests, ecosystems and biodiversity.
She stated that through joint activities, this time shows the contribution to the policy of the Royal Government on the management, protection, conservation and sustainable development of forests in Cambodia. Today's gathering is a symbol of unity, solidarity and cooperation for the cause of building, protecting and developing the motherland of Cambodia to be more prosperous.
Ms. Chea Serey said that at present, young people are actively involved in economic and social development, which shows that young people have a more important role in building a motherland with a spirit of unity and high responsibility. For the nation.
Ms. Chea Serey informed the students about the benefits of the forest that in one hectare of forest can emit 2.7 tons of oxygen, 1 ton of recycled paper, can save 17 trees equal to 1,400 liters of oil, which is equivalent to 4,000 watts of electricity and 27,000 liters of water.
On that occasion, CIMB Bank sponsored Kampong Thmor High School. This support was provided through Ms. Chea Serey, including: 1 water pump, 1 lawn mower and study materials for 216 12th grade students to take the exam.
In that, Ms. Chea Serey also sponsored 12 sets of bowls to improve the quality of petanque.
