Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin Leads a Parliamentary Delegation to Attend the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Annual Meeting in Australia
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of Cambodia, on the evening of January 11, 2020, led a high-level delegation of the National Assembly of Cambodia to attend the 28th Annual Meeting of the Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum (APPF). In Canberra, Australia, at the invitation of the President of the Australian Legislature.
At the forum, which was attended by parliamentarians from more than 30 countries, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin will address the opening ceremony of the 27th official meeting of the President of the APPF, which was hosted by the Cambodian Parliament in early 2019. The Australian Parliament also invited the Cambodian Parliament to share its experience in leading and organizing the 27th APPF Meeting of the Executive Committee.
During his meeting in Australia, the National Assembly President plans to hold bilateral talks with his Australian counterpart and hold talks with parliamentary leaders of other friendly countries to strengthen ties and cooperation between the two countries' parliamentary diplomacy. On the international stage, both multilateral and bilateral frameworks.
National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin is scheduled to meet with Cambodian people and students living and studying in Canberra, Australia.
Other members of the delegation will attend meetings of various APPF committees, including the Political and Security Committee, the Economic Committee, the Women's Parliamentary Committee and the Joint Proclamation Committee, the Regional Cooperation Committee, to exchange experiences with each other. On draft resolutions that address common issues in the areas of security, economy, society and environment.
The 27-nation parliament is composed of Australia, the Kingdom of Cambodia, China, Japan, the Republic of Korea, Mongolia, the Russian Federation, Indonesia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam, Fiji, Macedonia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, the Marshall Islands, Canada, Chile, Colombia, Mexico, Costa Rica, and the United States.
