70 years of Cambodia-US relations are more bitter than sweet
(Phnom Penh): By 2020, it has been 70 years since Cambodia and the United States were connected. The US Embassy in Cambodia this week hosted a series of events to celebrate the anniversary of the relationship between the two countries.
Patrick Muffy, US Ambassador to Cambodia, hosted a celebration of Diplomatic Day with the participation of Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation, civil servants, diplomats, investors and You are also a journalist. The Ambassador also organized a tricycle program in Phnom Penh.
In addition, it was observed that the Ambassador met with the Minister of Cambodia in various ministries and institutions to express the intention and commitment to strengthen relations and cooperation between the United States and the ministries and institutions that are the staff of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
Through these activities, the US Ambassador to Cambodia seems to be trying to express his intention that the United States wants good relations with Cambodia, which is a good sign for the relationship between Cambodia and the United States.
Although the current gestures and actions of the US Ambassador seem to indicate the intention to bring good relations with Cambodia. But if you look at the past 70 years, the relationship between Cambodia and the Co-Ministers is more bitter than sweet.
On the occasion of the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the United States and Cambodia, the US Ambassador praised Cambodia's progress and acknowledged that Cambodia has made great progress over the past two decades. The Ambassador hopes that the United States and Cambodia will continue to move forward together.
The US Ambassador also said that the US-Cambodia relationship for the past 70 years has not been easy, it is also problematic, but will focus on the areas of cooperation that will help promote this cooperation. Good and help Cambodia to prosper.
Patrick Muffy emphasized that the United States and Cambodia have a good foundation for cooperation, so the two countries will focus on this foundation to further develop US-Cambodian relations.
* In the first half of 2019, the trade volume between Cambodia and the United States amounted to $ 2.195 million, of which Cambodia exported $ 1.891 million, while the United States imported only $ 304 million.
In early 2018, the US government of President Donald Trump signed a law to extend the Generalized System of Preferences (GSP) for another three years to Cambodia from January 1, 2018 to December 31, 2020. .
