(Phnom Penh): Following the outbreak of unidentified pneumonia in Wuhan, Hubei Province, China, as an urgent measure for Cambodia to prevent this deadly disease, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia has installed heat scanners at the international airport. Cambodia's three are Phnom Penh, Sihanoukville and Siem Reap.
In addition, the Ministry of Health has set up separate wards at the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital, Sihanoukville Provincial Hospital and Siem Reap Provincial Hospital, with the necessary medical equipment and medicines for treatment.
In addition, the Ministry also informed the National Hospital and the 25 Health Departments of the Capital-Provinces to be ready to respond and provide immediate intervention in case of suspicion and are strengthening the work to monitor acute respiratory diseases and Regularly checked for abnormal patterns of the disease.
According to the World Health Organization, so far there has been no evidence of human-to-human transmission and no transmission to health workers. Experts are now gathering more epidemiological and laboratory information to identify the virus.
As of 8 a.m. on January 5, 2020, Wuhan Province reported a total of 59 patients with unidentified viral pneumonia, seven of whom were seriously ill and Others are in that situation. At present, all patients are being treated in isolation and no deaths.
Currently, the Ministry of Health of Cambodia is continuing to monitor the status of the disease in the region, in close consultation with the World Health Organization in Cambodia, and so far no cases of such diseases have occurred in Cambodia.
At the same time, Prof. Mam Bunheng, Minister of Health, also called on travelers traveling to or from Wuhan, Hubei Province, People's Republic of China to take the utmost care to take care of their personal health by taking measures. Some simple.
