Undocumented fish truck causes almost fatal accident and threatens to sue the authorities if the fish die in Stung Sen city, Kampong Thom province
(Kampong Thom): A five-wheeled truck carrying ten undocumented fish caused a traffic accident, seriously injuring one person, and the car owner even threatened to sue the authorities if his fish died.
After the incident, the land traffic police and the police force of the Economic Crimes Bureau of Kampong Thom Provincial Police arrived at the scene to measure until they stopped the exhibits and asked for documents to continue the legal procedure. Suddenly, the son of the fish owner handed over the phone to his father and boss That the owner of the rental car did not know the owner and even threatened that if the fish died, he would complain to the authorities who went to work directly.
According to people in the province, this case of illegal transport is not new, it is always transported every day with about 3 or 4 heavy vehicles using a single permit with your car. Run.
Experts revealed that the fish shipped out of Vietnam, which, in principle, the law on transport is that all vehicles must be accompanied by a transport license with a vehicle with a license plate and a clear owner has a letter from the border (PC).
Authorities stated that the fish owners threatened such authorities because there were people behind the intervention.
It should be noted that in Kampong Thom province, not only illegal fish are transported, even chickens imported from Thailand are almost entirely goods that do not meet the legal requirements of the Royal Government, all of which are questionable. Doubt the public that "it is a culture of intervention or the authorities conspired with the perpetrators."
