(Phnom Penh): General Vong Pisen, Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF), on the afternoon of January 10, 2020, paid a courtesy call on the new and old Chiefs of Staff of the old and new Chinese military attachés in the courtroom.
On that occasion, General Vong Pisen praised the achievements of Lt. Col. Lin Ningya, a former Chinese military attaché in the past, and believed that in the future, under the leadership of Colonel Li Jingfeng, The new military attaché in Cambodia will continue to run smoothly to further strengthen the friendship, solidarity and cooperation between the two governments, armies and peoples.
The Commander-in-Chief expressed his deep gratitude to the People's Republic of China for its continuous assistance to Cambodia, including in the field of Chinese military assistance, both in terms of facilities and training of human resources every year. Prove that China is always close to Cambodia.
In response, Lt. Col. Linya thanked the Commander-in-Chief for giving him valuable time to pay a courtesy call and appear before the new Chief of the Joint Chiefs of Staff.
Colonel Lin Ningya emphasized that over the past five years, he has been very pleased to have contributed to the development of better cooperation between the two armies, especially as a comprehensive strategic partner. This good result also depends on the attention, support and full cooperation of the Commander-in-Chief.
Colonel Li Jingfeng, director of the new military attaché office, said that in the new context of brotherly relations, the two countries' armies have a lot in common, especially the army is made up of people and does things for the people. .
On that occasion, Colonel Li Jingfeng also expressed his commitment in front of the Commander-in-Chief that in carrying out his diplomatic mission in Cambodia, he will do his best to push for The steel-like friendship between the two countries has further strengthened and expanded.
(Phnom Penh): "Personal special license plate" is just an additional option for car users, although there are "personal special license plate", normal license plate is still available for general car users. Car owners are not required to use a "personal special license plate". This was confirmed by Ms. Koy Sodany, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport.
"Personal Special License Plate", a new type of license plate that allows license plate owners to manage for life, was officially launched by the Ministry of Public Works and Transport on January 7, 2020. After the announcement, some people mistakenly thought that car owners were required to buy more of this type of license plate, which would make it more expensive for car owners.
This "personal special license plate", although some people have reacted or criticized on various issues. But also get support and buy from some car owners. According to Ms. Koy Sodani, after just two days of announcing the sale, there were up to 42 buyers and received about $ 220,000. The proceeds from the sale of the license plate are set aside for the national budget to cover state spending.
The license plate costs from 2 million riel up to 1 billion riel, but for the auction may be more. This "personal special number plate" can select and name as desired. Except for inappropriate words, names of leaders and historical locations. For prices, 8-digit numbers or characters are cheaper, but the smaller the number or characters, the more expensive the price.
This "personal special license plate" can be purchased for life by simply deleting the name when selling the car or they can sell the license plate when selling the car. The owner of the license plate can also keep the license plate for the children by simply exchanging information about who will continue to control the license plate. Senior Minister Kun Kim Recognizes the President and Vice President of the Cambodian Veterans Association in Pailin Province
