(Phnom Penh): On January 10, 2020, at the meeting hall of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, a workshop was held on the progress of the implementation of the strategic plan to prevent human trafficking and accidents caused by illegal drug use under the chairmanship of Mr. Sar Sokha. Secretary of State, Representative of Dr. Hang Chuon Naron, Minister of Education, Youth and Sports.
The event was also attended by the Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, the General Secretariat of the National Anti-Drug Authority and the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, and representatives of departments, units, members of the Anti-Drug Committee and Anti-trafficking in education in the 25 capitals and provinces.
On that occasion, Ms. Dr. Soeur Socheata, Undersecretary of State, Chair of the Anti-Drug and Anti-Human Trafficking Task Force at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, made a report on the progress of drug prevention and trafficking in order to strengthen the quality and efficiency of human resources in Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Samorn Bandith, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Information, stated that the information sector plays an important role in disseminating information on general knowledge and laws related to drug and human trafficking issues to the people.
Meanwhile, Lt. Gen. Pon Samkhan, Secretary General of the National Committee for Combating Human Trafficking, said that human trafficking is a transnational crime committed by organized organizations that are required to fight, prevent and rescue victims. Trading in all forms.
At the same time, General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, congratulated the progress and thanked the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and relevant ministries for participating in the fight against drugs for the common purpose of Build effective human resources as a potential resource for the nation.
In the interest of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports of Koh Kong, Banteay Meanchey, Battambang, Prey Veng, Phnom Penh, Kandal and Plan Plan, all of them have expressed their willingness to participate in preventing drug and human trafficking for the future of our children.
Mr. Sar Sokha thanked all stakeholders for their active participation in the fight against drugs, drug prevention and human trafficking, and requested all relevant authorities, Youth, Red Cross Scouts, Artists, and MCs. Civil society workers, please continue to participate actively and regularly like the early rain for the safety of the community.
