Kampong Thom MP: Peace is the most important factor in making the country grow and develop
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Nong Veasna, Member of Parliament for Kampong Thom Constituency and Chairman of Sandan District Assistance Team, Kampong Thom Province, this morning, January 10, 2020, participated in the celebration of the 41st Anniversary of the 7th January Victory Day. January 1979 - January 2020) in Sandan district with the participation of many members and people.
Speaking at the ceremony, Mr. Nong Veasna said that January 7, 2020 is the 41st anniversary of the historic January 7, 1979 Victory Day, which overthrew the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, the National Rescue and the Cambodian people. Resurrected from the massacre of the most brutal regime in time and ended the darkest era of Cambodia and opened a new era of independence, freedom, democracy and social progress.
Mr. Nong Veasna said that it was only on January 7, 1979 that things became as they are today, which brought peace to the whole country and there were examples for many countries such as Singapore, Japan, Thailand, Korea and other countries. China and so on. Therefore, Mr. Nong Veasna asked the Cambodian people, especially the people in Sandan district, to join in maintaining the peace that has been achieved through this difficulty for thousands of years to come.
"Peace is the most important factor in the development of the country, thanks to peace," he said.
He also called on the people to commemorate the achievements and sacrifices of the national liberators who liberated Cambodia from the genocidal regime until it is as successful and peaceful as it is today.
He stated that to celebrate the 41st anniversary of the January 7 victory, which is as peaceful as it is today, he also installed solar lanterns on the streets of the park and along the Sen River, as well as on the Hun Sen Bridge in Sandan district and installed lanterns. In Tamring commune, which is a remote commune, 95 kilometers from Kampong Thom provincial town.
He added that in Tamring commune, which was born from the achievement of peace under the guidance of Samdech Techo Hun Sen in the early 2001 to establish a core economic zone of rubber from rubber plantations and processing plants that can be set up. A rubber industry for Kampong Thom province.
He added that now Tamring commune has become a commune with a high economy and a prosperous people, and all these achievements are born of peace, thank you for peace and keep the peace.
