Phnom Penh Military sends a suspect to court
(Phnom Penh): On January 10, 2020, the competent authorities of the Criminal Investigation Office of the Phnom Penh Municipal Gendarmerie sent a suspect to court to be punished according to the law related to breach of trust.
The suspect, Khin Chhay, 30 years old, was arrested by the Sen Sok District Armed Forces on January 6, 2020 at 7:10 AM at JYAC Company, Street 1984, Phnom Penh Thmey Village, Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. The company owner filed a complaint.
After his arrest, the suspect confessed that he joined JW Asia in 2013 as a manager, air conditioner and received a salary of $ 400 per month.
Until November 2018, he went to install air conditioners for customers, until he never gave money to the company after customers paid for air conditioning installation and repair costs, he spent For personal gain, a total of 3,330 US dollars, with a lot of losses, the company called him for questioning and also complained to the military police in Sen Sok district to detain him.
Mongkul Borei district residents have water again, Senior Minister Kun Kim thanked the Minister of Water Resources and relevant authorities (Video inside) (Banteay Meanchey): About 8,000 families in Mongkul Borei district, Banteay Meanchey province have water again after officials and relevant authorities Together, pump water from the Serei Sophorn River into the Mongkul Borei River.
About 8,000 families in Mongkul Borei district have been facing water shortages in recent days after the Mongkul Borei River dried up. Immediately after seeing this threat, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources, arranged and sent a pump to pump water from the Serei Sophorn River into the Mongkul Borei River.
By the afternoon of January 10, 2020, water began to pump from the Serei Sophorn River into the Mongkul Borei River, and people can also draw water to use.
Senior Minister Kun Kim, First Vice-Chairman of the National Committee for Disaster Management, who was nicknamed "Senior Minister" because he flew from one place to another to solve the disaster this afternoon, went to the people's place. People also suffer from this drought.
The senior minister confirmed to Fresh News that people have now had water again by pumping water from the Serei Sophorn and other rivers into the Mongkul Borei River. The senior minister said that the team is currently monitoring and if people are still facing is to find a way to pump water from Boeung Kamping Kampouy in Battambang province.
However, Senior Minister Kun Kim called on the people of Mongkul Borei to download and use sparingly. The Senior Minister also asked for understanding and tolerance from the people in Mongkul Borei district not to continue to cultivate dry rice because it may lead to water shortage in this dry season.
