The Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SEC) signs a Memorandum of Understanding with Maybank within the framework of technical assistance for the development of the securities sector in Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SECC), said that the signing of a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) between Maybank Kim Eng Holding Limited and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to start cooperation Operating and providing technical assistance framework to promote the sustainable growth of the securities market in Cambodia is a good sign and image for overseas investors looking to invest in Cambodia.
The signing of the Memorandum of Understanding on "Cooperation and Technical Assistance Framework for the Development of the Securities Sector in Cambodia" took place on the afternoon of January 9, 2020.
Speaking at the press conference, Mr. Sou Socheat stated, "In order to lead local investment, we need professional investment and foreign investment is a real professional investment. Therefore, through the signing of the MoU between the Securities and Exchange Commission and Maybanks Bank in "Today is a good day to attract foreign investors to Cambodia."
"The banking system is very important in attracting foreign investors. If a country does not have a banking sector, all investors will not come to invest. Obviously, the securities sector operates on a solid foundation. Of the banking system.
"I am confident that today's MoU will further strengthen the relationship towards the partnership," he said. "This cooperation will help us to improve performance, promote the growth of the Cambodian securities market in the future and continue to contribute to the national economy."
"It is an honor to work with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia to develop the securities market in Cambodia," said Mohammed Yasin Abdullah, Chief Executive Officer of Maybank Kim Eng.
Maybank started its business in Cambodia in 1993 and is now one of the top 10 banks in Cambodia in terms of assets and has a network of 21 branches throughout Cambodia.
