(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction on January 10, 2020 issued a new instruction to all competent authorities in the field of construction to strengthen the quality and safety of construction.
In this new guideline, the Ministry strictly prohibits the implementation of five tasks, including:
1: It is strictly forbidden to build a building without a construction permit, repair or dismantling and a permit to open a construction site.
2. It is strictly forbidden to carry out construction or dismantling work by builders who do not have a license or a certificate of business license issued by the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction.
3. It is strictly forbidden for construction sites to be constructed or dismantled without the on-site engineers being responsible.
4: It is strictly forbidden to stay in the building under construction, even if it is temporary, and it is strictly forbidden for those who have no duty to enter the construction site.
5: Prohibit the use of all types of construction without a construction use certificate or construction permit issued by the competent authority.
In this instruction, the Ministry urges the competent authorities to pay attention to the implementation of five other principles and measures, including: construction permit, repair and dismantling, construction permit, construction site preparation, construction process and inspection work. And confirm construction.
Notably, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction issued a new guideline to improve the quality and safety of construction after the collapse of a building in Kep province last week, which caused 36 workers and children. One died and 23 were seriously injured.
The following are the new guidelines of the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction:
