The meeting was chaired by Dr. Steng Sokhom, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Task Force for Kamchay Mear District, with the participation of Kamchay Mear District Leaders, National Assistance Committees, District Party Committees and Commune Councils. Retired youth, school principals, citizens and all kinds of armed forces.
In this historic event, the people of Kamchay Mear district expressed their deepest gratitude to the leaders of the Cambodian People's Party for bringing peace and development to the country.
During the ceremony, Dr. Steng Sokhom read a meaningful speech on the historic January 7 Victory Day of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party and Prime Minister of Cambodia on the occasion of the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day. Phnom Penh to buy noodles.
He also highlighted some important points in Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech to emphasize to his compatriots, emphasizing the meaning of peace and development: "January 7 is the cause of peace in Cambodia, peace has brought Development.
"Today, even though the Cambodian people are living in harmony under the shadow of peace and development, we will always remember the most painful and dark past of the nation," he said. We are caused by the flames of war and the most heinous genocide.
Dr. Steng Sokhom recalled many of the merits of the January 7 Victory Day. The January 7 victory, which he highlighted, brought peace, freedom, as well as all rights to the Cambodian people, who had been completely lost under the genocidal regime of Pol Pot.
He also highlighted the recent situation in 2019, which he claimed was well developed despite some domestic problems and complex changes in the international situation. By. Moreover, what he wants to make clear is the issue of peace, political stability, security and public order, which is firmly guarded despite attempts to change the political regime in Cambodia.
For him, peace and political stability are the solid foundations of Cambodia's current economic development process. He stressed that through this peace, Cambodia has a golden opportunity for the development of its country to grow as it is today. This is a historical fact that no man or force can distort or destroy.
Even though 41 years have passed, the people of Kamchay Mear still remember the merits of January 7, the merits of all CPP leaders who led the country to peace and development.
The people of Kamchar Mear district are firmly committed to safeguarding the peace and achievements of the past 41 years and resolutely oppose any attempt to deprive Cambodia of peace. The people of Kamchay Mear district have clearly determined that January 7 is their second birthday, January 7 has really brought peace, January 7 has really brought national unity, January 7 has really brought Come to national development.
The people of Kamchay Mear district really gave the truth for January 7 and will remember it forever. This historic day is forever remembered in the memory of all people of all generations who love peace, freedom and justice. The people of Kamchay Mear district are committed to maintaining peace, peace, everything.
As a living witness to the war and the genocidal regime of Pol Pot, Dr. Steng Sokhom confirmed that January 7 is still a day of historical significance for the Cambodian nation throughout the country because everyone recognizes it. He said that anyone who denies "January 7" is denying his survival and that of his family.
Ang Mey Tinh closed with a happy atmosphere of solidarity and friendship with a solidarity meal in Kamchay Mear District Hall to celebrate the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day.
After attending the meeting to celebrate the anniversary of January 7, 2020, Dr. Steng Sokhom and his traveling companions inspected the construction of a dormitory for two teachers, one with two floors, 20 rooms and one with one floor. There are 10 rooms, canteen building in Hun Sen Kamchay Mear High School, donated by Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Interior.
Looking back at some countries, they are suffering the devastation of the horrors of war. The pictures we have seen of everyone these last few days are a practical example. Even the world's number one power, the United States, their soldiers and their families do not want to see war, because if there is war, death and destruction can happen at any time. Businesses or other jobs are also affected.
Therefore, while we are living in peace and enjoying the fruits of peace, we should love and help keep this peace from disappearing. And please do not wait until the time of war to value peace and want peace, because that is the desire that is too late, as the ancient Khmer proverb says, "When you see a coffin, you shed tears."
All in all, peace is the most precious thing for Cambodia. We also believe that every nation in the world longs for peace. But this desire is not always achieved.
So Cambodia, we have peace in our hands, should we let it go because of insults? Is absolutely impossible. The latest manifestation of the war must have left us devastated and increasingly valued the peace we are enjoying. May this tragedy be the spirit of maintaining the peace and well-being of the Khmer people forever! Thank you Peace! And thank you to those who brought peace to this poor country.
