(Phnom Penh): Oknha Try Pheap, CEO of Try Pheap Group and a personal adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party, expressed his admiration for Samdech Techo in the operation to rescue people from the collapse of buildings in Provinces last week.
During the rescue operation in Kep province last week, Mr. Try Pheap accompanied Samdech Techo in leading the rescue operation from the building to the end of the operation. Accompanying Samdech Techo Hun Sen to lead the operation made Mr. Try Pheap see firsthand Samdech Techo's management and determination to rescue the victims in that incident.
Mr. Try Pheap told the people that he was amazed at the spirit of Samdech Techo, a leader full of virtue and Brahma. Mr. Try Pheap told the people at the ceremony that Samdech was almost 70 years old, but because of his concern for the victims, he stayed up all night, could not sleep, could not stand his eyes, could not wait for food. Rescue the victims, both alive and dead, from the rubble.
Mr. Try Pheap described all the activities of Samdech Techo in the operation to the people to participate in the ceremony. Mr. Try Pheap told the people that it is very lucky for the Cambodian people that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a responsible leader and cares deeply about the well-being of the people.
Samdech Techo stayed at the site of the collapse until rescuers removed two surviving couples from the rubble. Despite sitting through the night, the eagerness to wait for the victims to get out of the piles did not make the head of government feel powerless or sleepy. When the two victims were removed from the building, Samdech Techo Hun Sen went out to receive the victims directly on the building.
After the victims were taken to the hospital, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also arrived at the hospital to monitor their health status. After the two victims were safe and there was no threat to their lives, Samdech Techo went to bed at around 5 am on January 4.
During the rescue operation under the collapsed building, it was seen that Samdech Techo Hun Sen and other government leaders, as well as the rescue team, had forgotten all their tiredness, focusing on Only important to rescue the victims.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen was observed that when he heard the rescue team confirming that they found the victim under the pile alive, his heart exploded and reminded the rescue team to do their best and speed up Rescue the victims as much as possible to save their lives. When victims leave the building, Samdech Techo always picks them up and then goes to the hospital to monitor their health.
In the 43-hour operation to rescue and dismantle the building, neither Samdech Techo Hun Sen nor other leaders, nor the rescue team, cared about sleeping or eating. Victim life.
The highly responsible actions of the head of the Royal Government in this rescue operation have been highly praised by the Cambodian people. The Cambodian people have said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen is a highly responsible leader and has taken care of the people first and foremost.
It should be noted that the rescue operation for the victims of the building collapse in Kep province took more than 43 hours with a force of nearly 2,000 rescuers and many other machines. There were 59 casualties, of which 36 were dead and 23 were alive.
