(Phnom Penh): The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries issued a new press release on January 9, 2020, highlighting the positive actions of the Ministry of Agriculture in cutting Reduce the number
Companies and quotas for importing live chickens from abroad to Cambodia.
The General Department said that seeing this situation, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has reduced the number of companies and the number of live chicken import quotas from Cambodia from 13 companies to 7 companies, from 44,000 per previous import. The day came to 17,000 per day.
The General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production stated that the results obtained after reducing the number of companies and the number of quotas for importing birds from abroad include:
Poultry farmers People poultry companies and the Cambodian Breeders 'Association support and appreciate the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries' action on reducing the number of companies and the number of live chicken import quotas to Cambodia. Domestic poultry production in all forms to balance prices, not affect farmers and help maintain labor and reduce migration
