The Cambodian people who survived the death knell of the Democratic Kampuchea regime always celebrated with great fanfare on the day of victory on January 7. The January 7 Victory Day celebration commemorates the heroism of the fighters and the sacrifices of the female warriors in the cause of national liberation from the Khmer Rouge genocidal regime.
