So far, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, under the direct command of Minister Lim Kean Hor and all relevant authorities, has been operating to pump water from other locations into the Mongkul Borei River and along the main canal to rescue. Temporarily.
He also claimed that the relevant authorities and the Ministry of Water Resources are now intervening as the water shortage is caused by people rushing to use too much water to supply their dry season rice, which is pumped beyond. The plan submitted by the provincial authorities has caused shortages.
In the face of this challenge, Chan Yutha, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology, who is leading the task force, told Fresh News that the Mongkol Borei River water source is now almost depleted. Gone can be used for at least another three days.
But at the same time, the Ministry has also found water sources from other districts to help supply, the Ministry has been installing water pumps to pump water from the Serei Sophorn River into a main canal and flow into the Mongkul Borei River. Overall, we can solve this challenge and not have the same challenges as in 2016.
In addition, Mr. Chan Yutha also advised the commune authorities to help protect this water source to avoid the cultivation of dry rice, because this water source is only for daily use because the dry season is still there. Long time no see.
On the morning of Wednesday, January 8, 2020, the Cambodian Red Cross delegation led by Mrs. Pum Chantyny, Secretary General of the Cambodian Red Cross, accompanied by the Branch Committee of the Youth District Sub-Branch. Condolences were shared with the families of the victims and a total of six victims, five dead and one injured, including one family with five members who died in Snuol Kong village, Boeung Pring commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province.
In this sad condolence, the Secretary-General brought the words of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia and the words of His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, who sent a message of sympathy and deep regret for the tragedy. That happened to all the families of the victims.
At the same time, she also expressed the highest consideration from the leaders at all levels, especially Samdech Techo Hun Sen, who always thinks about the well-being of all people at all times and everywhere.
At the same time, she offered her condolences to the bereaved families who lost their beloved children who sacrificed their physical and mental strength to work for a prosperous family life and prayed for the souls of the deceased to go to their deaths.
At the same time, she and her colleagues visited and handed over humanitarian donations to 21-year-old Soeuth Pei, who suffered head injuries in a building collapse in Kep province and is currently receiving treatment at his home in Snuol village. Kong, Boeung Pring commune, Thmor Kol district, Battambang province.
It should be noted that the noble gift of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, which gave the victim's family 2,000 USD, 360 kg of rice, 15 boxes of noodles, 150 cans of fish and 15 cases of orange juice.
Separately, the injured family received a royal gift of 2 boxes of noodles, 2 lots of milk, 4 kg of sugar, a mosquito net, a blanket, a sarong and a budget of $ 243.
The Cambodian Red Cross branch in Battambang province also shared the condolences and brought food, materials and money to the families of the victims.
