Santuk people celebrate 41st anniversary of January 7 Victory Day
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sou Sannisith, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Deputy Chairman of the Santuk District Assistance Team, organized a ceremony to celebrate the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day with nearly 2,000 participants.
Mr. Sou Sannisith said that because the values of peace have pushed Cambodia on the right path, which brings Cambodia peace and continuous development, and this peace and political stability has become a solid foundation of the economic development process. Cambodia has achieved a high growth rate of 7.1% in the context of low inflation, stable exchange rate and continued increase in international reserves.
"Obviously, growth is currently supported by better growth in the service sector and higher growth in the industrial sector, although the agricultural sector continues to grow slowly," he said. This political stability has given confidence to both domestic and foreign investors to invest in Cambodia, especially in the construction and manufacturing sectors.
With this, domestic consumption and international trade have increased significantly. In this context, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that with peace, only sustainable development and the peaceful and prosperous life of the peaceful people can ensure the stability and growth of democracy and freedom, and the success of the development process and The strength of democracy and, in turn, ensures the sustainability of peace.
