(Preah Vihear): The Cambodian Derivatives Exchange (CDX) and the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia and the Preah Vihear Provincial Administration jointly organized a workshop in Preah Vihear.
The workshop was organized by Mr. Sou Socheat, Director General of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, Mr. Kor Sum Bunsoeut, Deputy Governor of Preah Vihear Province.
The workshop was organized under the theme "What is Derivatives Trading: Investment Preparation and Relevant Awareness?" Provincial workshops aim to share knowledge, skills, experience, regulations and investment opportunities to the public in Cambodia.
Mr. Ko Subunsoeut highlighted the potential of Preah Vihear province and the attention of the Royal Government of Cambodia in the development of all sectors, especially the economic sector, which is reflected in the economic reforms that help Cambodia to grow economically. 7% per annum.
He added that through this workshop, participants are also expected to gain additional financial knowledge, especially in the derivatives market.
Mr. Sou Socheat also presented the current situation of the derivatives market in Cambodia, as well as the position of the Securities and Exchange Commission in expanding the development of the derivatives market further.
Mr. Sou Socheat encouraged investors to increase their knowledge and be ready to invest in derivatives to contribute to the national economic development.
"The derivatives market has greatly benefited the Cambodian economy by creating job opportunities for university graduates, creating investment income opportunities, and shifting from savings to savings," he said. "Investment, the creation of new investment options, the diversification of foreign investment into the country and the increase in revenue for the state through the payment of taxes."
(Kampong Thom): More than 3,000 members who participated in the celebration of the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day in Stong district, Kampong Thom province, are determined to protect, maintain and be grateful for peace, especially on January 7.
The sincere and sincere commitment and gratitude of the members was expressed at the 41st Anniversary of the 7 January Victory Day celebration held in Stong District on 7 January 2020 with the participation of Mr. Chea Chanto, Permanent Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the National Working Group for Stong District.
Mr. Chea Chanto quoted the speech of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian People's Party to address the Cambodian people in the deepest sense.
He summed up Samdech Techo's speech: "The overthrow of the genocidal regime of Pol Pot and the revival of the Cambodian people from the massacre of the most brutal regime on January 7, 1979 is the end of a great era. "The darkest of Cambodia and opened a new era of independence, freedom, democracy and social progress."
He continued that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Samdech Panha Chakrei Heng Samrin and Samdech Thamma Pothisal Chea Sim, former President of the Senate, the mother of January 7 and the only mother of peace, is the truth.
On that occasion, to celebrate the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day, Mr. Chea Chanto presented winter coats to more than 3,000 participants, each of whom received a T-shirt.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth Instructs the Ministry of Public Works and the Supreme National Economic Council to Prepare a Transitional Master Plan on "Multipurpose Connectivity and Logistics"
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the National Council for Logistics (NCCC), instructed the working group of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Supreme National Economic Council to continue their cooperation. Together to prepare a master plan for the transition of "multi-modal transport and logistics" for the benefit of society.
The introduction was made at the first meeting of the National Council for Logistics on the draft Transitional Master Plan on "Connecting Multipurpose Transport and Logistics" at the Ministry of Economy and Finance. This is according to a press release obtained by Fresh News on January 8.
This "Transitional Master Plan" incorporates five sectoral master plans from detailed study by development partners, including:
* Road transport master plan and road safety plan, * Rail transport master plan, * Inland waterway, sea and port master plan, * Sihanoukville Autonomous Port and Phnom Penh Autonomous Port master plan and * Logistics master plan.
The drafting of the Transitional Master Plan on "Connecting Multipurpose Transport Systems and Logistics" adheres to three main principles:
Following the discussion, the National Logistics Council decided:
1: Recognize the contribution of development partners in the preparation of detailed master plans in each sector 2: Officially approve the transition master plan for implementation in 2020-2021 and the "transition master plan" is the basis Develop a comprehensive master plan, which is scheduled for 2021.
Overall, the "Transitional Master Plan" plays an important role in directing as well as defining the overall framework of the transport infrastructure development plan by all means, including the logistics system, which will increase the efficiency of public investment in transport infrastructure and participation. Promote sustainable and inclusive economic growth.
Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Meeting, highly appreciated the efforts and cooperation of relevant ministries and institutions in preparing this transitional master plan and instructed the working group of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport and the Supreme National Economic Council to continue. Collaborate to prepare a comprehensive master plan in the future.
