Celebrate Victory Day on January 7! Senior CPP official leads ceremony in Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province
(Koh Kong): Mr. Meas Bunly, Acting Deputy Chairman of Botum Sakor District Assistance Team, represented by Mr. Chao Phirun, Chairman of Botum Sakor District Assistance Team, Koh Kong Province, and Mr. Hak Leng, District Governor and Chairman of Botum Sakor District CPP. On January 7, 2020, led the celebration of the 41st anniversary of the January 7 Victory Day at the headquarters of the Cambodian People's Party, Botum Sakor District, Koh Kong Province.
Mr. Meas Bunly said that today brings us all together on behalf of the Cambodian People's Party on behalf of all members of the CPP branch and the people of Botum Sakor district, Koh Kong province to commemorate the anniversary. Memories of January 7, a day that gives strength, happiness and peace to all of us.
Mr. Meas Bunly reminded that in the beginning or during the time when the country was at war in the geography around Botum Sakor district, even the roads could not travel up and down, most people, government officials travel by various means of the road. Water and Khmer Rouge forces ambushed and raided every village and every place where this geographical base of this district occurred.
In that situation, only Samdech Techo Hun Sen, using Samdech as a strategy called the strategy of win-win triangle strategy, then the triangle strategy was successful by coordinating the unification of Khmer Rouge forces in Samlot, Pailin, Anlong Veng, O'Smach. These are the prince's victorious policies that made the nation and all of us unite in peace, the Khmer Rouge forces and related forces have continuously laid down their arms.
He added that until now, we all live, learn, live, have a home, own land, each has full freedom because of peace. Therefore, we must all be thankful for the peace and peace that has led us and our country to progress and progress in all areas.
It should be noted that this afternoon, the team led by Lt. Gen. Meas Bunly led the team to visit the people in each commune of Botum Sakor district and organize a fun program by eating solidarity noodles and have Bands for dancing and entertainment. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police Crack Down on Illegal Gambling and Arrested 30 Illegal Gambling Arrests, Detained 30 Cambodian-Chinese Suspects
(Preah Sihanouk): For two days, on January 6-07, 2020, under the coordination of Mr. Lim Bunheng, Deputy Prosecutor of Preah Sihanouk Provincial Court, led by the Criminal Police Planning Officer, Preah City Police Inspectorate. Sihanouk and the police force of Sangkat 3 Administration Post inspected 3 illegal gambling venues.
The three illegal gambling venues embedded in the three illegal gambling places are: First: the name of Ta Chong Hoor Game City, near the dolphin roundabout in Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville, Second: Tak One J Game in the second group Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville and 3rd: No trademark in Group 2, Village 1, Sangkat 3, Sihanoukville.
Preah Sihanouk Provincial Police confirmed that the team inspected the sites and found that they did not have a business license from the competent authorities, as the occupants had secretly run illegal gambling under the banner of the operation. Experts brought 30 people (six women) to the provincial police for questioning.
