Mr. Keo Rattanak added that the 195 megawatts of electricity is clean energy from the Daun Sahong hydropower plant in Laos.
He considered the connection of electricity from Laos to the Cambodian national grid as the fruit of the two countries' efforts since November 2015. The Cambodian side rushed to build a transmission line day and night to Stung Treng province and from Stung Treng province to the Lao border to receive this energy before the 2021 plan stated in the agreement.
Mr. Keo Rattanak stated, "Today at 4:58 pm, the Electricity of Cambodia received 195 megawatts of electricity from the Don Sahong Hydropower Project in Laos as agreed." "It means that we can do it one year ahead of schedule, which is the result of the efforts of both countries and also another fruit of Cambodia to help ensure that there is no shortage of energy supply in the national system."
He added that with the connection of 195 megawatts of electricity from Laos and with the launch of a 150-megawatt coal-fired power plant in Sihanoukville last month, and with other measures that electricity Cambodia has considered this arrangement, it can be said that in 2020, Cambodia will no longer face electricity shortages.
