At the same time, Mr. Keo Rattanak, Director General, also asked for understanding on this electricity issue because the creation or construction of each source of electricity takes a long time, which is at least 3 years. Cambodian National Assembly President to Attend Asia-Pacific Parliamentary Forum Annual Meeting in Australia Next Week
The invitation to attend the APPF meeting of the President of the National Assembly was made at the invitation of the President of the Legislative Assembly of Australia. This is according to the announcement of the General Secretariat of the National Assembly.
Samdech Heng Samrin will address the opening ceremony of the 27th APPF in early 2019, when the Cambodian Parliament hosts the 27th APPF Annual Meeting. At the same time, Samdech will also deliver a speech to share experiences from the leadership and organization of the 27th APPF meeting in the Executive Committee meeting.
The 27-nation parliament is composed of Australia, the Kingdom of Cambodia, China, Japan, the Republic of Korea, Mongolia, the Russian Federation, Indonesia, Indonesia, Laos, Malaysia, the Philippines, Singapore, Thailand, Vietnam, Fiji, Macedonia, New Zealand, Papua New Guinea, the archipelago of Mars, Canada, Chile, Colombo, Costa Rica, and the United States.
During his meeting in Australia, the National Assembly President plans to hold bilateral talks with his Australian counterpart and hold talks with parliamentary leaders of other friendly countries to strengthen ties, cooperation and diplomacy in the Cambodian parliament. On the international stage, both multilateral and bilateral frameworks.
Other members of the delegation will attend meetings of various APPF committees, including the Political and Security Committee, the Economic Committee, the Women's Parliamentary Committee and the Joint Proclamation Committee, the Regional Cooperation Committee.
