Pan Sosak tells Cambodian cyclists to increase capacity
(Kep): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce and President of the Khmer Cycling Federation, encouraged Cambodian cyclists not to be discouraged by the failure to win the World Cycling Championships in Cambodia. The minister urged them to train harder to win and get good results in the next game.
The Minister's encouragement as well as the Reminder was made while attending the Victory Ceremony for the Third Phase Cyclists and the Solidarity Dinner of the 1st World Cycling Championships in the Coastal Region of Cambodia 2020 Held from January 4-6, 2020.
At the end of the competition, the Minister honored the best young Filipino medalist with a medal and white jersey and the best red jersey for Hong Kong, the best mountaineer. Of the entire cycling event.
On the same night, the Minister attended a solidarity dinner for the players and the organizing committee. On that occasion, the Minister informed that this cycling event is a historical event and a new initiative to promote cycling in Cambodia, as well as contribute to the development of national sports, tourism and socio-economic.
He said that such a racing event is the dream of the federation, which always wants to see and want to create a world-class cycling competition at the professional level in Cambodia for the Khmer Cycling Federation to gain knowledge, experience, technical skills through learning. Live, practice, do and see for yourself in further self-development goals.
Japanese art group in Cambodia gathers to perform traditional art to show love and remembrance of motherland
(Phnom Penh): Crowds, mostly Japanese and young people, gather to watch traditional Japanese summer art performances in Cambodia to show love and miss their homeland.
This traditional performance of Japanese cultural dance was held on the night of January 6, 2020 yesterday at a Japanese restaurant in Phnom Penh with the participation of Japanese people living and doing business in In Cambodia, too.
